://github.com/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commit/49c8005410d5ca5229c58b38a291cbd38f11a641","node_id":"C_kwDONZwSsNoAKDQ5YzgwMDU0MTBkNWNhNTIyOWM1OGIzOGEyOTFjYmQzOGYxMWE2NDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commit/72b02f980a6daded0ea7b14c33daedb9bd38c5fc","sha":"72b02f980a6daded0ea7b14c33daedb9bd38c5fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/72b02f980a6daded0ea7b14c33daedb9bd38c5fc"}],"sha":"49c8005410d5ca5229c58b38a291cbd38f11a641","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/49c8005410d5ca5229c58b38a291cbd38f11a641"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155619404?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hengxian-jiang/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hengxian-jiang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hengxian-jiang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hengxian-jiang/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hengxian-jiang","id":155619404,"login":"hengxian-jiang","node_id":"U_kgDOCUaQTA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hengxian-jiang/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hengxian-jiang/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hengxian-jiang/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hengxian-jiang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hengxian-jiang/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hengxian-jiang","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/72b02f980a6daded0ea7b14c33daedb9bd38c5fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T03:54:46Z","email":"155619404+hengxian-jiang@users.noreply.github.com","name":"hengxian-jiang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T03:54:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Atlas vue based notebook revamp (#3421)\n\n* feat(notebook-git-api): server-side git mirror for Atlas notebooks\n\nA trex function that mirrors notebook.document rows to a configured git repo,\nand serves notebook templates from a second repo.\n\nRoutes (all require x-user-id): POST /:id/mirror, GET /:id/remote-diff-check,\nPOST /:id/overwrite-from-remote, POST /overwrite-all-from-remote, GET /templates.\n\nNotes on the shape:\n\n- The Vue plugin writes rows straight to PostGraphile from the browser, so there\n  is no server-side seam on the write path. The store calls /mirror after a\n  successful write instead — the same carve-out shape metadata-api uses. A\n  dropped mirror leaves the repo a revision behind until the next write;\n  overwrite-all-from-remote is the repair path.\n- The git PAT comes only from NOTEBOOK_GIT_PAT in the function''s environment,\n  never from the database. V3__notebook_graphql_grants.sql grants SELECT on the\n  whole notebook schema to `authenticated` with no RLS, so a PAT in\n  notebook.app_settings would be readable by any user with one GraphQL query.\n- Content is compared canonically, not as strings. notebook.document.content is\n  JSONB and Postgres does not preserve key order, so a string compare would\n  report drift on every poll. This deliberately differs from the React\n  notebook.service.ts, whose column is TEXT.\n- Routing lives in router.ts behind dependency injection so it is unit-testable\n  without a live Deno.serve, following hades-api.\n- Unconfigured git and an unconfigured template repo are first-class states:\n  mirror skips, diff-check reports no differences, templates returns []. A\n  missing repo must never block notebook creation.\n- scopes/roles: both routes are declared in the plugin manifest because trex''s\n  pluginAuthz is fail-closed — an undeclared route is denied outright. They use\n  an empty scope list (any authenticated user), matching the access the notebook\n  data itself already has via PostGraphile.\n\n45 Deno tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(analytics-svc-init): destroy the knex pool so the init worker can exit\n\nanalytics-svc-init created a knex instance and never destroyed it. The pool\nkeeps open handles, so the Deno worker''s event loop never drains and the\nsupervisor force-kills the isolate on its wall-clock limit — visible as a\ncontinuous \"wall clock duration warning / early termination has been triggered\"\nstream during trex startup.\n\nFive sibling init functions (perseus-init, alp-usermgmt-init, portal-init,\nalp-idp-migration-init, prefect) already destroy their datasource in a finally\nblock; this one was new and missed the convention.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(notebook-git-api): serve notebook templates, move the API to an @ohdsi plugin\n\nEvery notebook-git-api route returned 401 regardless of the caller. trex routes\nnon-trusted plugin functions through d2eAuthn, which verifies the bearer token\nagainst ${LOGTO__ISSUER}/jwks — but docker-compose.yml points LOGTO__ISSUER at\nthe Logto host unconditionally, while scripts/cli.ts only starts Logto when\nD2E_IDP_MODE=logto-federated. Under D2E_IDP_MODE=trex that host does not exist,\nso jwtVerify always threw. No LOGTO__ISSUER value fixes it: the verifier appends\n/jwks, and trex''s own OIDC serves /.well-known/jwks.json.\n\nMove the function into @ohdsi/notebook-git. TRUSTED_PLUGIN_SCOPES (@trex/,\n@ohdsi/) mount under PLUGINS_BASE_PATH/<scope>/ and are guarded by trex''s own\nauth instead: authContext validates the trex-native HS256 token the client\nalready obtains from /trex-token, and sets app.user_id so the proxy injects the\nx-user-id the router requires. pluginAuthz is fail-open for routes with no\nREQUIRED_URL_SCOPES match, so no scopes entry is needed — unlike d2eAuthn, which\ndenies them. No trex change required.\n\nMake templates work against data2evidence/templates. Three things were wrong\nagainst the real repo:\n\n- listFiles did not recurse and the notebooks live in notebooks/, so the listing\n  was always empty. Git now takes a validated subDir; paths still have to\n  resolve inside it, and isomorphic-git still gets repo-relative paths.\n- the field is notebookContent, not content.\n- notebookContent is the React notebook''s Starboard/jupystar TEXT format, but\n  the Vue notebook needs structured NotebookData. jupystar.ts converts it,\n  including the `# %%---` per-cell metadata header that would otherwise render\n  as literal `# id: ...` at the top of every cell.\n\nLanguage comes from the code, not the frontmatter label: all four published\ntemplates declare python while every cell is R.\n\nVerified against the live repo: 4 templates, 12-15 cells each, all r.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Restore dc-local file changes\n\n* fix(notebook): bump trex-notebook for the kernel and styling fixes\n\nPicks up two fixes in the notebook plugin:\n\n- The Python kernel now starts. Its worker was requested from the origin root\n  (vite emitted absolute asset URLs with no `base`) and, once reachable, the\n  hardcoded CDN version did not match the installed pyodide package.\n- library(rD2E) now resolves in the R kernel, via the same source-injection and\n  library() shim the React notebook uses. rD2E is not an installable webR\n  package.\n\nAlso lets Tailwind''s font sizes reach the notebook''s buttons: Atlas ships an\nunlayered `button{font:inherit}`, which beat the plugin''s @layer''d utilities,\nso toolbar text kept the host font size.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix copilot suggestion\n\n* fix(notebook): bump trex-notebook for the pyodide resolution CI fix\n\nResolves the pyodide version from the notebook lib that actually declares it,\ninstead of via node builtins this browser package cannot typecheck against.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(notebook): bump trex-notebook for the pyodide test fix\n\nThe version assertion hardcoded a locally-resolved pyodide version and failed\non CI, which pins a different one from the same semver range.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(notebook-git-api): authorize routes, not just authenticate the caller\n\nThe plugin declared no route scopes and the handler only checked x-user-id,\nwhich says who is calling but not what they may do. trex''s pluginAuthz — the\ntrusted-scope path this plugin uses — is FAIL-OPEN: a request matching no\nREQUIRED_URL_SCOPES entry is passed through. So any signed-in user could call\nPOST /overwrite-all-from-remote and rewrite every notebook from the repo, while\nthe portal restricts the same operation to portal.notebook.systemAdmin.write\n(plugins/functions/package.json).\n\nAdd per-method scopes mirroring the portal: read for templates and\nremote-diff-check, update for mirror and overwrite-from-remote, and\nsystemAdmin.write for the bulk overwrite.\n\nTwo details the entries depend on:\n\n- pluginAuthz matches req.originalUrl, which carries the query string, so a\n  `$`-anchored pattern misses \"...?x=1\" and fail-open then allows the call. The\n  restrictive rule is therefore left unanchored — over-matching a strict rule is\n  safe, over-matching a permissive one is not.\n- scopes from every matching entry are OR''d and only one is required, so the\n  patterns are kept disjoint: the bulk route resolves to exactly\n  [systemAdmin.write] and picks up no weaker alternative.\n\nA backstop entry maps anything else under the plugin to systemAdmin.write, so a\nroute added later is denied by default rather than shipping unauthorized. It\ncannot weaken the rules above, which already allow system admins.\n\nTests assert the resulting matrix, including the query-string case and the\ndefault for an unlisted route — both silent failures at runtime.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(notebook): point trex-notebook at merged develop\n\nOHDSI/trex-notebook#13 was squash-merged, so the feature-branch commit this\ngitlink named (425f1506) never landed on develop and is reachable only from a\nbranch that will be deleted. d2e develop meanwhile advanced the same gitlink to\nb0c7ac0, hence the conflict.\n\ndevelop''s tip 809dab7 is a descendant of b0c7ac0 and also contains the squashed\n#13, so it supersedes both sides and nothing is lost.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9698320519505c0ad503ae04803aec59d2950e9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/git/trees/9698320519505c0ad503ae04803aec59d2950e9b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/git/commits/72b02f980a6daded0ea7b14c33daedb9bd38c5fc","verification":{"payload":"tree 9698320519505c0ad503ae04803aec59d2950e9b\nparent 70ab3793147ba362280dd4a55cfb48fd3cb9e9ee\nauthor hengxian-jiang <155619404+hengxian-jiang@users.noreply.github.com> 1790913286 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790913286 +0000\n\nAtlas vue based notebook revamp (#3421)\n\n* feat(notebook-git-api): server-side git mirror for Atlas notebooks\n\nA trex function that mirrors notebook.document rows to a configured git repo,\nand serves notebook templates from a second repo.\n\nRoutes (all require x-user-id): POST /:id/mirror, GET /:id/remote-diff-check,\nPOST /:id/overwrite-from-remote, POST /overwrite-all-from-remote, GET /templates.\n\nNotes on the shape:\n\n- The Vue plugin writes rows straight to PostGraphile from the browser, so there\n  is no server-side seam on the write path. The store calls /mirror after a\n  successful write instead — the same carve-out shape metadata-api uses. A\n  dropped mirror leaves the repo a revision behind until the next write;\n  overwrite-all-from-remote is the repair path.\n- The git PAT comes only from NOTEBOOK_GIT_PAT in the function''s environment,\n  never from the database. V3__notebook_graphql_grants.sql grants SELECT on the\n  whole notebook schema to `authenticated` with no RLS, so a PAT in\n  notebook.app_settings would be readable by any user with one GraphQL query.\n- Content is compared canonically, not as strings. notebook.document.content is\n  JSONB and Postgres does not preserve key order, so a string compare would\n  report drift on every poll. This deliberately differs from the React\n  notebook.service.ts, whose column is TEXT.\n- Routing lives in router.ts behind dependency injection so it is unit-testable\n  without a live Deno.serve, following hades-api.\n- Unconfigured git and an unconfigured template repo are first-class states:\n  mirror skips, diff-check reports no differences, templates returns []. A\n  missing repo must never block notebook creation.\n- scopes/roles: both routes are declared in the plugin manifest because trex''s\n  pluginAuthz is fail-closed — an undeclared route is denied outright. They use\n  an empty scope list (any authenticated user), matching the access the notebook\n  data itself already has via PostGraphile.\n\n45 Deno tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(analytics-svc-init): destroy the knex pool so the init worker can exit\n\nanalytics-svc-init created a knex instance and never destroyed it. The pool\nkeeps open handles, so the Deno worker''s event loop never drains and the\nsupervisor force-kills the isolate on its wall-clock limit — visible as a\ncontinuous \"wall clock duration warning / early termination has been triggered\"\nstream during trex startup.\n\nFive sibling init functions (perseus-init, alp-usermgmt-init, portal-init,\nalp-idp-migration-init, prefect) already destroy their datasource in a finally\nblock; this one was new and missed the convention.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(notebook-git-api): serve notebook templates, move the API to an @ohdsi plugin\n\nEvery notebook-git-api route returned 401 regardless of the caller. trex routes\nnon-trusted plugin functions through d2eAuthn, which verifies the bearer token\nagainst ${LOGTO__ISSUER}/jwks — but docker-compose.yml points LOGTO__ISSUER at\nthe Logto host unconditionally, while scripts/cli.ts only starts Logto when\nD2E_IDP_MODE=logto-federated. Under D2E_IDP_MODE=trex that host does not exist,\nso jwtVerify always threw. No LOGTO__ISSUER value fixes it: the verifier appends\n/jwks, and trex''s own OIDC serves /.well-known/jwks.json.\n\nMove the function into @ohdsi/notebook-git. TRUSTED_PLUGIN_SCOPES (@trex/,\n@ohdsi/) mount under PLUGINS_BASE_PATH/<scope>/ and are guarded by trex''s own\nauth instead: authContext validates the trex-native HS256 token the client\nalready obtains from /trex-token, and sets app.user_id so the proxy injects the\nx-user-id the router requires. pluginAuthz is fail-open for routes with no\nREQUIRED_URL_SCOPES match, so no scopes entry is needed — unlike d2eAuthn, which\ndenies them. No trex change required.\n\nMake templates work against data2evidence/templates. Three things were wrong\nagainst the real repo:\n\n- listFiles did not recurse and the notebooks live in notebooks/, so the listing\n  was always empty. Git now takes a validated subDir; paths still have to\n  resolve inside it, and isomorphic-git still gets repo-relative paths.\n- the field is notebookContent, not content.\n- notebookContent is the React notebook''s Starboard/jupystar TEXT format, but\n  the Vue notebook needs structured NotebookData. jupystar.ts converts it,\n  including the `# %%---` per-cell metadata header that would otherwise render\n  as literal `# id: ...` at the top of every cell.\n\nLanguage comes from the code, not the frontmatter label: all four published\ntemplates declare python while every cell is R.\n\nVerified against the live repo: 4 templates, 12-15 cells each, all r.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Restore dc-local file changes\n\n* fix(notebook): bump trex-notebook for the kernel and styling fixes\n\nPicks up two fixes in the notebook plugin:\n\n- The Python kernel now starts. Its worker was requested from the origin root\n  (vite emitted absolute asset URLs with no `base`) and, once reachable, the\n  hardcoded CDN version did not match the installed pyodide package.\n- library(rD2E) now resolves in the R kernel, via the same source-injection and\n  library() shim the React notebook uses. rD2E is not an installable webR\n  package.\n\nAlso lets Tailwind''s font sizes reach the notebook''s buttons: Atlas ships an\nunlayered `button{font:inherit}`, which beat the plugin''s @layer''d utilities,\nso toolbar text kept the host font size.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix copilot suggestion\n\n* fix(notebook): bump trex-notebook for the pyodide resolution CI fix\n\nResolves the pyodide version from the notebook lib that actually declares it,\ninstead of via node builtins this browser package cannot typecheck against.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(notebook): bump trex-notebook for the pyodide test fix\n\nThe version assertion hardcoded a locally-resolved pyodide version and failed\non CI, which pins a different one from the same semver range.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(notebook-git-api): authorize routes, not just authenticate the caller\n\nThe plugin declared no route scopes and the handler only checked x-user-id,\nwhich says who is calling but not what they may do. trex''s pluginAuthz — the\ntrusted-scope path this plugin uses — is FAIL-OPEN: a request matching no\nREQUIRED_URL_SCOPES entry is passed through. So any signed-in user could call\nPOST /overwrite-all-from-remote and rewrite every notebook from the repo, while\nthe portal restricts the same operation to portal.notebook.systemAdmin.write\n(plugins/functions/package.json).\n\nAdd per-method scopes mirroring the portal: read for templates and\nremote-diff-check, update for mirror and overwrite-from-remote, and\nsystemAdmin.write for the bulk overwrite.\n\nTwo details the entries depend on:\n\n- pluginAuthz matches req.originalUrl, which carries the query string, so a\n  `$`-anchored pattern misses \"...?x=1\" and fail-open then allows the call. The\n  restrictive rule is therefore left unanchored — over-matching a strict rule is\n  safe, over-matching a permissive one is not.\n- scopes from every matching entry are OR''d and only one is required, so the\n  patterns are kept disjoint: the bulk route resolves to exactly\n  [systemAdmin.write] and picks up no weaker alternative.\n\nA backstop entry maps anything else under the plugin to systemAdmin.write, so a\nroute added later is denied by default rather than shipping unauthorized. It\ncannot weaken the rules above, which already allow system admins.\n\nTests assert the resulting matrix, including the query-string case and the\ndefault for an unlisted route — both silent failures at runtime.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(notebook): point trex-notebook at merged develop\n\nOHDSI/trex-notebook#13 was squash-merged, so the feature-branch commit this\ngitlink named (425f1506) never landed on develop and is reachable only from a\nbranch that will be deleted. d2e develop meanwhile advanced the same gitlink to\nb0c7ac0, hence the conflict.\n\ndevelop''s tip 809dab7 is a descendant of b0c7ac0 and also contains the squashed\n#13, so it supersedes both sides and nothing is lost.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvysXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiVYQAGPRnPIbbCjetKxNZHeO6pYq\