fb48fd3cb9e9ee","sha":"70ab3793147ba362280dd4a55cfb48fd3cb9e9ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/70ab3793147ba362280dd4a55cfb48fd3cb9e9ee"}],"sha":"72b02f980a6daded0ea7b14c33daedb9bd38c5fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/72b02f980a6daded0ea7b14c33daedb9bd38c5fc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80243918?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/khairul-syazwan","id":80243918,"login":"khairul-syazwan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMjQzOTE4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/70ab3793147ba362280dd4a55cfb48fd3cb9e9ee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T03:32:09Z","email":"80243918+khairul-syazwan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Khairul Syazwan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T03:32:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(vue-mri): open the Atlas3 concept set editor from the filter card (#3440)\n\n* feat(vue-mri): open the Atlas3 concept set editor from the filter card\n\nIn the native Atlas3 mount, the concept set \"+\" and the pencil on a set\nnow open Atlas3''s own concept set editor drawer. Before, both opened a\npick-only chooser, which could not create or edit a set.\n\n- Send `conceptSet:edit` (OHDSI/Atlas3#363) in place of\n  `conceptSet:choose`. \"+\" sends no id and opens a new set. The pencil\n  sends the set''s id and opens that set. The saved set comes back\n  through the caller''s own onClose, so the filter cards do not change.\n- Remove the 4 s wait. Atlas3 puts no time limit on this request,\n  because a person is editing. An Atlas3 without the handler times the\n  request out at 30 s, and the control closes with no change.\n- Pin @ohdsi/atlas3 to 0.1.0-20260929021642-294c2d1, the release of\n  #363.\n- Keep dist-atlas-native out of the Docker build context, as\n  dist-atlas already is.\n\nPicking an existing set is the card''s own dropdown, which needs nothing\nfrom the host. The portal is not changed: it does not load this entry.\n\n* fix(vue-mri): map concept set refs between the filter card and Atlas3\n\nThe pencil on a set from the card''s dropdown failed in Atlas with\n\"Could not open concept set webapi:1\". The card holds D2E concept set\nrefs (\"webapi:N\", \"legacy:N\", or a bare number, where a bare number\nbelow 1_000_000_000 is a legacy set). The bridge sent that ref to\nAtlas3 as is, and WebAPI answered GET /conceptset/webapi:1 with a 500.\n\nThe reply had the same problem the other way. The bridge put Atlas3''s\nbare WebAPI id on the card, which D2E reads as a legacy set of the same\nnumber.\n\nTranslate at the bridge, with the existing query-filter parser:\n- to Atlas3: \"webapi:N\" (or its offset form) becomes N; no id opens a\n  new set;\n- from Atlas3: N becomes \"webapi:N\";\n- a legacy set is not in WebAPI, so the Atlas3 editor cannot open it.\n  The bridge does not send the request, and the control closes with no\n  change.\n\n* refactor(vue-mri): remove comments from the concept set editor bridge","tree":{"sha":"142808837344ff0c5e06f79170aacb8567b5fefa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/git/trees/142808837344ff0c5e06f79170aacb8567b5fefa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/git/commits/70ab3793147ba362280dd4a55cfb48fd3cb9e9ee","verification":{"payload":"tree 142808837344ff0c5e06f79170aacb8567b5fefa\nparent f7e8a887a1114681ab388d206ad77628ec1e5138\nauthor Khairul Syazwan <80243918+khairul-syazwan@users.noreply.github.com> 1790911929 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790911929 +0000\n\nfeat(vue-mri): open the Atlas3 concept set editor from the filter card (#3440)\n\n* feat(vue-mri): open the Atlas3 concept set editor from the filter card\n\nIn the native Atlas3 mount, the concept set \"+\" and the pencil on a set\nnow open Atlas3''s own concept set editor drawer. Before, both opened a\npick-only chooser, which could not create or edit a set.\n\n- Send `conceptSet:edit` (OHDSI/Atlas3#363) in place of\n  `conceptSet:choose`. \"+\" sends no id and opens a new set. The pencil\n  sends the set''s id and opens that set. The saved set comes back\n  through the caller''s own onClose, so the filter cards do not change.\n- Remove the 4 s wait. Atlas3 puts no time limit on this request,\n  because a person is editing. An Atlas3 without the handler times the\n  request out at 30 s, and the control closes with no change.\n- Pin @ohdsi/atlas3 to 0.1.0-20260929021642-294c2d1, the release of\n  #363.\n- Keep dist-atlas-native out of the Docker build context, as\n  dist-atlas already is.\n\nPicking an existing set is the card''s own dropdown, which needs nothing\nfrom the host. The portal is not changed: it does not load this entry.\n\n* fix(vue-mri): map concept set refs between the filter card and Atlas3\n\nThe pencil on a set from the card''s dropdown failed in Atlas with\n\"Could not open concept set webapi:1\". The card holds D2E concept set\nrefs (\"webapi:N\", \"legacy:N\", or a bare number, where a bare number\nbelow 1_000_000_000 is a legacy set). The bridge sent that ref to\nAtlas3 as is, and WebAPI answered GET /conceptset/webapi:1 with a 500.\n\nThe reply had the same problem the other way. The bridge put Atlas3''s\nbare WebAPI id on the card, which D2E reads as a legacy set of the same\nnumber.\n\nTranslate at the bridge, with the existing query-filter parser:\n- to Atlas3: \"webapi:N\" (or its offset form) becomes N; no id opens a\n  new set;\n- from Atlas3: N becomes \"webapi:N\";\n- a legacy set is not in WebAPI, so the Atlas3 editor cannot open it.\n  The bridge does not send the request, and the control closes with no\n  change.\n\n* refactor(vue-mri): remove comments from the concept set editor bridge","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvyXJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVDsQAJ46BcyQspM1d5F90ZFTSsLZ\nITwMqqN1q0uux7FHBH0M3PzRqGn0shBfAJVDklRbySXxYSQyRW/uPpuO9fHg1Ree\nCttowYoTxxyCs9Z8y1AXm9+dC+94fQI3hLtazG3NZdE6ahgfymjpxRBgzYJ95Pur\ng8BXUKeB/I7R3X3u5wi2q9KINkGomVxLjMpmmfCtohpaj9FEGeyrA1H3ObeWWx+t\nIIm8QmQcNExEQeh0EybwRATOpXn5eelEDNpNt7D8VYExzj+5flAawcSFJA+wYG38\nAPPW8/L5l8bph0fs+y4dBGM9OcDTIsB+iXttcIR12SgHVQ0APKukbhU1ekYCSp0n\nk/b5hUVV9evcstq42QdgDgnQ6kgAq0f/efSdHYwAS5haMoRSuUpbBJgPH2U/u53L\nbPmEIY/uwYNV0G4JSULhS8tlRWSl+vHAON2hgu9DVbcyxXxFHZIkxA7iTpKO7oLV\nHxqXSQA55ivYRxmHX5JAbnIQetcipWynUjKwxwF42Pgdm9MbcSka+u4ht5Dcqi3g\nH49ieCpa34U9iYGtxg5buRB9ki8Yjb3lEzCxINoveLcvxxygXWk1Q8hqgouPazsk\nKjoSQu4rtEJalWIDM775PaDD/pGEVl2tRHCIxxuAGQHVYN51yVYDVPmbmxUQtMah\nnB3l5Mc2nHuXgiJEe9Dc\n=hOVT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T03:32:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commit/70ab3793147ba362280dd4a55cfb48fd3cb9e9ee","node_id":"C_kwDONZwSsNoAKDcwYWIzNzkzMTQ3YmEzNjIyODBkZDRhNTVjZmI0OGZkM2NiOWU5ZWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commit/f7e8a887a1114681ab388d206ad77628ec1e5138","sha":"f7e8a887a1114681ab388d206ad77628ec1e5138","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/f7e8a887a1114681ab388d206ad77628ec1e5138"}],"sha":"70ab3793147ba362280dd4a55cfb48fd3cb9e9ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/70ab3793147ba362280dd4a55cfb48fd3cb9e9ee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80243918?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/khairul-syazwan","id":80243918,"login":"khairul-syazwan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMjQzOTE4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/f7e8a887a1114681ab388d206ad77628ec1e5138/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T02:05:14Z","email":"80243918+khairul-syazwan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Khairul Syazwan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T02:05:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ui): show only accessible data sources in Data Exploration and Wizards (#3455)\n\n* fix(ui): show only accessible data sources in Data Exploration and Wizards\n\nThe data source selectors in Data Exploration and Wizards listed every\nsource, including PUBLIC and DEFAULT datasets the user has no researcher\nrole for. Both now filter the list by the dataset roles from\n/usermgmt/api/me/roles. The Data Exploration selector is also not\nrendered in the portal build, where it could only be a disabled label.\n\nCloses #3442\n\n* no-mistakes(review): Auto-switch Data Exploration to an accessible data source\n\n* no-mistakes(document): Trim stale data-sources doc comment clause\n\n* fix(vue-mri): clear the data sources when they cannot be loaded\n\n* no-mistakes(review): Clear vue-mri data sources at fetch start\n\n* no-mistakes(document): Trim stale \"only\" from data-sources state comment","tree":{"sha":"a1f2194c2f3c021d6d1c3ee02ba38d0e9ffdcdde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/git/trees/a1f2194c2f3c021d6d1c3ee02ba38d0e9ffdcdde"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/git/commits/f7e8a887a1114681ab388d206ad77628ec1e5138","verification":{"payload":"tree a1f2194c2f3c021d6d1c3ee02ba38d0e9ffdcdde\nparent e5995ea327ffade34ac083eaccbb6b717eff9b45\nauthor Khairul Syazwan <80243918+khairul-syazwan@users.noreply.github.com> 1790906714 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790906714 +0000\n\nfix(ui): show only accessible data sources in Data Exploration and Wizards (#3455)\n\n* fix(ui): show only accessible data sources in Data Exploration and Wizards\n\nThe data source selectors in Data Exploration and Wizards listed every\nsource, including PUBLIC and DEFAULT datasets the user has no researcher\nrole for. Both now filter the list by the dataset roles from\n/usermgmt/api/me/roles. The Data Exploration selector is also not\nrendered in the portal build, where it could only be a disabled label.\n\nCloses #3442\n\n* no-mistakes(review): Auto-switch Data Exploration to an accessible data source\n\n* no-mistakes(document): Trim stale data-sources doc comment clause\n\n* fix(vue-mri): clear the data sources when they cannot be loaded\n\n* no-mistakes(review): Clear vue-mri data sources at fetch start\n\n* no-mistakes(document): Trim stale \"only\" from data-sources state comment","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvxFqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiSwQAC5F/BCjQPOghTla5uhYTgfd\nFpXtqQAiNrMnt1Raja0Ccr9okOVgce17XQ4nYOYr4tbd1iUsYVX5sN6PVFXneApd\ntQMIupA+L81PnpdUwsFFIDWGdZQZ37/S5y75rYoR1nFDTCGU/pHJ6T3DShifmcIz\nINWEB2qUdeqZnftz6C8MwjGB6LZ6M9q1d38+OS7/Opmsl2WyyXwBIh8oXMDomyxp\nw2Z9uErJhnF9I6e1P58766D1wKkszUc8e3TAC9T0JluHKtv07YMCx+9IuaRi0qEQ\nx3ix59+yh4tGy4asbNhx2kQ/PDJvMzq0+SXkojXUApHckaYP9rzsv1D1hx0bEXSu\n8p8rGF6Fq8bH6Rgu25hETzXQZcwn7S6UXqCoYKqtIh03+yWiJpaNV/4rweAWwb3w\nlfP8IIx2uKZr8ypBOx7xNfYasAXXwYXvsv6HeuGEmbUJRLMx03+TLa4P3rlUjC8W\nyloSLRY9/jrABMeNjqDNyAygfo/GscH1RaJviNHBdqa7qRXfWPWXBKp8ZF7zsXrX\nu09fPa7mmp+gKrIVSIgDb3R0PoR32VRQvIIY0OlkVgAvzwU3B7KnurDyBwIfKVRl\nXjKGEhyq6Zxuh4HVZJu8hhYiFwDkln3AipL9PEuMaZY4RMN27eAyM4f6UCGZomjb\n4IkRFU8OHyqHx8XAVDZy\n=QnfT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T02:05:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/fo