mit/77723fa8c1ebee902154dfcc4deaa70d2176b00a","node_id":"C_kwDONZwSsNoAKDc3NzIzZmE4YzFlYmVlOTAyMTU0ZGZjYzRkZWFhNzBkMjE3NmIwMGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commit/fc3384cc8d783fd2216867f52a23219680ec5ede","sha":"fc3384cc8d783fd2216867f52a23219680ec5ede","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/fc3384cc8d783fd2216867f52a23219680ec5ede"}],"sha":"77723fa8c1ebee902154dfcc4deaa70d2176b00a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/77723fa8c1ebee902154dfcc4deaa70d2176b00a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80243918?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/khairul-syazwan","id":80243918,"login":"khairul-syazwan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMjQzOTE4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/fc3384cc8d783fd2216867f52a23219680ec5ede/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T13:37:10Z","email":"80243918+khairul-syazwan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Khairul Syazwan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T13:37:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ui): add the d2e component library and the Histoire explorer (#3204)\n\n* refactor(vue-mri): remove the unused atlas theme\n\n(cherry picked from commit 8f22ee68dd96ffd43f8105289599c311770b62e8)\n\n* feat(ui): add the @d2e/ui package with design tokens and histoire\n\n(cherry picked from commit 2e095dec72fc364af0dcb1bfdc9d51e14d999596)\n\n* feat(ui): add D2eDialog, D2eButton and D2eTextField\n\n(cherry picked from commit e5a8dbb430e21d58c4c389cfa234ead2ae242631)\n\n* refactor(vue-mri): drive the vuetify d2e theme from @d2e/ui tokens\n\n(cherry picked from commit 59aadc48cdf285d91eeabdc3e7369687e14fd01b)\n\n* fix(ui): use literal colors in D2eButton to avoid bootstrap utility collisions\n\n(cherry picked from commit 75414bea71e8840a6bc35d7318003d409f3067c2)\n\n* style(ui): format the library files with prettier\n\nLibrary half of the original formatting commit. The application half\ngoes with the dialog changes.\n\n* refactor(ui): use mri-brand theme key for D2eButton colors\n\n(cherry picked from commit 977b92b633cc47993eafd32780fcfad74e72ee8b)\n\n* feat(ui): add slice 2 design tokens\n\n(cherry picked from commit 268c408fa58447db64aac3493d7454b0a8f27bb8)\n\n* feat(ui): add D2eStatusChip, D2eIconButton and D2eMenu\n\n(cherry picked from commit 50d4ae4682c4b2c3273b3bb246373301b23a396b)\n\n* feat(ui): add D2eCard, D2eToolbar and D2eExplorationCard\n\n(cherry picked from commit 2bf1177dc6b87f17a66fb79248fe9ce587dfad58)\n\n* feat(ui): make D2eCard width configurable\n\n(cherry picked from commit 7f5bedd16d14b7b6b8fbdcf56a681c3f06bd7045)\n\n* fix(ui): emit unitless font weight and line height tokens\n\nThe token generator added `px` to each number. This made\n`--d2e-font-*-weight` and the ratio `--d2e-font-*-line-height` values\ninvalid, for example `font-weight: 600px` and `line-height: 1.2px`. The\nbrowser ignored both declarations.\n\nThe effect was not visible in the dialogs, because each affected element\nholds one line of text. It was visible in D2eExplorationCard, where the\nmetadata rows collapsed to 1.5 px and printed on top of each other.\n\nKeep `weight`, `lineHeight`, `opacity` and `zIndex` unitless. Add a test\nthat fails if a weight or a ratio line height gets a unit again.\n\n(cherry picked from commit ca03e1f38574680e87d73a6038774b208e75cb8d)\n\n* chore(ui): track the component explorer as a sub-project\n\nThe explorer was an untracked proof of concept. Track it, so that each\ndeveloper can start it with the same dependency versions.\n\nHistoire needs vite 7. `plugins/ui/package.json` pins vite to 6.4.2 with\nan override, to hold libs/react-notebook at vite 6. Bun applies an\noverride to all packages in the workspace. The workspace globs are\n`libs/*` and `apps/*`, which match one level only, so this directory is\noutside the workspace. It uses npm and its own lockfile, and it can\ntherefore use vite 7.\n\nAlso:\n\n- Align `vue` with apps/vue-mri-ui-lib at 3.5.17. `vuetify` already\n  agreed at 3.12.0. The explorer must show what the application renders.\n- Add `.nvmrc` and `engine-strict=true`, because the explorer needs\n  Node 20.19 or later and a default shell Node can be older.\n- Keep the lockfile in git. `plugins/ui/.gitignore` ignores each\n  `package-lock.json`, so the explorer negates that rule.\n- Add `.prettierignore`, to keep `prettier --write .` away from the\n  lockfile and the build output.\n\n(cherry picked from commit d849a464dfeb988e61d20c136a11cff7039c3217)\n\n* chore(ui): remove the histoire setup that the workspace cannot run\n\n`histoire.config.ts` and `histoire.setup.ts` were in the library root,\nand the `ui:dev` and `ui:build` scripts started them. They cannot run,\nbecause histoire needs vite 7 and the workspace override pins vite 6.\n\nThe working copies are now in `explorer/`. Two configurations, where one\nof them cannot run, is a trap for the next reader.\n\nThis also removes an undeclared dependency problem: the deleted\n`histoire.setup.ts` imported `@mdi/font`, `@fontsource-variable/ibm-plex-sans`\nand `sass`, which this package never declared. They resolved only through\nbun hoisting. The explorer declares all three.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 59ede28af997fa5cb6b1e518cc699a3281adb204)\n\n* docs(ui): explain how to start the component explorer\n\nGive the library a README, and give the explorer a README with one\ncommand sequence that includes the Node version step. Record why the\nexplorer is outside the workspace, and the two rules that keep it\nworking.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 65560a77dcee6921c47006d506600c8ca19306aa)\n\n* test(ui): guard the explorer against workspace and version drift\n\nTwo properties are load-bearing and silent when they break:\n\n- The workspace globs match one level only. A deeper glob pulls the\n  explorer into the workspace, where the vite 6 override stops Histoire.\n- The explorer must use the vue and vuetify versions of the application,\n  or it shows something the application does not render.\n\nAssert both against the three package.json files. The test reads JSON\nonly; it mounts no component.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 346ff0f147ae47caac80806d71c671aed12a4e01)\n\n* fix(ui): keep the explorer on the vue version histoire accepts\n\n`@histoire/plugin-vue@1.0.0-beta.1` needs `vue ^3.5.26`, and\napps/vue-mri-ui-lib pins `vue 3.5.17`. An exact match makes `npm ci`\nfail with ERESOLVE.\n\nPin 3.5.26 and record the constraint in the README. The parity test\nalready compares the major and minor version only, so it still holds.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 9e9bbbbc04f97c12b4ded963acc567264680e4c5)\n\n* fix(ui): correct the modal scale, add button icons, stop scrim dismissal\n\nThree gaps found by checking the library against the Figma design system\n(file lpbqxd8B0OkRKH9kJoCCEa) through the component explorer.\n\n**Modal scale.** The Figma variables are Modal/S 540, Modal/L 900 and\nModal/XL 1200. There is no Modal/M, and 600 appears nowhere in the design\nsystem, but `tokens.ts` carried `md: 600` and D2eDialog defaulted to it.\nDrop the invented size, add a `size` prop over the real scale, and default\nto Modal/S — the rename, delete and materialize frames are all Modal/S.\n`maxWidth` stays as an escape hatch. A test locks the scale.\n\n**Button icons.** The Figma Button set has a `Sub category` axis of\nDefault / Icon front / Icon back. D2eButton had none of it. Its `icon`\nprop forwarded to `v-btn`''s `icon`, which makes an icon-only round button\nand drops the label, so the \"with icon\" story rendered no label at all.\nReplace it with `prependIcon` and `appendIcon`. Use D2eIconButton when an\nicon-only control is wanted.\n\n**Scrim dismissal.** MODAL CLOSE BEHAVIOR (2106:162) says clicking the\noverlay must not dismiss a modal, for every modal type. The dialog was\ndismissable. `v-dialog` is now always persistent, and Escape is handled\ndirectly so informational modals still close on it. `closeOnEscape`\nturns that off for long forms and multi-step flows, which the same\nframe says must raise a confirm-discard step instead.\n\nThe `persistent` prop is gone: the overlay never dismisses now, so the\nonly remaining axis is Escape.\n\n* fix(ui): split the dialog sizes into variants and drop the button ripple\n\nThe single \"sizes\" story showed one dialog at one size, so the scale was\nnot demonstrable — the sizes looked like they did nothing.\n\nGive each size its own variant. The `size` prop was in fact working; the\nstory sandbox was fixed at 720 px, so Modal/L (900) and Modal/XL (1200)\nboth clamped to the pane and rendered identically. Setting\n`responsive-disabled` on the story lets the preview scale with the\nwindow: S renders at 540 everywhere, L reaches 900 and XL reaches 1200\non a wide window, and both clamp below that — the same thing a real\nbrowser does. Each variant states its max-width.\n\nAlso turn off the Vuetify ripple on D2eButton, D2eIconButton and the\ndialog close button. The Figma button set defines discrete Hover,\nFocused and Pressed states and no ripple animation.\n\n* fix(ui): source-export the d2e component library to unblock the atlas build\n\nThe patient-analytics sub-plugin is installed in CI with\n`npm install --workspaces=false` inside apps/vue-mri-ui-lib, which\nresolves @d2e/ui from the registry and 404s on the private package.\n\nAlias @d2e/ui to libs/d2e-ui/src/index.ts and @d2e/ui/tokens.css to\nlibs/d2e-ui/src/tokens/tokens.css in the three vite configs and in\ntsconfig, and drop the dependency. This keeps the source-export model\nand works for both bun and npm.\n\n* fix(ui): resolve the d2e library''s vue/vuetify during the isolated atlas build\n\nThe patient-analytics atlas build installs only the app with\n`npm install --workspaces=false`, so the d2e library source aliased from\nlibs/d2e-ui sits outside the app node_modules and cannot resolve the vue\nand vuetify it imports. Alias vue and the vuetify entries the library uses\n(components, directives, styles, and the package root) to the app''s\ninstalled copy, leaving the Sass subpaths such as vuetify/settings for the\nSass node importer.\n\n* fix(ui): rebuild D2eExplorationCard against the current Figma design\n\nThe card was built from an older node and was structurally wrong. Rebuilt\nfrom the Exploration card component set (ticket file, 1810:239213 —\nready / Not run / Stale) via the Figma MCP.\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- The card surface is white with a 1px #DEDCDA border and radius 16. The\n  #FAF8F8 radius-12 surface we used for the whole card is actually the\n  nested \"Exploration bookmark\" panel, which was missing entirely.\n- Added the person count row: count in Heading 4 with the status chip\n  right-aligned beside it. This was the most prominent element in the\n  design and we had none of it.\n- Added the nested bookmark panel (created by / last updated / version)\n  with its rule.\n- Removed the invented `By:` label. The design has no such label; the\n  chip belongs on the count row.\n- The checkbox moves to the right of the title, in the 20 px box the\n  design reserves.\n- Metadata values are now Subtitle 2 in Primary/Default, right aligned,\n  and both name and description truncate with a tooltip, per the design''s\n  own note.\n- `status` becomes `ready | not-run | stale` and drives the chip. The\n  `#lead` slot replaces the count so `not-run` can carry the Materialize\n  action, as the design shows.\n- The action bar gets the design''s top border and right alignment.\n\nAlso fixes two defects this surfaced:\n\n- Heading letter spacing. Figma''s -2 on Heading 1-4 is a percentage, not\n  pixels — the Heading 4 spec renders as tracking -0.48px at 24px, i.e.\n  -2%. We emitted \"-2px\", about 4x too tight at 24px. Now -0.02em, with a\n  test that rejects a pixel value coming back.\n- D2eIconButton painted a surface and a shadow, because v-btn defaults to\n  the `elevated` variant. The design''s icon buttons have neither.\n\nBREAKING: `status` is now a string union, not an object, and\n`D2eExplorationCardMetadataRow` is renamed `D2eExplorationCardRow`. The\nexploration page on the follow-up branch consumes both.\n\n* fix(ui): only the primary icon button fills when disabled\n\nFigma 2006:843 (ICON BUTTON) disables each category differently:\nprimary fills with Neutral/Lighter, secondary keeps its outline over a\ntransparent surface, and no-stroke stays bare. We painted the grey fill\nbehind all three, so disabled secondary and no-stroke buttons carried a\npill that the design does not have.\n\nVerified in the browser: disabled no-stroke and secondary now compute to\nrgba(0,0,0,0), primary to rgb(222,220,218).\n\nAlso replace the ad-hoc \"states\" story with the category x state grid the\nFigma sheet uses, so the difference is visible.\n\n* fix(ui): size every exploration card toolbar button to the design''s 48px\n\nThe card''s action bar mixed 44px and 48px buttons. When the toolbar\nbuttons were switched to size=\"lg\", the edit only matched tags whose\n`icon=` sat on the same line; prettier had wrapped the rest, so those\nsilently kept the 44px default and rendered a smaller glyph beside their\nneighbours.\n\nFigma''s action bar (1798:192998) is p-12 with a 24px icon, i.e. 48px, for\nevery button. All 17 story buttons now say so.\n\nMeasured after: 5 of 5 at 48x48, radius 100px, bar padding 4px 8px,\njustify flex-end, gap 4px — matching the frame.\n\n* fix(ui): resolve vue and vuetify wherever they install, not app-locally\n\nBoth CI failures on this PR came from one line. The vuetify aliases added\nfor the isolated atlas build hardcoded\n`apps/vue-mri-ui-lib/node_modules/vuetify`, which exists only under\n`npm install --workspaces=false`. The bun workspace install that\n`build_plugins` and `test-mri-frontend` use hoists vuetify to\n`plugins/ui/node_modules`, so both jobs died on the missing path:\n\n  build_plugins:      Could not load .../vue-mri-ui-lib/node_modules/\n                      vuetify/lib/framework.js: ENOENT\n  test-mri-frontend:  Failed to resolve import \"vuetify\" and\n                      \"vuetify/components/VBtn\"\n\nIt passed locally only because this worktree still had an app-local copy\nleft over from running the atlas install by hand.\n\nResolve the real directory with `createRequire(...).resolve()` instead,\nfalling back to the app-local path, so the same config works under both\ninstall shapes. Applied to `vue` as well, which had the same hardcoded\nform. `require.resolve` also returns the realpath, so the existing dedupe\nintent is preserved.\n\nFails loudly with a named error if neither location resolves, rather than\nproducing an ENOENT deep inside rollup.\n\n* refactor(vue-mri): drop the theme class, the app has one theme\n\nThe Atlas theme is gone, so `.theme-d2e` gated the whole palette behind a\nclass that something had to remember to add — and one entry path had\nstopped adding it. `main.ts` called `applyAppTheme()` only in the\nnon-atlas branch, so `VITE_STANDALONE_ATLAS=true` rendered with no theme\nclass at all and every `--color-*` variable resolved to nothing.\n\nMove the palette onto `:root:root`, matching the block already above it\nin the same file and keeping specificity over d4l-ui.css. The class then\nhas no purpose, and neither do the two functions that set it:\n\n- `utils/ThemeManager.ts` was `remove(''theme-atlas'')` + `add(''theme-d2e'')`.\n  The remove guarded a selector that no longer exists anywhere.\n- `bootstrap/themeBootstrap.ts` was a pass-through wrapper whose only\n  other job was importing the stylesheet.\n\nBoth entry points now import the stylesheet directly. `theme-d2e` was not\nused as a scoping selector anywhere, so nothing else changes.\n\nRemoves the bootstrap test with the files: it asserted the class\nbehaviour that no longer exists.\n\nVerified: `.theme-d2e` no longer appears in the built bundle and the\npalette variables still do; all three build variants pass.\n\n* docs(ui): correct the component and theme docs I made stale\n\nThree prop tables and one README section described APIs removed earlier in\nthis branch:\n\n- D2eButton.story.md still listed `icon`. Passing it falls through to\n  v-btn''s own `icon` prop, which makes the button icon-only and drops the\n  label — the exact bug the component was changed to avoid. Replaced with\n  `prependIcon` / `appendIcon` and a warning.\n- D2eDialog.story.md still listed `maxWidth: 600` and a `persistent`\n  prop. 600 is not a design size and `persistent` no longer exists.\n  Replaced with `size` and `closeOnEscape`.\n- vue-mri-ui-lib/README.md still told readers to call\n  `applyTheme(''atlas'')`. Both the function and the Atlas theme are gone.\n\n* ci(ui): run the @d2e/ui library checks\n\nThe library shipped 25 tests, a token-drift guard and the explorer parity\nassertions, and CI ran none of them. `ui-test-vue.yml` filtered on\n`plugins/ui/apps/vue-mri-ui-lib/**` only, so a library-only change did not\neven trigger the workflow.\n\nAdd `plugins/ui/libs/d2e-ui/**` to the filter — the application consumes\nthe library, so either changing should test both — and run the library''s\n`tokens:check` and `test` after the app''s suite, reusing the same\n`bun install`.\n\n`tokens:check` regenerates tokens.css and diffs it against git, so it\ncatches someone editing tokens.ts without regenerating. Verified: exit 1\non that change, exit 0 once restored.\n\n* refactor(ui): rename the mri-* theme keys to brand*\n\nThe shared library carried application-specific naming. `@d2e/ui` is\nmeant to serve the portal once it moves to Vue, and `mri-brand` reads as\nMRI-only to any other consumer.\n\n  mri-brand       -> brand\n  mri-brand-hover -> brand-hover\n  mri-contrast    -> brand-contrast\n  mri-info        -> brand-info\n\nValues are unchanged.\n\nDeliberately **not** renamed to `primary`. The original plan gives two\nconditions for that, and only one is met. The Figma extraction is done,\nbut Bootstrap 4.6.1 is still imported inside `.mri-app-vue-container`\n(styles/style.scss:11), so `primary` would still collide: Bootstrap''s\nscoped `.bg-primary`/`.text-primary` beat Vuetify''s, and Bootstrap 4\ndefines no `--bs-primary-rgb`, so the declaration is invalid at\ncomputed-value time and the button renders transparent. `brand` is\ncollision-free because Bootstrap''s `$theme-colors` has no such entry.\nRename to `primary` once Bootstrap leaves the portal scope.\n\nNothing outside the library consumed these keys — no `color=\"mri-brand\"`\nprops and no `bg-mri-*` utility classes. The `--color-mri-brand` CSS\ncustom property in the application palette is a different namespace and\nis untouched.\n\nVerified in the explorer: primary renders rgb(0, 0, 128), secondary and\nghost keep navy text, danger stays rgb(163, 41, 61).\n\n* feat(ui): build @d2e/ui as a distributable component library\n\nThe portal is moving to Vue and will share these components, so the\nlibrary needs a real contract rather than a source export that every\nconsumer compiles itself.\n\n- Build with vite lib mode into `dist/index.js` + `dist/index.css`, types\n  via `vue-tsc`. Not the rollup/babel chain libs/portal-components uses:\n  that is rollup 2 plus six babel packages for React/TSX, and vite handles\n  Vue SFCs natively.\n- `vue` and `vuetify` stay external as peer dependencies.\n- Components now import the Vuetify pieces they use, so the package works\n  without the consumer running vite-plugin-vuetify.\n- Entry points move to dist; `./tokens.css` stays on source because it is\n  generated from tokens.ts and guarded by tokens:check.\n- `scripts/verify-dist.mjs` checks the artifact in CI.\n\nTwo things this surfaced:\n\nAdding the Vuetify imports broke three unit tests, which imported their\nconstant maps from the `.vue` files and so began loading Vuetify''s CSS\nunder vitest''s node environment. Moved those maps into plain modules\n(`buttonVariants`, `iconButtonSizes`, `statusChipVariants`,\n`explorationCardStatus`), following the existing `dialogSizes.ts`\npattern. The public API is unchanged; tests no longer touch Vuetify.\n\nThe obvious smoke test — importing dist in plain node — cannot work,\nbecause vuetify''s ESM pulls in .css. `verify:dist` checks statically\ninstead, and asserts *positively* that vue and vuetify are still\nimported: when a peer gets bundled it stops appearing as an import, so\nlooking only for unexpected imports misses the case that matters.\nVerified by dropping vuetify from `external` — the check fails on both\nthe missing import and a 197 kB bundle against the 150 kB ceiling.\n\nVerified: 25 lib tests, tokens:check, dist verify, all three vue-mri\nbuild variants, explorer 8 stories / 30 variants, and every component\nstill renders in the browser with no console errors.\n\n* fix(ui): cover every export in the dist guard, and correct the README\n\n`verify-dist.mjs` checked 13 names while `src/index.ts` exports 17 values. The\ncheck is a subset test, so the four constant maps this branch added —\nVARIANT_MAP, SIZE_MAP, STATUS_CHIP_VARIANT_MAP and ICON_BUTTON_SIZE_MAP — went\nunguarded. Dropping or renaming any of them would not have failed the build.\nThe guard now reports 17 exports.\n\nThe README header still said the application uses the source and there is no\nbuild step, directly above the new section on consuming the built package.\nSay what is true of both: the application reads source through vite aliases,\nand every other consumer uses the artifact.\n\nFound in review of #3251.\n\n* fix(ui): close #3204''s remaining Copilot review gaps\n\n- D2eDialog: card is now a flex column with a capped max-height and a\n  scrollable body, so a long form or short viewport keeps the header/\n  actions visible instead of clipping content.\n- D2eTextField: disable attribute inheritance so a caller''s listeners\n  (blur, click, ...) aren''t applied twice — once via forwardAttrs, once\n  via Vue''s default inheritance onto the same root.\n- D2eIconButton: require icon and ariaLabel. There''s no content slot, so\n  a call missing either produced a blank, unlabeled control.\n- D2eMenu: implement the roving-tabindex ARIA menu keyboard model\n  (Arrow Up/Down, Home/End) the role=\"menu\"/\"menuitem\" markup already\n  implied but didn''t back.\n- D2eExplorationCard: derive the checkbox''s default accessible name from\n  the exploration name instead of a shared \"Select exploration\" label.\n\nThe other six comments on that review were already resolved by later\ncommits on this branch (main.ts''s theme class was removed outright, the\ntwo story docs and explorer/.gitignore''s lockfile were fixed in\n87be952db and 10aaf0a9b, and D2eExplorationCard''s truncation/tooltip and\n\"By:\" prefix were fixed rebuilding it against the Figma design). Left\nthe missing D2eDialog behavior tests out — the fix would require\nmounting the component in vitest, which the repo''s testing policy rules\nout; that belongs in Playwright once the dialog is wired into an app.\n\n* refactor(ui): one source of truth for CSS design values, and no Bootstrap (#3253)\n\n* fix(vue-mri): define the colour properties that nothing defined\n\nEight `var(--color-…)` sites named a property that no stylesheet defines and\ngave no fallback. Each produced an invalid declaration, so the element\ninherited its colour instead. Error states rendered as normal text.\n\n`d4l-ui.css` supplies `--color-feedback-success` and `--color-feedback-alarm`\nbut no `-error`, and no `--color-text-primary`. Define both in `_main.scss`.\n\n`--color-feedback-error` takes `#a3293d`, the value the nine ShinyViewer sites\nalready carry as their fallback, so their rendering does not change. It is not\nrenamed to `--color-feedback-alarm`: that name holds d4l''s `#d53939`, is live\nin `DownloadMenu.vue`, and renaming would have flipped those nine working\nsites to the wrong red.\n\n`--color-text-primary` takes `#000080`, matching the fallback `_main.scss`\nalready uses for it.\n\nAlso drop the `color` declaration on the Execute side panel card title. It\nnamed `--color-support-soft-red`, which d4l does not define; the heading has\nalways inherited, and a red card title is not intended.\n\nEleven undefined names remain. Every one is used only with a fallback.\n\n* refactor(vue-mri): replace Bootstrap 4 with a scoped shim\n\nBootstrap 4.6.1 no longer compiles into the portal scope. `_bootstrap-shim.scss`\nreproduces what the app actually used: the reboot, the 16 utility and grid\nclasses that had no app rule of their own, and the base for the `.btn`,\n`.form-control`, `.card`, `.nav` and `.modal-*` families that app rules layer\non top. Values are taken from the app''s own Bootstrap build, not from the\ndefault one: the app overrode $font-size-base to 0.875rem after Bootstrap had\nalready bound $input-btn-font-size to 1rem, so the shim keeps 1rem there.\n\n`.text-primary` and `.bg-primary` are deliberately absent. They were the reason\n`@d2e/ui` carries a `brand` theme key: Bootstrap''s copies are scoped, carry\n!important and define no --bs-primary-rgb, so they beat Vuetify''s and render\ntransparent. `style.scss` no longer needs its .text-primary workaround, and the\nrename to `primary` is now unblocked.\n\n`_mri-bootstrap-variables.scss` becomes `_app-variables.scss`, 520 declarations\ndown to the ~20 the app reads plus their transitive dependencies. $primary and\n$blue (#007bff) are gone; nothing read them and they contradicted\n--color-primary.\n\nThe first shim draft dropped 50 element rules from the reboot. Screenshot\ndiffing found three panels had grown 4-12px; svg and img had lost\n`vertical-align: middle`, so every icon added its descender gap back into the\nrow height. The reboot is now complete except for print styles.\n\nVerified: app, atlas and atlas-app builds pass; 906 unit tests pass, with the\napp-segmented-button failure that is local-only. Visual re-verification against\nthe pre-change screenshots is still outstanding.\n\n* fix(vue-mri): match the shim to what the app''s Bootstrap build emitted\n\nThe shim was transcribed from `mri-bootstrap.scss` compiled on its own, which\nis not what the app shipped. `style.scss` does\n`@use ''./mri-bootstrap-variables'' as *` before it imports Bootstrap, so\n$font-size-base is already 0.875rem when Bootstrap evaluates\n`$input-btn-font-size: $font-size-base !default`. Five rules were one type\nstep too large:\n\n  .form-control      1rem      -> 0.875rem\n  .btn               1rem      -> 0.875rem\n  .form-control-sm   0.875rem  -> 0.765625rem\n  .btn-sm            0.875rem  -> 0.765625rem\n  .col-form-label-sm 0.875rem  -> 0.765625rem\n\nThat was the whole height regression: each text row rendered ~2px taller\nagainst a fixed control height, accumulating down a panel. The earlier\nsuspicion that `.col-form-label` was mis-padded was wrong; `.col-form-label-sm`\nwins on those labels and its calc(0.1rem + 1px) is the 2.6px observed.\n\nA full rule-by-rule diff against the original then found more gaps: `.container`\nwas absent entirely, along with `[hidden]`, the checkbox/radio box-sizing, the\nnumber-input spinners, `[type=search]`, `[role=button]`, `abbr[title]`, the\ncode/kbd/mark typography, `.card > hr`, `.form-control::-ms-expand`, and the\n`textarea`/`select` escapes from .form-control''s fixed height.\n\nAlso restores the `is-invalid` error icon (background-image plus the\npadding-right that reserves room for it), narrows `.is-invalid ~\n.invalid-feedback` to Bootstrap''s `.form-control.is-invalid ~`, and adds the\nprefers-reduced-motion guards for .form-control, .btn and .spinner-border.\n\nThe shim now differs from the original in five places, all deliberate:\nhtml/body (style.scss owns the container), two @media print borders, and\n`0rem` vs `0` on .modal-header.\n\nVerified: five component screenshots are pixel-identical to the pre-removal\nbaseline (RMSE 0), including the three that had grown. The two remaining\nnon-zero diffs are test-data drift, not CSS - the cohort under test moved from\nversion 1 to 2 with a new filter; the dialog itself matches exactly. App,\natlas and atlas-app builds pass; 906 unit tests pass.\n\n* refactor(ui): fold the brand theme key back into primary\n\n`brand` existed only because Bootstrap 4 was in the portal scope: its scoped\n`.bg-primary`/`.text-primary` carry !important and define no --bs-primary-rgb,\nso they beat Vuetify''s utilities and rendered transparent. Bootstrap''s\n$theme-colors had no `brand` entry, so the duplicate could not collide. The\nshim does not emit those utilities, so the collision is gone.\n\n`brand` and `brand-contrast` were exact duplicates of the existing `primary`\nkey (#000080), so they are deleted rather than renamed. `brand-hover` and\n`brand-info` keep their values as `primary-hover` and `primary-info`.\nD2eButton''s primary, secondary and ghost variants now use `primary`.\n\nVerified in the running app: inside .mri-app-vue-container both .bg-primary\nand .text-primary resolve to rgb(0, 0, 128), and only Vuetify''s rules apply.\ntokens:check clean, 25 library tests, verify:dist reports 17 exports, app and\natlas builds pass, 906 app tests pass.\n\n* refactor(vue-mri): point the colour palette at the design tokens\n\n`_main.scss` becomes an alias layer. Consumers keep their names; only the\ndefinitions change, so a regression is attributable to one line.\n\nOf the 105 properties it defined, 14 were consumed by nothing and are deleted.\nEight of those held values with no design token, which is why the unmappable\ngroup is 40 and not 48. Verified safe: no property name is built dynamically\nanywhere in the tree, none of the 14 appears elsewhere in plugins/ui, and the\nremoval cascade is empty.\n\nTwo more are gone as names. `--color-primary` and `--color-text-primary` were\nsynonyms for a token, not semantic names, and `--color-primary` was a name d4l\nalso defines, so all 126 call sites now read `var(--d2e-color-primary,\n#000080)` directly. Four fallback variants existed and three were wrong -\n#1f425a, #6c757d, #545b62 and #007bff, Bootstrap greys and blue that would have\nrendered if tokens.css ever failed to load. All are normalised.\n\nThe other 47 keep their names as aliases. Only 2 of the 49 token-resolving\nnames were primitive synonyms; the remaining 47 are semantic and carry 431 call\nsites, so rewriting them would collapse intent into primitives -\n--color-footer-button-text-light would become indistinguishable from sixty\nother whites.\n\nOf the 89 that survive: 29 alias directly, 18 are indirect, 2 are not colours,\nand 40 are quarantined under a banner. Those 40 have no equivalent in the\ndesign system - a legacy family of mid blues and teals up to delta 117 from the\nnearest token. They are not snapped and not imported into @d2e/ui; either would\nbe a visible recolour that needs design input.\n\nThen adds the 38 names d4l-ui.css also defines, so our stylesheets depend on\nour tokens rather than on a vendor file sharing our namespace. d4l keeps its\nown copies for its shadow-DOM components. Every consumed property without a\nfallback is now defined by us.\n\nVerified: dimensions unchanged on all five component screenshots; RMSE is\n~0.001, the 15 deliberate sub-perceptual snaps where a value sat within delta\n12 of its token. App and atlas builds pass, 906 unit tests pass.\n\n* docs(vue-mri): record why the shim drops Bootstrap''s print block\n\nEvery other omission in the shim is justified inline; this one was not.\nNothing calls window.print() and no d-print-* class is used, so it only\naffects a manual Ctrl+P.\n\nFound in review of #3253.\n\n* docs(vue-mri): note the deferred btn-primary/secondary/link colour finding\n\nPre-existing and left alone in this PR because fixing it recolours a shipping\nbutton. Recorded at the rule so it is not rediscovered from scratch.\n\nFound in review of #3253.\n\n* fix(vue-mri): correct five shim rules that diverged from the Bootstrap build\n\nFound by compiling style.scss on both branches and diffing rule-by-rule. The\nscreenshot comparison did not cover any of these.\n\nThe important one is new behaviour, not a missing rule. The shim carried\n`.form-control.is-invalid ~ .invalid-feedback { display: block }`, but\nBootstrap''s validation mixin interpolates `&`, so nested inside\n.mri-app-vue-container it compiled to `.mri-app-vue-container.is-invalid ~\n.invalid-feedback` - a compound selector that never matched. The rule was dead,\nand the app depends on that: FiltersFooter and QueryFilterModern each place\nseveral .invalid-feedback siblings after one input and reveal the right one\nwith an inline `display: block`. Live, the rule shows all of them at once, so\nan invalid cohort name rendered \"invalid name\", \"must not exceed 255\ncharacters\" and \"empty name\" together. It is now documented as deliberately\nabsent.\n\nFour rules were genuinely missing:\n\n- `select.form-control.is-invalid` and `textarea.form-control.is-invalid`\n  reposition the error icon. Without them the year pickers in\n  CompleteRequiredFiltersModal put the icon under the native dropdown arrow.\n- `[tabindex=\"-1\"]:focus:not(:focus-visible) { outline: 0 !important }`.\n  Without it ResizeObserver, bs-dropdown-item, app-tab, app-segmented-button\n  and Drawer paint a focus ring on programmatic or mouse focus.\n- `appearance: none` on date, time, month and datetime-local `.form-control`.\n  Without it the native control ignores the fixed height on iOS Safari.\n- The `:active:focus` box-shadow on the button variants, so they keep a focus\n  ring while held down.\n\nEach value is taken from the original compiled output and verified against it.\n\nFound in review of #3253.\n\n* feat(ui): rebuild the dialogs on the d2e component library (#3259)\n\n* feat(vue-mri): reskin the rename and delete dialogs (#3122, #3124)\n\n(cherry picked from commit 56c4facdfecb565007f514581c9fbdbb24b2413d)\n\n* feat(vue-mri): reskin the materialize dialog and drop the prop-watcher (#3118)\n\n(cherry picked from commit 0e71bd0fd1b5c71cc6a92204fcea51158ac9d21b)\n\n* refactor(vue-mri): rebuild UnsavedChangesDialog on D2eDialog\n\n(cherry picked from commit 67b5ebbcf4a655b78ed95968b37ad9d19a7f14c4)\n\n* style(vue-mri): format the dialog files with prettier\n\nApplication half of the original formatting commit. The library half is\nin the component-library branch.\n\n* fix(vue-mri): stop the UA input border striking through Vuetify field labels\n\n`vuetify-settings.scss` sets `$reset: false`, so Vuetify''s reset never runs.\nThat reset is what removes the user-agent border from form controls\n(`button, input, select, textarea { background-color: transparent;\nborder-style: none }`). Without it, `.v-field__input` keeps the browser''s\n2px inset grey border across the full width of the field, and an outlined\nfield''s floating label sits on that line — so the label renders struck\nthrough.\n\nVuetify''s own outline was correct throughout: the `start` and `end` segments\ncarry the navy border and the `notch` is at 0, so the gap for the label was\nopen. The grey line came from the raw input underneath.\n\nReproduce only that one rule, scoped to `.v-field`, so the app''s own\nBootstrap-style inputs keep their borders. Enabling the full Vuetify reset\nwould restyle the whole application.\n\nFound in manual verification. This is why the field renders correctly in\nHistoire, which loads Vuetify''s styles normally, and not in the app.\n\n* fix(ui): remove the dead space Vuetify components inherit from the app\n\nFour separate leaks put roughly 118px of unwanted space into every dialog.\nNone of them were design values; D2eDialog''s Figma padding is untouched.\n\n1. D2eTextField never set `hide-details`, so Vuetify reserved its 22px message\n   slot permanently. It now defaults to \"auto\", which reserves the space only\n   when there is a message. Errors still show.\n\n2. The shim''s `label` rule reached Vuetify''s field label. The notch label is\n   `position: static`, so Bootstrap''s 0.5rem added real height inside the\n   border gap. Scoped to `label:not(.v-label)`.\n\n3. The shim''s `hr` rule reached VDivider, which renders an <hr>. Bootstrap''s\n   1rem margins added 32px per divider, and a dialog has two. Scoped to\n   `hr:not(.v-divider)`.\n\n4. With those margins gone the browser''s own 0.5em <hr> margin took over,\n   because vuetify-settings.scss sets `$reset: false` and Vuetify''s reset is\n   what would normally zero it. `.v-divider { margin: 0 }` in the app scope.\n\nItems 2 and 3 are the same class of bug as the input border fixed in\n072cd4383: the shim faithfully reproduces Bootstrap''s element-level reboot,\nand Vuetify builds its components out of those same bare elements. Being\nfaithful to Bootstrap is the wrong goal wherever Vuetify now renders. The shim\nstyles twelve such elements; `button` is the next one worth checking, since\n`.mri-app-vue-container button` outranks `.v-btn`.\n\nRename dialog measured before and after: height 343 -> 238px, gap above the\nfield 70 -> 38px, below 57 -> 25px, field 52 -> 48px.\n\n25 library tests, verify:dist 17 exports, 906 app tests, atlas builds pass.\n\n* feat(vue-mri): rebuild the save-current-filters dialog on D2eDialog\n\nFound during manual verification: this dialog was never migrated. Its body was\nraw Bootstrap markup - form-group, row, col-sm-12, col-form-label,\nform-control, is-invalid - with three invalid-feedback divs toggled by inline\n`display: block` styles.\n\nNow D2eDialog + D2eTextField + D2eButton, matching the other four dialogs. The\nthree error strings fold into a `cohortNameErrors` computed feeding\n`error-messages`, so Vuetify owns their display and the field no longer needs\nthe is-invalid class.\n\nNote this is not the last one. A sweep found 16 more active messageBox dialogs\noutside the deprecated query-filter tree, including the reset-filters dialog in\nthis same file. They are listed with a suggested clustering in\ndocs/projects/vue-mri-ui/pr2/06-remaining-dialog-migration.md.\n\n* feat(vue-mri): port the reset-filters dialog and tighten the dialog body\n\nThree changes from manual verification.\n\nThe save-current-filters dialog loses its hint line. It told the user to enter\na name, which the empty-name validation already covers.\n\nThe reset-filters dialog moves to D2eDialog + D2eButton. It was the immediate\nneighbour of the one migrated in 7f57070aa and looked out of place beside it.\nIts old 400px width goes; it now uses the Modal/S default like the other\nconfirm dialogs. `messageBox` is no longer used in FiltersFooter, so the import\nand registration are gone too.\n\nD2eDialog''s body now collapses its last child''s bottom margin. A <p> in the\nbody carries a 1rem margin from the Bootstrap shim, which stacked on the body''s\n24px padding and put 40px above the divider. Collapsing the last child is\nbetter than dropping the padding: a body ending in a field has no margin of its\nown and still needs the 24px.\n\nThat is the fourth place the shim''s element-level reboot has leaked into\ncomponent markup, after input, label and hr.\n\n25 library tests, verify:dist 17 exports, 906 app tests, app build pass.\n\n* feat(vue-mri): rebuild the CSV download dialog on D2eDialog\n\nSeventh dialog migrated. The parent gates it with `v-if=\"csvShow\"`, so it is\nalways open when mounted and takes `:model-value=\"true\"`.\n\nDrops the inline `style=\"padding: 24px\"` that compensated for MessageBox\nhaving no body padding; D2eDialog supplies it. Buttons are reordered to\nCancel then Download, matching the other migrated dialogs.\n\n`LoadingAnimation` was imported and registered but never used in the template;\nit goes with `messageBox` and `appButton`.\n\n* fix(vue-mri): restore Enter-to-confirm and tidy the migrated dialogs\n\nTwo functional regressions from the migration, both mine.\n\n`v-focus` was replaced with the plain `autofocus` attribute on the CSV\ndownload and reset-filters confirm buttons. D2eButton declares no `autofocus`\nprop, so it fell through to the <button> as a raw attribute - and the HTML\nautofocus flush runs once per document, so it is inert for an element inserted\nlater. VDialog then focused its content wrapper instead, and pressing Enter did\nnothing. Both are back on `v-focus`, which calls el.focus() on mount. The text\nfields were never affected: VTextField declares `autofocus` and focuses\nimperatively.\n\nAddCohort''s Atlas branch still said \"Click OK to materialize this cohort\" after\nthe button was relabelled to Materialize, and the string was hardcoded English\nin a file where everything else is translated. It is now\nMRI_PA_COLL_CONFIRM_MATERIALIZE, added to all three locales. The dialog title\nalso regains the bookmark name, which the old header carried and the new one\ndropped - with several saved filters listed, there was nothing on screen saying\nwhich one was being materialized.\n\nBookmarks.renameErrorMessages returned on the first match, so a name that was\nboth a duplicate and too long showed only the duplicate error while the Rename\nbutton was disabled on length, leaving the button dead with no explanation. It\nnow accumulates, matching FiltersFooter.cohortNameErrors.\n\nD2eDialog''s `> :last-child` margin collapse excluded the busy overlay, which\nbecomes the last child whenever `busy` is true and handed the margin back\nmid-operation. The nested rule also moved below the declarations to clear Dart\nSass''s mixed-decls deprecation.\n\nUnsavedChangesDialog now emits `update:modelValue` alongside `stay`, so v-model\nis no longer write-only for a consumer that does not wire the `stay` handler.\n\nFound in review of #3259.\n\n* fix(ui): collapse the duplicate Vue install that breaks slot rendering\n\nplugins/ui installed two copies of Vue. vue-mri pinned \"vue\": \"3.5.17\"\nexactly, while apps/jobs and libs/d2e-ui resolved to 3.5.22, so bun\nhoisted 3.5.22 and nested 3.5.17 under the app.\n\nvite.config.ts aliases \"vue\" to the app copy, so every transformed\nmodule used 3.5.17. @vue/test-utils ships CommonJS, so its own\nrequire(\"vue\") bypassed the alias and mount() rendered with 3.5.22.\nThe two halves then disagreed: renderSlot read a\ncurrentRenderingInstance that the other runtime had set, found null,\nand failed with \"Cannot read properties of null (reading ''ce'')\". Any\nSFC that declares <slot> crashed. UnsavedChangesDialog is the first\nsuch component under test, so the fault surfaced here.\n\nRelax the vue-mri pin so bun hoists one copy, and add a workspace\noverride so that copy stays on 3.5.17. No app changes Vue version.\n\nThe split also masked a wrong assertion in app-segmented-button:\nprop reactivity did not reach the renderer, so the test asserted that\na newly selected item stays unselected. Correct it.\n\nAdd a guard to vitest.setup.ts. It compares the vue that the app\nresolves with the vue that @vue/test-utils resolves, and fails with a\nnamed error if they diverge again.\n\n* feat(vue-mri): Data Exploration page (#3116) (#3262)\n\n* feat(portal): make researcher plugin app ids route-aware\n\n(cherry picked from commit 7af376f251d8b5458d7ce7c829724bc2d07369e2)\n\n* feat(ui): register the exploration plugin route\n\n(cherry picked from commit 14fc760b2c6a65ff598a8b08b92ea2e5681452e7)\n\n* feat(vue-mri): add the exploration page shell and navigation view\n\n(cherry picked from commit 4c95249add0688260ca9192744f4a18a564f87a7)\n\n* fix(vue-mri): complete initial load on the exploration view\n\n(cherry picked from commit c9bf0c638dbb77f4b69769b697a2532192ced886)\n\n* refactor(vue-mri): drop the exploration route plumbing\n\nThe exploration page is the main view of vue-mri, reached in place, not a\nsecond single-spa route. Remove the second uiplugin entry, the route-aware\nresearcher app ids, the view prop and its plumbing, and the App.vue switch.\n\nResearcherStudyPluginRenderer.tsx and plugins/ui/package.json now match\norigin/develop again.\n\n* feat(vue-mri): mount the exploration page in place of the bookmarks list\n\nHoist the exploration view out of the splitter in PatientAnalytics, gated on\ndisplayCohorts, and drop the <bookmarks> block it replaces. The first nav tab\nstill calls toggleCohorts(true), which now returns to the page.\n\nCarry over the behaviour that lived in Bookmarks.vue:\n\n- the ?bmkId= deep-link restore, as a watch on querystring.bmkId\n- loading a bookmark on card click, behind the unsaved-changes guard, then\n  swapping to the splitter view\n\nFollow Bookmarks.vue in the page itself: source the username through\nusePortalContext, drop the completeInitialLoad dispatch and the on-mount load\nnow that PatientAnalytics owns both, and build the six metadata rows the\ndesign asks for. Unmaterialised rows show a dash instead of disappearing.\n\nAlso remove the debug logging from BookmarkItems.vue.\n\n* feat(ui): add D2eCheckbox, D2eSelect and an anchored D2eMenu\n\nThree form primitives the exploration toolbar and card need. D2eMenu was a\nstatic button list with no trigger or open/close logic; it now takes an\nactivator slot, anchors through VMenu, and navigates with the arrow keys.\n\nEach ships with a Histoire story and a unit test over its constant map, and\ntakes every colour from a --d2e-* token.\n\n* feat(vue-mri): build out the exploration toolbar, card and actions\n\nCloses the rest of #3116 on the exploration page.\n\nToolbar: scored search (id 100, name 50, description 25, author 10) lifted out\nof BookmarkItems.vue into a pure, tested helper; a Sort by menu offering Last\nupdated and Name A-Z/Z-A; the data source styled as a disabled D2eSelect; and\na working \"Start new exploration\".\n\nCards: person count, the three materialisation rows and the Exploration\nbookmark panel, with an id row that reads Cohort ID for Atlas records. A\nnever-materialised card shows a Materialize action in place of the count.\n\nActions: Materialize and a More menu carrying Rename and Delete, gated on\nownership and on whether the dataset can materialise cohorts. Rename and\nDelete are extracted from Bookmarks.vue into their own components so the card\nhas an entry point for #3122 and #3124.\n\nEvery visible string resolves through i18n; the de and zh strings need native\nreview.\n\n* fix(vue-mri): correct the exploration card and page against the Figma frame\n\nCard, from frame 1798:192269:\n- Add the status chip. \"Ready\" and \"Not run yet\" are derivable from the\n  bookmark-to-cohort link; \"stale\" is not, so it is never produced (#3117).\n- Cards fill their grid cell instead of sitting at a fixed 324px, and take a\n  hover state and a pointer cursor so it reads as clickable.\n- The lead Materialize is an outlined button with a leading icon, per the\n  not-run variant.\n\nFixes:\n- \"Start new exploration\" was dead: PatientAnalytics does not map\n  getBookmarks, so checkCohortName threw on an undefined list.\n- Materialize opened the exploration instead of the dialog. Its click bubbled\n  from the lead row to the card root, which was not in the ignore list.\n- Closing the materialize dialog no longer reloads the list. AddCohort already\n  reloads on success, so the close handler was a duplicate.\n- Drop the refresh button; it is not in the frame.\n\nAdd the data quality, filter summary and analyze icons as inert placeholders\nso the action bar matches the frame. They belong to #3119, #3120 and #3121.\n\n* fix(vue-mri): match the exploration page container, icons and id row\n\n- Wrap the page in the tinted surface plus one rounded white card, inset 24px\n  (Figma 1676:221311). The card was previously invisible against a white page.\n- Close the breadcrumb with the 24x2 secondary rule, and drop the breadcrumb to\n  10px Medium with 1px tracking (Figma 1676:221313).\n- Lay the grid out as fixed 324px columns rather than flexible ones; the frame\n  is 1344 = 4x324 + 3x16. Toolbar right group closes to an 8px gap.\n- The id row shows the materialised cohort''s id, so a card that has never been\n  materialised now reads \"-\" instead of repeating the bookmark id.\n- Replace the guessed MDI glyphs with the icons exported from action bar\n  1798:192998, rendered through a new slot on D2eIconButton and D2eButton.\n\nAnalyze keeps an MDI glyph: Figma''s export for that one instance returns a\nstale layer named \"Bell\" whose geometry is a bell, while the rendered node is a\nchart line. The reason is recorded on the component.\n\n* fix(vue-mri): polish the exploration toolbar, card chrome and more menu\n\n- Search: the field owns the 16px inset and the icon an 8px end margin, so the\n  magnifier no longer reads as a second, empty prepend slot.\n- Sort by is a real text button with a 22px prepended sort icon exported from\n  Figma 2634:58663, which also gives it padding away from the primary button.\n- Card lead row gains a bottom margin, and D2eStatusChip gains the 8px\n  horizontal padding the frame specifies.\n- Card Materialize outlines in Primary/Lightest (Figma 1798:192920), not the\n  default primary.\n- Quick-action tooltips are white with neutral 12px text (Figma 1798:208323).\n  The rule is unscoped because Vuetify teleports tooltip content to body.\n- More menu follows Figma 1801:215921: 44px rows, 16px labels, leading icons,\n  Delete in the alarm colour through a new `danger` flag on D2eMenuItem, and\n  Duplicate present but disabled until #3123''s backend command exists.\n\n* fix(vue-mri): tooltip the More button, colour menu icons, tidy the data source\n\n- The More (⋮) button gains the tooltip its four neighbours already had.\n- Menu icons take the row''s colour, so Rename reads primary, Delete alarm and\n  a disabled row neutral (Figma 1801:215921).\n- The data source label was clipped because Figma''s 12px line-height at a 12px\n  font size cuts the glyph box; the line box may now grow. The read-only field\n  also keeps full contrast and drops the empty details row that rendered as a\n  stray rule beneath it.\n- Card title and every metadata value now carry a tooltip only while the text\n  is actually truncated, per the note on frame 2635:208762. The overflow test\n  is a pure function with its own unit test.\n\n* fix(vue-mri): close the defects found in code review\n\nGuards restored from Bookmarks.vue:\n- Rename was offered on Atlas records, where the D2E branch dereferences a null\n  bookmark and throws into a silent catch. Gate it on the bookmark type as well\n  as ownership.\n- Reopening the exploration that is already active re-loaded it, discarding an\n  in-progress edit and prompting for unsaved changes on a no-op. Short-circuit\n  to the splitter view instead.\n- A bookmark incompatible with the active config failed into an empty catch, so\n  the click looked dead. Surface it as an alert, as the message box used to.\n- Delete reset the filters but not the chart properties, so a deleted\n  exploration''s axes and display mode leaked into the empty state. Use the\n  resetChart action, which dispatches both.\n\nData correctness:\n- Materialize is hidden for a record with neither a bookmark nor an Atlas\n  definition; it was building a generate URL containing \"null\".\n- Card keys are namespaced by source table. A bookmark id and a cohort id can\n  collide, and one checkbox then selected two cards.\n- AddCohort was passed `bookmark.bookmarkname`, which formatBookmark never\n  sets; the field is `name`.\n\nAlso: only the lead row''s button swallows the card click, not the person count\nand status chip beside it; only a card that opens looks clickable; a clickable\ncard is reachable by keyboard; and the dialogs no longer trigger a second list\nreload on top of their own.\n\n* chore(ui): pin vue to 3.5.22\n\nReview asked for an exact pin in both plugins/ui/package.json and\nplugins/ui/apps/vue-mri-ui-lib/package.json, per the decision taken in\nthe workshop.\n\nThe application dependency was a caret range, \"^3.5.17\", so an install\non a new machine or a later date could resolve a different patch from\nthe one the root override names. That is the same class of drift this\nbranch already fixed once: a second Vue copy in the graph breaks slot\nrendering, and the symptom appears far from the cause. An exact version\nin both places means the override and the dependency cannot disagree.\n\nThe component explorer stays on 3.5.26. It is outside the bun workspace\nbecause Histoire needs a different Vite, and explorer-parity.test.ts\ncompares the Vue *minor*, not the patch, so 3.5 on both sides keeps that\nguard satisfied.\n\nVerified: one vue in the app''s resolution path at 3.5.22; 1083 vue-mri\ntests pass; the d2e-ui suite, including the parity guard, passes; all\nfour builds pass.\n\nThe nested vue 3.2.0 under gethue is untouched. It is a transitive\ndependency isolated in its own node_modules and never reaches the app.\n\n* feat(vue-mri): hide the Data quality action until it does something\n\nThe button rendered on every exploration card so the action bar matched\nthe frame, but clicking it did nothing: the data quality page belongs to\nanother plugin and wiring it up is #3119. A control that looks live and\nis inert reads as a broken feature, which is worse than not offering it\nyet.\n\nHidden behind a SHOW_DATA_QUALITY constant rather than deleted. The icon,\nthe label key, the test id and the render loop all stay, so bringing it\nback for the next release is a one line change and not a rebuild.\n\nThe loop is left in place too, over an empty list, so a future action can\nbe added without restoring markup.\n\nVerified against a running stack rather than assumed: no\nexplorations-dq-btn renders, while materialize, filter summary, analyze\nand the More menu still render on all twelve cards. 1191 unit tests pass\nand the portal build passes.\n\nExplorationsPage.vue does not satisfy prettier, and did not before this\nchange either, so it is left as it is rather than reformatted into an\nunrelated diff.\n\n* test(e2e): enter the cohort builder through the redesigned page (#3348)\n\n* test(e2e): enter the cohort builder through the redesigned page\n\nThe suite entered the cohort builder by clicking a button labelled\n\"D2E\" (MRI_PA_CREATE_D2E_COHORT_TEXT) in the old Bookmarks header. The\nData Exploration redesign replaced that page, and the button with it, so\nthe click timed out after 20 seconds.\n\nThis is not a screenshot mismatch. The element does not exist, the test\nnever reached its assertions, and with maxFailures at 1 in CI that single\ntimeout stopped the other 68 tests from running at all.\n\n25 call sites across 19 files. A test id rather than the new label, so it\nsurvives copy changes and does not depend on the run''s locale.\n\n* test(e2e): drop the Atlas button assertion, which has no equivalent\n\nThe old Bookmarks header carried a D2E / Atlas / Import / Compare button\ngroup. The redesign has a single \"Start new exploration\" action, so the\ncheck that the Atlas cohort-definition button is visible has no control\nleft to point at, in any state.\n\nRather than assert something weaker that would pass for the wrong\nreason, this step now asserts what it is really there for: that turning\nPA-Atlas on leaves the Cohorts screen reachable and rendering.\n\nThe missing Atlas entry point is a question for review, not a test fix.\nNothing in the redesign notes records dropping the Atlas create and\nimport actions. If they are meant to survive they need a home on the new\npage, and this assertion should come back.\n\n* test(e2e): select cohorts by checkbox before comparing\n\nBoth specs run the same \"select two cohorts, then Compare\" flow, and\nboth break on the selection. The bulk-actions bar keeps the ''Compare''\nlabel, so those assertions are untouched.\n\n- e2e_PA_and_cohorts used `pa-cohort-card-*` and `pa-cohort-select-btn`.\n  Those ids exist only in BookmarkItems.vue, which is imported only by\n  Bookmarks.vue, which the redesign no longer mounts. They are absent\n  from the built bundle - the component is tree-shaken out - so they\n  could never match.\n- patient-group_comparison clicked an svg inside each card''s `.footer`.\n  That structure is gone.\n\nBoth now check the card''s own checkbox, which carries the accessible\nname \"Select exploration <name>\". Naming the cohort also fixes a latent\nweakness: the list sorts by last updated, so nth-child(1) and (2) were\nnever guaranteed to be the two cohorts the test had just created.\n\nFound by auditing selectors against the current UI, not by CI - CI stops\nat the first failure, so it would have taken two more 40-minute cycles\nto surface these. Verified against a running stack: the selector checks\ntwo cards, raises the bulk bar and leaves Compare enabled.\n\n* test(e2e): refresh the 01-example baseline for the redesigned page\n\nWith the selector fixed the test reached its screenshot, which then\nfailed on 12,566 pixels, 2% of the image. Two real changes, both\nexpected from this stack and both confirmed by eye against the expected\nimage CI uploaded:\n\n- The builder tab reads \"New exploration\" where it read \"New cohort\".\n- Filter-panel fields sit a few pixels lower, about 24px by the\n  INCLUSION/Exclusion tabs, from the design-token spacing.\n\nNothing else moved. The chart, the toolbar and the 1,321 / 2,694 count\nare identical, with no overlap, clipping or missing control - so this is\nthe baseline moving, not a regression.\n\nThe replacement is the PNG CI itself rendered, taken from the failing\nrun''s error-context artifact. A macOS run writes example-1-darwin.png,\nwhich CI never reads.\n\nCI retried, so the run carried two attempts. They differ by 3 pixels at\na maximum channel delta of 1 - antialiasing noise, inside Playwright''s\nthreshold - which is the evidence that one committed baseline holds\nacross runs.\n\n* test(e2e): a supported way to refresh screenshot baselines on Linux\n\nBaselines are committed per platform and CI runs Linux, so the files are\n`*-linux.png`. A run on macOS writes `*-darwin.png`, which CI never\nreads. There was no documented way to regenerate the Linux ones, so a\nbaseline that legitimately moved had no route back to green.\n\n`container` builds the image CI builds and re-renders against the local\nstack. One trick worth recording: the stack answers TLS only for SNI\n`localhost`, so dialling the caddy container by name returns a TLS\ninternal error rather than a certificate warning that ignoreHTTPSErrors\nwould absorb. The script forwards localhost:41100 inside the container\ninstead.\n\n`from-ci` takes the screenshots CI actually rendered, from the artifact\nthe workflow already uploads. This is the faithful option and the only\npractical one on Apple Silicon, where container mode runs amd64 Chromium\nunder emulation - a 24 second test had not finished after ten minutes.\n\nBoth modes tell the reader to open every changed PNG before committing,\nbecause --update-snapshots records a regression as happily as a fix.\n\n* test(e2e): assert the redesigned Cohorts toolbar on page load\n\nCI confirmed this one. cohortPageLoad is a smoke test that the Cohorts\nscreen renders its primary controls, and every control it asserted came\nfrom the old Bookmarks header: the ''Create Cohort:'' title and a\nD2E / Import / Shared / Compare button group.\n\nIt now asserts the toolbar the redesign puts there - search, filters,\nsort, new exploration and the data source select - plus the page root.\n\nThree of the old assertions have no replacement, which is recorded in\nthe test rather than quietly dropped:\n\n- ''Shared'', the show-shared-cohorts toggle, has no equivalent.\n- ''Import'', for an Atlas cohort definition, has no entry point on the\n  new page. That is the same open question atlas_cohort_definition.spec\n  raises, not something this test can asserted around.\n- ''Compare'' moved into the bulk-actions bar, which appears only once a\n  card is selected, so it is no longer a page-load control.\n\nVerified against a running stack: all six locators resolve on load.\n\n* test(e2e): act on exploration cards by name, not by icon position\n\nThe last of the suite''s dependencies on the old Bookmarks card, fixed in\none pass rather than one CI cycle at a time.\n\nEach old card carried five unlabelled icons and tests reached them\npositionally - `.footer > div:nth-child(2) > svg` for rename,\n`nth-child(5)` for delete. That markup is gone. It was fragile on its own\nterms too: the position encoded the action, so inserting an icon would\nsilently repoint a test at a different one, and `.first()` meant several\n\"delete this cohort\" steps actually deleted whichever card sorted first.\n\nAdd tests/explorations.ts and name the action instead of counting\nsiblings: explorationCard, selectExploration, explorationAction,\nexplorationMenuAction, confirmExplorationDialog, deleteExploration.\n\nThe reskinned dialogs moved more than markup, and those assertions are\nupdated with them:\n\n  Rename Saved Filter          -> Rename exploration name\n  Delete Saved Filter          -> Delete filter?\n  confirm button \"Save\"        -> \"Rename\"\n  confirm button \"Delete\"      -> \"Yes, delete\"\n\nThe helper confirms through the `pa-save-dialog-save-btn` test id, which\nis stable across both dialogs and survives the next label change.\n\npatient-analytics-config-mri asserted the old header as an aria\nsnapshot. It now asserts the toolbar controls by test id: the snapshot\npinned copy and ordering the test does not care about, which is exactly\nwhat made a reskin fail it.\n\nMenu items are role=\"menuitem\", so they cannot collide with a same-named\nrole=\"button\" in the dialog underneath - which matters for Rename and\nDelete, where the confirm button repeats the word.\n\nVerified: all 69 tests parse, no reference to removed markup remains,\nand cohortPageLoad passes against a running stack. The specs that create\ntheir own cohorts cannot run locally - they need CI''s monthOfBirth seed\npatch - so CI is the authority on those.\n\n* test(e2e): assert the empty state, not its wording\n\nTwo specs asserted \"You have not yet saved any cohort definitions\",\nwhich was the old Bookmarks list''s empty state. The redesign''s reads\n\"No explorations yet\" with the body \"Your saved data exploration will\nappear here.\"\n\nBoth now assert the `explorations-empty` test id. The point of the step\nis that the list emptied after a delete, not what the copy says, and a\ntest id does not have to be revisited the next time the wording is\ntuned.\n\nFound by the same audit pass as the card selectors, not by CI.\n\n* test(e2e): confirm dialogs through their buttons, not a <footer>\n\nCI''s fourth and, by this sweep, last class of redesign breakage.\n\nEvery dialog in the cohort builder used to render its buttons inside a\n`<template v-slot:footer>`, which produced a real `<footer>` element, and\n15 call sites reached the Save and Cancel buttons through\n`page.locator(''footer'')`. D2eDialog renders `<div class=\"d2e-dialog__actions\">`\ninstead, so the locator matches nothing and every one of them times out.\n\nThey now use `pa-save-dialog-save-btn` and `pa-save-dialog-cancel-btn`,\nwhich the components already carried and which do not depend on the\ndialog''s element structure.\n\nAll 15 are the dialog''s buttons, not the builder''s own Save: the old\nmarkup put the dialog''s footer in the same place, and bookmark.spec''s\nCancel click is only meaningful inside the dialog. The builder''s own\nSave has its own id, pa-save-cohort-btn, and is untouched here.\n\nChecked the other old modal hooks in the same pass: `.modal-wrapper` and\n`.modal-body` still exist, because the thirteen dialogs still on\nMessageBox were never migrated. Those call sites are left alone.\n\n* test(e2e): name which Save is meant, the builder''s or the dialog''s\n\nFifth class, and it only appeared once the fourth was fixed.\n\nThe builder''s Save (pa-save-cohort-btn) opens the save dialog, and that\ndialog has its own Save (pa-save-dialog-save-btn). Both are called\n\"Save\", so `getByRole(''button'', { name: ''Save'' })` is ambiguous whenever\nboth are on the page, and Playwright''s strict mode fails rather than\nguess. CI caught it on bookmark.spec''s *second* Save click, with both\nbuttons in the accessibility tree.\n\nEach call site is now explicit about which button it means. The split is\nby what the test does next: a Save followed by the \"Enter name\" field is\nthe builder''s, a Save that confirms is the dialog''s.\n\nThe Save buttons on the admin configuration pages - wizard,\natlas_cohort_definition, cohort-entry-and-exit, smoketest_mri''s config\nstep - are a different screen with no such pairing, and are left alone.\n\nI first wrote that D2eDialog retains its content when closed, and that\nthis was why the collision appeared now. A probe against a running stack\ndisproved it: the dialog''s Save button count goes 0 -> 1 -> 0 -> 1\nacross open, cancel and reopen, so closed dialogs do unmount. The\ncollision is real and reproduced by CI, but I have not established why\nit did not bite before this branch, and the claim is removed rather than\nleft standing on a guess.\n\nThat probe does confirm the fix itself: pa-save-dialog-save-btn resolves\nto exactly one element while a dialog is open, even though three\ncomponents share the id, because only the open dialog is mounted.\n\n* test(e2e): name the rename dialog''s field\n\nFour bare `getByRole(''textbox'')` calls in the rename flow. Measured on a\nrunning stack, the Data Exploration page has three text inputs while the\nrename dialog is open - the dialog''s field plus the page''s own search\nbox and data source select - so the bare locator is ambiguous and\nPlaywright''s strict mode fails rather than pick one.\n\nThey now name the field, \"Exploration name\", which is the rename\ndialog''s label and distinct from the save dialog''s \"Enter name\".\n\nPre-emptive: CI has not reached these lines yet. It is the same shape as\nthe Save collision it did reach, and the ambiguity is confirmed by\ncounting the inputs rather than assumed.\n\n* test(e2e): delete by name in patient-list too\n\nMissed by the earlier sweep. My grep required the `.footer` ancestor and\nthis call site omits it - `div:nth-child(5) > svg` on its own - so it\nnever matched the pattern even though it is the same old card icon, in\nthe same position, meaning the same delete action.\n\nThe confirm that follows it was labelled \"Delete\"; the reskinned dialog\nconfirms with \"Yes, delete\". Both halves moved, so both are replaced by\ndeleteExploration().\n\nRe-checked the rest of the vue-mri specs for positional icon clicks with\na pattern that does not assume `.footer`: this was the only one left.\nThe remaining `getByRole(''button'', { name: ''Delete'' })` calls are scoped\nto a `userRow` in the admin user table and are a different control.\n\n* test(e2e): assert the card, not the old card''s concatenated text\n\nSeventh cause. The old card rendered its name and icon labels as one\ntext node, so the suite asserted strings like `${NAME.savedFilters}0.\nIcons/`. The card is a component now and that text does not exist.\n\nNine assertions across three specs. They use explorationCard(page, name)\ninstead, which finds the card by the name shown on it and does not\ndepend on how the rest of the card serialises to text.\n\nAlso lift maxFailures for the next few runs, marked TEMPORARY and to be\nreverted before merge.\n\nA cap of 1 ends the run at the first failure, so this branch has been\nsurfacing one cause per CI cycle at roughly forty minutes each - six\ncycles for six causes, with no way to know how many remain. Three of\nthose causes were only visible at runtime, so no amount of static\nauditing would have found them ahead of time. Lifting the cap lists\nevery remaining failure in one run.\n\n* test(e2e): refresh three baselines, and stop asserting dialogs in #pane-left\n\nWith maxFailures lifted the run listed everything at once: 41 passed, 8\nfailed, in three groups.\n\nScreenshots (3). cohort-entry-and-exit, extended-query-logic and\nfiltering-bar…","tree":{"sha":"a2fea34aa2385522fae19706c72b563d213dec89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/git/trees/a2fea34aa2385522fae19706c72b563d213dec89"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/git/commits/fc3384cc8d783fd2216867f52a23219680ec5ede","verification":{"payload":"tree a2fea34aa2385522fae19706c72b563d213dec89\nparent 5bd030792fd339a5f9894cf596d8ee224cde2496\nauthor Khairul Syazwan <80243918+khairul-syazwan@users.noreply.github.com> 1790170630 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790170630 +0000\n\nfeat(ui): add the d2e component library and the Histoire explorer (#3204)\n\n* refactor(vue-mri): remove the unused atlas theme\n\n(cherry picked from commit 8f22ee68dd96ffd43f8105289599c311770b62e8)\n\n* feat(ui): add the @d2e/ui package with design tokens and histoire\n\n(cherry picked from commit 2e095dec72fc364af0dcb1bfdc9d51e14d999596)\n\n* feat(ui): add D2eDialog, D2eButton and D2eTextField\n\n(cherry picked from commit e5a8dbb430e21d58c4c389cfa234ead2ae242631)\n\n* refactor(vue-mri): drive the vuetify d2e theme from @d2e/ui tokens\n\n(cherry picked from commit 59aadc48cdf285d91eeabdc3e7369687e14fd01b)\n\n* fix(ui): use literal colors in D2eButton to avoid bootstrap utility collisions\n\n(cherry picked from commit 75414bea71e8840a6bc35d7318003d409f3067c2)\n\n* style(ui): format the library files with prettier\n\nLibrary half of the original formatting commit. The application half\ngoes with the dialog changes.\n\n* refactor(ui): use mri-brand theme key for D2eButton colors\n\n(cherry picked from commit 977b92b633cc47993eafd32780fcfad74e72ee8b)\n\n* feat(ui): add slice 2 design tokens\n\n(cherry picked from commit 268c408fa58447db64aac3493d7454b0a8f27bb8)\n\n* feat(ui): add D2eStatusChip, D2eIconButton and D2eMenu\n\n(cherry picked from commit 50d4ae4682c4b2c3273b3bb246373301b23a396b)\n\n* feat(ui): add D2eCard, D2eToolbar and D2eExplorationCard\n\n(cherry picked from commit 2bf1177dc6b87f17a66fb79248fe9ce587dfad58)\n\n* feat(ui): make D2eCard width configurable\n\n(cherry picked from commit 7f5bedd16d14b7b6b8fbdcf56a681c3f06bd7045)\n\n* fix(ui): emit unitless font weight and line height tokens\n\nThe token generator added `px` to each number. This made\n`--d2e-font-*-weight` and the ratio `--d2e-font-*-line-height` values\ninvalid, for example `font-weight: 600px` and `line-height: 1.2px`. The\nbrowser ignored both declarations.\n\nThe effect was not visible in the dialogs, because each affected element\nholds one line of text. It was visible in D2eExplorationCard, where the\nmetadata rows collapsed to 1.5 px and printed on top of each other.\n\nKeep `weight`, `lineHeight`, `opacity` and `zIndex` unitless. Add a test\nthat fails if a weight or a ratio line height gets a unit again.\n\n(cherry picked from commit ca03e1f38574680e87d73a6038774b208e75cb8d)\n\n* chore(ui): track the component explorer as a sub-project\n\nThe explorer was an untracked proof of concept. Track it, so that each\ndeveloper can start it with the same dependency versions.\n\nHistoire needs vite 7. `plugins/ui/package.json` pins vite to 6.4.2 with\nan override, to hold libs/react-notebook at vite 6. Bun applies an\noverride to all packages in the workspace. The workspace globs are\n`libs/*` and `apps/*`, which match one level only, so this directory is\noutside the workspace. It uses npm and its own lockfile, and it can\ntherefore use vite 7.\n\nAlso:\n\n- Align `vue` with apps/vue-mri-ui-lib at 3.5.17. `vuetify` already\n  agreed at 3.12.0. The explorer must show what the application renders.\n- Add `.nvmrc` and `engine-strict=true`, because the explorer needs\n  Node 20.19 or later and a default shell Node can be older.\n- Keep the lockfile in git. `plugins/ui/.gitignore` ignores each\n  `package-lock.json`, so the explorer negates that rule.\n- Add `.prettierignore`, to keep `prettier --write .` away from the\n  lockfile and the build output.\n\n(cherry picked from commit d849a464dfeb988e61d20c136a11cff7039c3217)\n\n* chore(ui): remove the histoire setup that the workspace cannot run\n\n`histoire.config.ts` and `histoire.setup.ts` were in the library root,\nand the `ui:dev` and `ui:build` scripts started them. They cannot run,\nbecause histoire needs vite 7 and the workspace override pins vite 6.\n\nThe working copies are now in `explorer/`. Two configurations, where one\nof them cannot run, is a trap for the next reader.\n\nThis also removes an undeclared dependency problem: the deleted\n`histoire.setup.ts` imported `@mdi/font`, `@fontsource-variable/ibm-plex-sans`\nand `sass`, which this package never declared. They resolved only through\nbun hoisting. The explorer declares all three.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 59ede28af997fa5cb6b1e518cc699a3281adb204)\n\n* docs(ui): explain how to start the component explorer\n\nGive the library a README, and give the explorer a README with one\ncommand sequence that includes the Node version step. Record why the\nexplorer is outside the workspace, and the two rules that keep it\nworking.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 65560a77dcee6921c47006d506600c8ca19306aa)\n\n* test(ui): guard the explorer against workspace and version drift\n\nTwo properties are load-bearing and silent when they break:\n\n- The workspace globs match one level only. A deeper glob pulls the\n  explorer into the workspace, where the vite 6 override stops Histoire.\n- The explorer must use the vue and vuetify versions of the application,\n  or it shows something the application does not render.\n\nAssert both against the three package.json files. The test reads JSON\nonly; it mounts no component.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 346ff0f147ae47caac80806d71c671aed12a4e01)\n\n* fix(ui): keep the explorer on the vue version histoire accepts\n\n`@histoire/plugin-vue@1.0.0-beta.1` needs `vue ^3.5.26`, and\napps/vue-mri-ui-lib pins `vue 3.5.17`. An exact match makes `npm ci`\nfail with ERESOLVE.\n\nPin 3.5.26 and record the constraint in the README. The parity test\nalready compares the major and minor version only, so it still holds.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 9e9bbbbc04f97c12b4ded963acc567264680e4c5)\n\n* fix(ui): correct the modal scale, add button icons, stop scrim dismissal\n\nThree gaps found by checking the library against the Figma design system\n(file lpbqxd8B0OkRKH9kJoCCEa) through the component explorer.\n\n**Modal scale.** The Figma variables are Modal/S 540, Modal/L 900 and\nModal/XL 1200. There is no Modal/M, and 600 appears nowhere in the design\nsystem, but `tokens.ts` carried `md: 600` and D2eDialog defaulted to it.\nDrop the invented size, add a `size` prop over the real scale, and default\nto Modal/S — the rename, delete and materialize frames are all Modal/S.\n`maxWidth` stays as an escape hatch. A test locks the scale.\n\n**Button icons.** The Figma Button set has a `Sub category` axis of\nDefault / Icon front / Icon back. D2eButton had none of it. Its `icon`\nprop forwarded to `v-btn`''s `icon`, which makes an icon-only round button\nand drops the label, so the \"with icon\" story rendered no label at all.\nReplace it with `prependIcon` and `appendIcon`. Use D2eIconButton when an\nicon-only control is wanted.\n\n**Scrim dismissal.** MODAL CLOSE BEHAVIOR (2106:162) says clicking the\noverlay must not dismiss a modal, for every modal type. The dialog was\ndismissable. `v-dialog` is now always persistent, and Escape is handled\ndirectly so informational modals still close on it. `closeOnEscape`\nturns that off for long forms and multi-step flows, which the same\nframe says must raise a confirm-discard step instead.\n\nThe `persistent` prop is gone: the overlay never dismisses now, so the\nonly remaining axis is Escape.\n\n* fix(ui): split the dialog sizes into variants and drop the button ripple\n\nThe single \"sizes\" story showed one dialog at one size, so the scale was\nnot demonstrable — the sizes looked like they did nothing.\n\nGive each size its own variant. The `size` prop was in fact working; the\nstory sandbox was fixed at 720 px, so Modal/L (900) and Modal/XL (1200)\nboth clamped to the pane and rendered identically. Setting\n`responsive-disabled` on the story lets the preview scale with the\nwindow: S renders at 540 everywhere, L reaches 900 and XL reaches 1200\non a wide window, and both clamp below that — the same thing a real\nbrowser does. Each variant states its max-width.\n\nAlso turn off the Vuetify ripple on D2eButton, D2eIconButton and the\ndialog close button. The Figma button set defines discrete Hover,\nFocused and Pressed states and no ripple animation.\n\n* fix(ui): source-export the d2e component library to unblock the atlas build\n\nThe patient-analytics sub-plugin is installed in CI with\n`npm install --workspaces=false` inside apps/vue-mri-ui-lib, which\nresolves @d2e/ui from the registry and 404s on the private package.\n\nAlias @d2e/ui to libs/d2e-ui/src/index.ts and @d2e/ui/tokens.css to\nlibs/d2e-ui/src/tokens/tokens.css in the three vite configs and in\ntsconfig, and drop the dependency. This keeps the source-export model\nand works for both bun and npm.\n\n* fix(ui): resolve the d2e library''s vue/vuetify during the isolated atlas build\n\nThe patient-analytics atlas build installs only the app with\n`npm install --workspaces=false`, so the d2e library source aliased from\nlibs/d2e-ui sits outside the app node_modules and cannot resolve the vue\nand vuetify it imports. Alias vue and the vuetify entries the library uses\n(components, directives, styles, and the package root) to the app''s\ninstalled copy, leaving the Sass subpaths such as vuetify/settings for the\nSass node importer.\n\n* fix(ui): rebuild D2eExplorationCard against the current Figma design\n\nThe card was built from an older node and was structurally wrong. Rebuilt\nfrom the Exploration card component set (ticket file, 1810:239213 —\nready / Not run / Stale) via the Figma MCP.\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- The card surface is white with a 1px #DEDCDA border and radius 16. The\n  #FAF8F8 radius-12 surface we used for the whole card is actually the\n  nested \"Exploration bookmark\" panel, which was missing entirely.\n- Added the person count row: count in Heading 4 with the status chip\n  right-aligned beside it. This was the most prominent element in the\n  design and we had none of it.\n- Added the nested bookmark panel (created by / last updated / version)\n  with its rule.\n- Removed the invented `By:` label. The design has no such label; the\n  chip belongs on the count row.\n- The checkbox moves to the right of the title, in the 20 px box the\n  design reserves.\n- Metadata values are now Subtitle 2 in Primary/Default, right aligned,\n  and both name and description truncate with a tooltip, per the design''s\n  own note.\n- `status` becomes `ready | not-run | stale` and drives the chip. The\n  `#lead` slot replaces the count so `not-run` can carry the Materialize\n  action, as the design shows.\n- The action bar gets the design''s top border and right alignment.\n\nAlso fixes two defects this surfaced:\n\n- Heading letter spacing. Figma''s -2 on Heading 1-4 is a percentage, not\n  pixels — the Heading 4 spec renders as tracking -0.48px at 24px, i.e.\n  -2%. We emitted \"-2px\", about 4x too tight at 24px. Now -0.02em, with a\n  test that rejects a pixel value coming back.\n- D2eIconButton painted a surface and a shadow, because v-btn defaults to\n  the `elevated` variant. The design''s icon buttons have neither.\n\nBREAKING: `status` is now a string union, not an object, and\n`D2eExplorationCardMetadataRow` is renamed `D2eExplorationCardRow`. The\nexploration page on the follow-up branch consumes both.\n\n* fix(ui): only the primary icon button fills when disabled\n\nFigma 2006:843 (ICON BUTTON) disables each category differently:\nprimary fills with Neutral/Lighter, secondary keeps its outline over a\ntransparent surface, and no-stroke stays bare. We painted the grey fill\nbehind all three, so disabled secondary and no-stroke buttons carried a\npill that the design does not have.\n\nVerified in the browser: disabled no-stroke and secondary now compute to\nrgba(0,0,0,0), primary to rgb(222,220,218).\n\nAlso replace the ad-hoc \"states\" story with the category x state grid the\nFigma sheet uses, so the difference is visible.\n\n* fix(ui): size every exploration card toolbar button to the design''s 48px\n\nThe card''s action bar mixed 44px and 48px buttons. When the toolbar\nbuttons were switched to size=\"lg\", the edit only matched tags whose\n`icon=` sat on the same line; prettier had wrapped the rest, so those\nsilently kept the 44px default and rendered a smaller glyph beside their\nneighbours.\n\nFigma''s action bar (1798:192998) is p-12 with a 24px icon, i.e. 48px, for\nevery button. All 17 story buttons now say so.\n\nMeasured after: 5 of 5 at 48x48, radius 100px, bar padding 4px 8px,\njustify flex-end, gap 4px — matching the frame.\n\n* fix(ui): resolve vue and vuetify wherever they install, not app-locally\n\nBoth CI failures on this PR came from one line. The vuetify aliases added\nfor the isolated atlas build hardcoded\n`apps/vue-mri-ui-lib/node_modules/vuetify`, which exists only under\n`npm install --workspaces=false`. The bun workspace install that\n`build_plugins` and `test-mri-frontend` use hoists vuetify to\n`plugins/ui/node_modules`, so both jobs died on the missing path:\n\n  build_plugins:      Could not load .../vue-mri-ui-lib/node_modules/\n                      vuetify/lib/framework.js: ENOENT\n  test-mri-frontend:  Failed to resolve import \"vuetify\" and\n                      \"vuetify/components/VBtn\"\n\nIt passed locally only because this worktree still had an app-local copy\nleft over from running the atlas install by hand.\n\nResolve the real directory with `createRequire(...).resolve()` instead,\nfalling back to the app-local path, so the same config works under both\ninstall shapes. Applied to `vue` as well, which had the same hardcoded\nform. `require.resolve` also returns the realpath, so the existing dedupe\nintent is preserved.\n\nFails loudly with a named error if neither location resolves, rather than\nproducing an ENOENT deep inside rollup.\n\n* refactor(vue-mri): drop the theme class, the app has one theme\n\nThe Atlas theme is gone, so `.theme-d2e` gated the whole palette behind a\nclass that something had to remember to add — and one entry path had\nstopped adding it. `main.ts` called `applyAppTheme()` only in the\nnon-atlas branch, so `VITE_STANDALONE_ATLAS=true` rendered with no theme\nclass at all and every `--color-*` variable resolved to nothing.\n\nMove the palette onto `:root:root`, matching the block already above it\nin the same file and keeping specificity over d4l-ui.css. The class then\nhas no purpose, and neither do the two functions that set it:\n\n- `utils/ThemeManager.ts` was `remove(''theme-atlas'')` + `add(''theme-d2e'')`.\n  The remove guarded a selector that no longer exists anywhere.\n- `bootstrap/themeBootstrap.ts` was a pass-through wrapper whose only\n  other job was importing the stylesheet.\n\nBoth entry points now import the stylesheet directly. `theme-d2e` was not\nused as a scoping selector anywhere, so nothing else changes.\n\nRemoves the bootstrap test with the files: it asserted the class\nbehaviour that no longer exists.\n\nVerified: `.theme-d2e` no longer appears in the built bundle and the\npalette variables still do; all three build variants pass.\n\n* docs(ui): correct the component and theme docs I made stale\n\nThree prop tables and one README section described APIs removed earlier in\nthis branch:\n\n- D2eButton.story.md still listed `icon`. Passing it falls through to\n  v-btn''s own `icon` prop, which makes the button icon-only and drops the\n  label — the exact bug the component was changed to avoid. Replaced with\n  `prependIcon` / `appendIcon` and a warning.\n- D2eDialog.story.md still listed `maxWidth: 600` and a `persistent`\n  prop. 600 is not a design size and `persistent` no longer exists.\n  Replaced with `size` and `closeOnEscape`.\n- vue-mri-ui-lib/README.md still told readers to call\n  `applyTheme(''atlas'')`. Both the function and the Atlas theme are gone.\n\n* ci(ui): run the @d2e/ui library checks\n\nThe library shipped 25 tests, a token-drift guard and the explorer parity\nassertions, and CI ran none of them. `ui-test-vue.yml` filtered on\n`plugins/ui/apps/vue-mri-ui-lib/**` only, so a library-only change did not\neven trigger the workflow.\n\nAdd `plugins/ui/libs/d2e-ui/**` to the filter — the application consumes\nthe library, so either changing should test both — and run the library''s\n`tokens:check` and `test` after the app''s suite, reusing the same\n`bun install`.\n\n`tokens:check` regenerates tokens.css and diffs it against git, so it\ncatches someone editing tokens.ts without regenerating. Verified: exit 1\non that change, exit 0 once restored.\n\n* refactor(ui): rename the mri-* theme keys to brand*\n\nThe shared library carried application-specific naming. `@d2e/ui` is\nmeant to serve the portal once it moves to Vue, and `mri-brand` reads as\nMRI-only to any other consumer.\n\n  mri-brand       -> brand\n  mri-brand-hover -> brand-hover\n  mri-contrast    -> brand-contrast\n  mri-info        -> brand-info\n\nValues are unchanged.\n\nDeliberately **not** renamed to `primary`. The original plan gives two\nconditions for that, and only one is met. The Figma extraction is done,\nbut Bootstrap 4.6.1 is still imported inside `.mri-app-vue-container`\n(styles/style.scss:11), so `primary` would still collide: Bootstrap''s\nscoped `.bg-primary`/`.text-primary` beat Vuetify''s, and Bootstrap 4\ndefines no `--bs-primary-rgb`, so the declaration is invalid at\ncomputed-value time and the button renders transparent. `brand` is\ncollision-free because Bootstrap''s `$theme-colors` has no such entry.\nRename to `primary` once Bootstrap leaves the portal scope.\n\nNothing outside the library consumed these keys — no `color=\"mri-brand\"`\nprops and no `bg-mri-*` utility classes. The `--color-mri-brand` CSS\ncustom property in the application palette is a different namespace and\nis untouched.\n\nVerified in the explorer: primary renders rgb(0, 0, 128), secondary and\nghost keep navy text, danger stays rgb(163, 41, 61).\n\n* feat(ui): build @d2e/ui as a distributable component library\n\nThe portal is moving to Vue and will share these components, so the\nlibrary needs a real contract rather than a source export that every\nconsumer compiles itself.\n\n- Build with vite lib mode into `dist/index.js` + `dist/index.css`, types\n  via `vue-tsc`. Not the rollup/babel chain libs/portal-components uses:\n  that is rollup 2 plus six babel packages for React/TSX, and vite handles\n  Vue SFCs natively.\n- `vue` and `vuetify` stay external as peer dependencies.\n- Components now import the Vuetify pieces they use, so the package works\n  without the consumer running vite-plugin-vuetify.\n- Entry points move to dist; `./tokens.css` stays on source because it is\n  generated from tokens.ts and guarded by tokens:check.\n- `scripts/verify-dist.mjs` checks the artifact in CI.\n\nTwo things this surfaced:\n\nAdding the Vuetify imports broke three unit tests, which imported their\nconstant maps from the `.vue` files and so began loading Vuetify''s CSS\nunder vitest''s node environment. Moved those maps into plain modules\n(`buttonVariants`, `iconButtonSizes`, `statusChipVariants`,\n`explorationCardStatus`), following the existing `dialogSizes.ts`\npattern. The public API is unchanged; tests no longer touch Vuetify.\n\nThe obvious smoke test — importing dist in plain node — cannot work,\nbecause vuetify''s ESM pulls in .css. `verify:dist` checks statically\ninstead, and asserts *positively* that vue and vuetify are still\nimported: when a peer gets bundled it stops appearing as an import, so\nlooking only for unexpected imports misses the case that matters.\nVerified by dropping vuetify from `external` — the check fails on both\nthe missing import and a 197 kB bundle against the 150 kB ceiling.\n\nVerified: 25 lib tests, tokens:check, dist verify, all three vue-mri\nbuild variants, explorer 8 stories / 30 variants, and every component\nstill renders in the browser with no console errors.\n\n* fix(ui): cover every export in the dist guard, and correct the README\n\n`verify-dist.mjs` checked 13 names while `src/index.ts` exports 17 values. The\ncheck is a subset test, so the four constant maps this branch added —\nVARIANT_MAP, SIZE_MAP, STATUS_CHIP_VARIANT_MAP and ICON_BUTTON_SIZE_MAP — went\nunguarded. Dropping or renaming any of them would not have failed the build.\nThe guard now reports 17 exports.\n\nThe README header still said the application uses the source and there is no\nbuild step, directly above the new section on consuming the built package.\nSay what is true of both: the application reads source through vite aliases,\nand every other consumer uses the artifact.\n\nFound in review of #3251.\n\n* fix(ui): close #3204''s remaining Copilot review gaps\n\n- D2eDialog: card is now a flex column with a capped max-height and a\n  scrollable body, so a long form or short viewport keeps the header/\n  actions visible instead of clipping content.\n- D2eTextField: disable attribute inheritance so a caller''s listeners\n  (blur, click, ...) aren''t applied twice — once via forwardAttrs, once\n  via Vue''s default inheritance onto the same root.\n- D2eIconButton: require icon and ariaLabel. There''s no content slot, so\n  a call missing either produced a blank, unlabeled control.\n- D2eMenu: implement the roving-tabindex ARIA menu keyboard model\n  (Arrow Up/Down, Home/End) the role=\"menu\"/\"menuitem\" markup already\n  implied but didn''t back.\n- D2eExplorationCard: derive the checkbox''s default accessible name from\n  the exploration name instead of a shared \"Select exploration\" label.\n\nThe other six comments on that review were already resolved by later\ncommits on this branch (main.ts''s theme class was removed outright, the\ntwo story docs and explorer/.gitignore''s lockfile were fixed in\n87be952db and 10aaf0a9b, and D2eExplorationCard''s truncation/tooltip and\n\"By:\" prefix were fixed rebuilding it against the Figma design). Left\nthe missing D2eDialog behavior tests out — the fix would require\nmounting the component in vitest, which the repo''s testing policy rules\nout; that belongs in Playwright once the dialog is wired into an app.\n\n* refactor(ui): one source of truth for CSS design values, and no Bootstrap (#3253)\n\n* fix(vue-mri): define the colour properties that nothing defined\n\nEight `var(--color-…)` sites named a property that no stylesheet defines and\ngave no fallback. Each produced an invalid declaration, so the element\ninherited its colour instead. Error states rendered as normal text.\n\n`d4l-ui.css` supplies `--color-feedback-success` and `--color-feedback-alarm`\nbut no `-error`, and no `--color-text-primary`. Define both in `_main.scss`.\n\n`--color-feedback-error` takes `#a3293d`, the value the nine ShinyViewer sites\nalready carry as their fallback, so their rendering does not change. It is not\nrenamed to `--color-feedback-alarm`: that name holds d4l''s `#d53939`, is live\nin `DownloadMenu.vue`, and renaming would have flipped those nine working\nsites to the wrong red.\n\n`--color-text-primary` takes `#000080`, matching the fallback `_main.scss`\nalready uses for it.\n\nAlso drop the `color` declaration on the Execute side panel card title. It\nnamed `--color-support-soft-red`, which d4l does not define; the heading has\nalways inherited, and a red card title is not intended.\n\nEleven undefined names remain. Every one is used only with a fallback.\n\n* refactor(vue-mri): replace Bootstrap 4 with a scoped shim\n\nBootstrap 4.6.1 no longer compiles into the portal scope. `_bootstrap-shim.scss`\nreproduces what the app actually used: the reboot, the 16 utility and grid\nclasses that had no app rule of their own, and the base for the `.btn`,\n`.form-control`, `.card`, `.nav` and `.modal-*` families that app rules layer\non top. Values are taken from the app''s own Bootstrap build, not from the\ndefault one: the app overrode $font-size-base to 0.875rem after Bootstrap had\nalready bound $input-btn-font-size to 1rem, so the shim keeps 1rem there.\n\n`.text-primary` and `.bg-primary` are deliberately absent. They were the reason\n`@d2e/ui` carries a `brand` theme key: Bootstrap''s copies are scoped, carry\n!important and define no --bs-primary-rgb, so they beat Vuetify''s and render\ntransparent. `style.scss` no longer needs its .text-primary workaround, and the\nrename to `primary` is now unblocked.\n\n`_mri-bootstrap-variables.scss` becomes `_app-variables.scss`, 520 declarations\ndown to the ~20 the app reads plus their transitive dependencies. $primary and\n$blue (#007bff) are gone; nothing read them and they contradicted\n--color-primary.\n\nThe first shim draft dropped 50 element rules from the reboot. Screenshot\ndiffing found three panels had grown 4-12px; svg and img had lost\n`vertical-align: middle`, so every icon added its descender gap back into the\nrow height. The reboot is now complete except for print styles.\n\nVerified: app, atlas and atlas-app builds pass; 906 unit tests pass, with the\napp-segmented-button failure that is local-only. Visual re-verification against\nthe pre-change screenshots is still outstanding.\n\n* fix(vue-mri): match the shim to what the app''s Bootstrap build emitted\n\nThe shim was transcribed from `mri-bootstrap.scss` compiled on its own, which\nis not what the app shipped. `style.scss` does\n`@use ''./mri-bootstrap-variables'' as *` before it imports Bootstrap, so\n$font-size-base is already 0.875rem when Bootstrap evaluates\n`$input-btn-font-size: $font-size-base !default`. Five rules were one type\nstep too large:\n\n  .form-control      1rem      -> 0.875rem\n  .btn               1rem      -> 0.875rem\n  .form-control-sm   0.875rem  -> 0.765625rem\n  .btn-sm            0.875rem  -> 0.765625rem\n  .col-form-label-sm 0.875rem  -> 0.765625rem\n\nThat was the whole height regression: each text row rendered ~2px taller\nagainst a fixed control height, accumulating down a panel. The earlier\nsuspicion that `.col-form-label` was mis-padded was wrong; `.col-form-label-sm`\nwins on those labels and its calc(0.1rem + 1px) is the 2.6px observed.\n\nA full rule-by-rule diff against the original then found more gaps: `.container`\nwas absent entirely, along with `[hidden]`, the checkbox/radio box-sizing, the\nnumber-input spinners, `[type=search]`, `[role=button]`, `abbr[title]`, the\ncode/kbd/mark typography, `.card > hr`, `.form-control::-ms-expand`, and the\n`textarea`/`select` escapes from .form-control''s fixed height.\n\nAlso restores the `is-invalid` error icon (background-image plus the\npadding-right that reserves room for it), narrows `.is-invalid ~\n.invalid-feedback` to Bootstrap''s `.form-control.is-invalid ~`, and adds the\nprefers-reduced-motion guards for .form-control, .btn and .spinner-border.\n\nThe shim now differs from the original in five places, all deliberate:\nhtml/body (style.scss owns the container), two @media print borders, and\n`0rem` vs `0` on .modal-header.\n\nVerified: five component screenshots are pixel-identical to the pre-removal\nbaseline (RMSE 0), including the three that had grown. The two remaining\nnon-zero diffs are test-data drift, not CSS - the cohort under test moved from\nversion 1 to 2 with a new filter; the dialog itself matches exactly. App,\natlas and atlas-app builds pass; 906 unit tests pass.\n\n* refactor(ui): fold the brand theme key back into primary\n\n`brand` existed only because Bootstrap 4 was in the portal scope: its scoped\n`.bg-primary`/`.text-primary` carry !important and define no --bs-primary-rgb,\nso they beat Vuetify''s utilities and rendered transparent. Bootstrap''s\n$theme-colors had no `brand` entry, so the duplicate could not collide. The\nshim does not emit those utilities, so the collision is gone.\n\n`brand` and `brand-contrast` were exact duplicates of the existing `primary`\nkey (#000080), so they are deleted rather than renamed. `brand-hover` and\n`brand-info` keep their values as `primary-hover` and `primary-info`.\nD2eButton''s primary, secondary and ghost variants now use `primary`.\n\nVerified in the running app: inside .mri-app-vue-container both .bg-primary\nand .text-primary resolve to rgb(0, 0, 128), and only Vuetify''s rules apply.\ntokens:check clean, 25 library tests, verify:dist reports 17 exports, app and\natlas builds pass, 906 app tests pass.\n\n* refactor(vue-mri): point the colour palette at the design tokens\n\n`_main.scss` becomes an alias layer. Consumers keep their names; only the\ndefinitions change, so a regression is attributable to one line.\n\nOf the 105 properties it defined, 14 were consumed by nothing and are deleted.\nEight of those held values with no design token, which is why the unmappable\ngroup is 40 and not 48. Verified safe: no property name is built dynamically\nanywhere in the tree, none of the 14 appears elsewhere in plugins/ui, and the\nremoval cascade is empty.\n\nTwo more are gone as names. `--color-primary` and `--color-text-primary` were\nsynonyms for a token, not semantic names, and `--color-primary` was a name d4l\nalso defines, so all 126 call sites now read `var(--d2e-color-primary,\n#000080)` directly. Four fallback variants existed and three were wrong -\n#1f425a, #6c757d, #545b62 and #007bff, Bootstrap greys and blue that would have\nrendered if tokens.css ever failed to load. All are normalised.\n\nThe other 47 keep their names as aliases. Only 2 of the 49 token-resolving\nnames were primitive synonyms; the remaining 47 are semantic and carry 431 call\nsites, so rewriting them would collapse intent into primitives -\n--color-footer-button-text-light would become indistinguishable from sixty\nother whites.\n\nOf the 89 that survive: 29 alias directly, 18 are indirect, 2 are not colours,\nand 40 are quarantined under a banner. Those 40 have no equivalent in the\ndesign system - a legacy family of mid blues and teals up to delta 117 from the\nnearest token. They are not snapped and not imported into @d2e/ui; either would\nbe a visible recolour that needs design input.\n\nThen adds the 38 names d4l-ui.css also defines, so our stylesheets depend on\nour tokens rather than on a vendor file sharing our namespace. d4l keeps its\nown copies for its shadow-DOM components. Every consumed property without a\nfallback is now defined by us.\n\nVerified: dimensions unchanged on all five component screenshots; RMSE is\n~0.001, the 15 deliberate sub-perceptual snaps where a value sat within delta\n12 of its token. App and atlas builds pass, 906 unit tests pass.\n\n* docs(vue-mri): record why the shim drops Bootstrap''s print block\n\nEvery other omission in the shim is justified inline; this one was not.\nNothing calls window.print() and no d-print-* class is used, so it only\naffects a manual Ctrl+P.\n\nFound in review of #3253.\n\n* docs(vue-mri): note the deferred btn-primary/secondary/link colour finding\n\nPre-existing and left alone in this PR because fixing it recolours a shipping\nbutton. Recorded at the rule so it is not rediscovered from scratch.\n\nFound in review of #3253.\n\n* fix(vue-mri): correct five shim rules that diverged from the Bootstrap build\n\nFound by compiling style.scss on both branches and diffing rule-by-rule. The\nscreenshot comparison did not cover any of these.\n\nThe important one is new behaviour, not a missing rule. The shim carried\n`.form-control.is-invalid ~ .invalid-feedback { display: block }`, but\nBootstrap''s validation mixin interpolates `&`, so nested inside\n.mri-app-vue-container it compiled to `.mri-app-vue-container.is-invalid ~\n.invalid-feedback` - a compound selector that never matched. The rule was dead,\nand the app depends on that: FiltersFooter and QueryFilterModern each place\nseveral .invalid-feedback siblings after one input and reveal the right one\nwith an inline `display: block`. Live, the rule shows all of them at once, so\nan invalid cohort name rendered \"invalid name\", \"must not exceed 255\ncharacters\" and \"empty name\" together. It is now documented as deliberately\nabsent.\n\nFour rules were genuinely missing:\n\n- `select.form-control.is-invalid` and `textarea.form-control.is-invalid`\n  reposition the error icon. Without them the year pickers in\n  CompleteRequiredFiltersModal put the icon under the native dropdown arrow.\n- `[tabindex=\"-1\"]:focus:not(:focus-visible) { outline: 0 !important }`.\n  Without it ResizeObserver, bs-dropdown-item, app-tab, app-segmented-button\n  and Drawer paint a focus ring on programmatic or mouse focus.\n- `appearance: none` on date, time, month and datetime-local `.form-control`.\n  Without it the native control ignores the fixed height on iOS Safari.\n- The `:active:focus` box-shadow on the button variants, so they keep a focus\n  ring while held down.\n\nEach value is taken from the original compiled output and verified against it.\n\nFound in review of #3253.\n\n* feat(ui): rebuild the dialogs on the d2e component library (#3259)\n\n* feat(vue-mri): reskin the rename and delete dialogs (#3122, #3124)\n\n(cherry picked from commit 56c4facdfecb565007f514581c9fbdbb24b2413d)\n\n* feat(vue-mri): reskin the materialize dialog and drop the prop-watcher (#3118)\n\n(cherry picked from commit 0e71bd0fd1b5c71cc6a92204fcea51158ac9d21b)\n\n* refactor(vue-mri): rebuild UnsavedChangesDialog on D2eDialog\n\n(cherry picked from commit 67b5ebbcf4a655b78ed95968b37ad9d19a7f14c4)\n\n* style(vue-mri): format the dialog files with prettier\n\nApplication half of the original formatting commit. The library half is\nin the component-library branch.\n\n* fix(vue-mri): stop the UA input border striking through Vuetify field labels\n\n`vuetify-settings.scss` sets `$reset: false`, so Vuetify''s reset never runs.\nThat reset is what removes the user-agent border from form controls\n(`button, input, select, textarea { background-color: transparent;\nborder-style: none }`). Without it, `.v-field__input` keeps the browser''s\n2px inset grey border across the full width of the field, and an outlined\nfield''s floating label sits on that line — so the label renders struck\nthrough.\n\nVuetify''s own outline was correct throughout: the `start` and `end` segments\ncarry the navy border and the `notch` is at 0, so the gap for the label was\nopen. The grey line came from the raw input underneath.\n\nReproduce only that one rule, scoped to `.v-field`, so the app''s own\nBootstrap-style inputs keep their borders. Enabling the full Vuetify reset\nwould restyle the whole application.\n\nFound in manual verification. This is why the field renders correctly in\nHistoire, which loads Vuetify''s styles normally, and not in the app.\n\n* fix(ui): remove the dead space Vuetify components inherit from the app\n\nFour separate leaks put roughly 118px of unwanted space into every dialog.\nNone of them were design values; D2eDialog''s Figma padding is untouched.\n\n1. D2eTextField never set `hide-details`, so Vuetify reserved its 22px message\n   slot permanently. It now defaults to \"auto\", which reserves the space only\n   when there is a message. Errors still show.\n\n2. The shim''s `label` rule reached Vuetify''s field label. The notch label is\n   `position: static`, so Bootstrap''s 0.5rem added real height inside the\n   border gap. Scoped to `label:not(.v-label)`.\n\n3. The shim''s `hr` rule reached VDivider, which renders an <hr>. Bootstrap''s\n   1rem margins added 32px per divider, and a dialog has two. Scoped to\n   `hr:not(.v-divider)`.\n\n4. With those margins gone the browser''s own 0.5em <hr> margin took over,\n   because vuetify-settings.scss sets `$reset: false` and Vuetify''s reset is\n   what would normally zero it. `.v-divider { margin: 0 }` in the app scope.\n\nItems 2 and 3 are the same class of bug as the input border fixed in\n072cd4383: the shim faithfully reproduces Bootstrap''s element-level reboot,\nand Vuetify builds its components out of those same bare elements. Being\nfaithful to Bootstrap is the wrong goal wherever Vuetify now renders. The shim\nstyles twelve such elements; `button` is the next one worth checking, since\n`.mri-app-vue-container button` outranks `.v-btn`.\n\nRename dialog measured before and after: height 343 -> 238px, gap above the\nfield 70 -> 38px, below 57 -> 25px, field 52 -> 48px.\n\n25 library tests, verify:dist 17 exports, 906 app tests, atlas builds pass.\n\n* feat(vue-mri): rebuild the save-current-filters dialog on D2eDialog\n\nFound during manual verification: this dialog was never migrated. Its body was\nraw Bootstrap markup - form-group, row, col-sm-12, col-form-label,\nform-control, is-invalid - with three invalid-feedback divs toggled by inline\n`display: block` styles.\n\nNow D2eDialog + D2eTextField + D2eButton, matching the other four dialogs. The\nthree error strings fold into a `cohortNameErrors` computed feeding\n`error-messages`, so Vuetify owns their display and the field no longer needs\nthe is-invalid class.\n\nNote this is not the last one. A sweep found 16 more active messageBox dialogs\noutside the deprecated query-filter tree, including the reset-filters dialog in\nthis same file. They are listed with a suggested clustering in\ndocs/projects/vue-mri-ui/pr2/06-remaining-dialog-migration.md.\n\n* feat(vue-mri): port the reset-filters dialog and tighten the dialog body\n\nThree changes from manual verification.\n\nThe save-current-filters dialog loses its hint line. It told the user to enter\na name, which the empty-name validation already covers.\n\nThe reset-filters dialog moves to D2eDialog + D2eButton. It was the immediate\nneighbour of the one migrated in 7f57070aa and looked out of place beside it.\nIts old 400px width goes; it now uses the Modal/S default like the other\nconfirm dialogs. `messageBox` is no longer used in FiltersFooter, so the import\nand registration are gone too.\n\nD2eDialog''s body now collapses its last child''s bottom margin. A <p> in the\nbody carries a 1rem margin from the Bootstrap shim, which stacked on the body''s\n24px padding and put 40px above the divider. Collapsing the last child is\nbetter than dropping the padding: a body ending in a field has no margin of its\nown and still needs the 24px.\n\nThat is the fourth place the shim''s element-level reboot has leaked into\ncomponent markup, after input, label and hr.\n\n25 library tests, verify:dist 17 exports, 906 app tests, app build pass.\n\n* feat(vue-mri): rebuild the CSV download dialog on D2eDialog\n\nSeventh dialog migrated. The parent gates it with `v-if=\"csvShow\"`, so it is\nalways open when mounted and takes `:model-value=\"true\"`.\n\nDrops the inline `style=\"padding: 24px\"` that compensated for MessageBox\nhaving no body padding; D2eDialog supplies it. Buttons are reordered to\nCancel then Download, matching the other migrated dialogs.\n\n`LoadingAnimation` was imported and registered but never used in the template;\nit goes with `messageBox` and `appButton`.\n\n* fix(vue-mri): restore Enter-to-confirm and tidy the migrated dialogs\n\nTwo functional regressions from the migration, both mine.\n\n`v-focus` was replaced with the plain `autofocus` attribute on the CSV\ndownload and reset-filters confirm buttons. D2eButton declares no `autofocus`\nprop, so it fell through to the <button> as a raw attribute - and the HTML\nautofocus flush runs once per document, so it is inert for an element inserted\nlater. VDialog then focused its content wrapper instead, and pressing Enter did\nnothing. Both are back on `v-focus`, which calls el.focus() on mount. The text\nfields were never affected: VTextField declares `autofocus` and focuses\nimperatively.\n\nAddCohort''s Atlas branch still said \"Click OK to materialize this cohort\" after\nthe button was relabelled to Materialize, and the string was hardcoded English\nin a file where everything else is translated. It is now\nMRI_PA_COLL_CONFIRM_MATERIALIZE, added to all three locales. The dialog title\nalso regains the bookmark name, which the old header carried and the new one\ndropped - with several saved filters listed, there was nothing on screen saying\nwhich one was being materialized.\n\nBookmarks.renameErrorMessages returned on the first match, so a name that was\nboth a duplicate and too long showed only the duplicate error while the Rename\nbutton was disabled on length, leaving the button dead with no explanation. It\nnow accumulates, matching FiltersFooter.cohortNameErrors.\n\nD2eDialog''s `> :last-child` margin collapse excluded the busy overlay, which\nbecomes the last child whenever `busy` is true and handed the margin back\nmid-operation. The nested rule also moved below the declarations to clear Dart\nSass''s mixed-decls deprecation.\n\nUnsavedChangesDialog now emits `update:modelValue` alongside `stay`, so v-model\nis no longer write-only for a consumer that does not wire the `stay` handler.\n\nFound in review of #3259.\n\n* fix(ui): collapse the duplicate Vue install that breaks slot rendering\n\nplugins/ui installed two copies of Vue. vue-mri pinned \"vue\": \"3.5.17\"\nexactly, while apps/jobs and libs/d2e-ui resolved to 3.5.22, so bun\nhoisted 3.5.22 and nested 3.5.17 under the app.\n\nvite.config.ts aliases \"vue\" to the app copy, so every transformed\nmodule used 3.5.17. @vue/test-utils ships CommonJS, so its own\nrequire(\"vue\") bypassed the alias and mount() rendered with 3.5.22.\nThe two halves then disagreed: renderSlot read a\ncurrentRenderingInstance that the other runtime had set, found null,\nand failed with \"Cannot read properties of null (reading ''ce'')\". Any\nSFC that declares <slot> crashed. UnsavedChangesDialog is the first\nsuch component under test, so the fault surfaced here.\n\nRelax the vue-mri pin so bun hoists one copy, and add a workspace\noverride so that copy stays on 3.5.17. No app changes Vue version.\n\nThe split also masked a wrong assertion in app-segmented-button:\nprop reactivity did not reach the renderer, so the test asserted that\na newly selected item stays unselected. Correct it.\n\nAdd a guard to vitest.setup.ts. It compares the vue that the app\nresolves with the vue that @vue/test-utils resolves, and fails with a\nnamed error if they diverge again.\n\n* feat(vue-mri): Data Exploration page (#3116) (#3262)\n\n* feat(portal): make researcher plugin app ids route-aware\n\n(cherry picked from commit 7af376f251d8b5458d7ce7c829724bc2d07369e2)\n\n* feat(ui): register the exploration plugin route\n\n(cherry picked from commit 14fc760b2c6a65ff598a8b08b92ea2e5681452e7)\n\n* feat(vue-mri): add the exploration page shell and navigation view\n\n(cherry picked from commit 4c95249add0688260ca9192744f4a18a564f87a7)\n\n* fix(vue-mri): complete initial load on the exploration view\n\n(cherry picked from commit c9bf0c638dbb77f4b69769b697a2532192ced886)\n\n* refactor(vue-mri): drop the exploration route plumbing\n\nThe exploration page is the main view of vue-mri, reached in place, not a\nsecond single-spa route. Remove the second uiplugin entry, the route-aware\nresearcher app ids, the view prop and its plumbing, and the App.vue switch.\n\nResearcherStudyPluginRenderer.tsx and plugins/ui/package.json now match\norigin/develop again.\n\n* feat(vue-mri): mount the exploration page in place of the bookmarks list\n\nHoist the exploration view out of the splitter in PatientAnalytics, gated on\ndisplayCohorts, and drop the <bookmarks> block it replaces. The first nav tab\nstill calls toggleCohorts(true), which now returns to the page.\n\nCarry over the behaviour that lived in Bookmarks.vue:\n\n- the ?bmkId= deep-link restore, as a watch on querystring.bmkId\n- loading a bookmark on card click, behind the unsaved-changes guard, then\n  swapping to the splitter view\n\nFollow Bookmarks.vue in the page itself: source the username through\nusePortalContext, drop the completeInitialLoad dispatch and the on-mount load\nnow that PatientAnalytics owns both, and build the six metadata rows the\ndesign asks for. Unmaterialised rows show a dash instead of disappearing.\n\nAlso remove the debug logging from BookmarkItems.vue.\n\n* feat(ui): add D2eCheckbox, D2eSelect and an anchored D2eMenu\n\nThree form primitives the exploration toolbar and card need. D2eMenu was a\nstatic button list with no trigger or open/close logic; it now takes an\nactivator slot, anchors through VMenu, and navigates with the arrow keys.\n\nEach ships with a Histoire story and a unit test over its constant map, and\ntakes every colour from a --d2e-* token.\n\n* feat(vue-mri): build out the exploration toolbar, card and actions\n\nCloses the rest of #3116 on the exploration page.\n\nToolbar: scored search (id 100, name 50, description 25, author 10) lifted out\nof BookmarkItems.vue into a pure, tested helper; a Sort by menu offering Last\nupdated and Name A-Z/Z-A; the data source styled as a disabled D2eSelect; and\na working \"Start new exploration\".\n\nCards: person count, the three materialisation rows and the Exploration\nbookmark panel, with an id row that reads Cohort ID for Atlas records. A\nnever-materialised card shows a Materialize action in place of the count.\n\nActions: Materialize and a More menu carrying Rename and Delete, gated on\nownership and on whether the dataset can materialise cohorts. Rename and\nDelete are extracted from Bookmarks.vue into their own components so the card\nhas an entry point for #3122 and #3124.\n\nEvery visible string resolves through i18n; the de and zh strings need native\nreview.\n\n* fix(vue-mri): correct the exploration card and page against the Figma frame\n\nCard, from frame 1798:192269:\n- Add the status chip. \"Ready\" and \"Not run yet\" are derivable from the\n  bookmark-to-cohort link; \"stale\" is not, so it is never produced (#3117).\n- Cards fill their grid cell instead of sitting at a fixed 324px, and take a\n  hover state and a pointer cursor so it reads as clickable.\n- The lead Materialize is an outlined button with a leading icon, per the\n  not-run variant.\n\nFixes:\n- \"Start new exploration\" was dead: PatientAnalytics does not map\n  getBookmarks, so checkCohortName threw on an undefined list.\n- Materialize opened the exploration instead of the dialog. Its click bubbled\n  from the lead row to the card root, which was not in the ignore list.\n- Closing the materialize dialog no longer reloads the list. AddCohort already\n  reloads on success, so the close handler was a duplicate.\n- Drop the refresh button; it is not in the frame.\n\nAdd the data quality, filter summary and analyze icons as inert placeholders\nso the action bar matches the frame. They belong to #3119, #3120 and #3121.\n\n* fix(vue-mri): match the exploration page container, icons and id row\n\n- Wrap the page in the tinted surface plus one rounded white card, inset 24px\n  (Figma 1676:221311). The card was previously invisible against a white page.\n- Close the breadcrumb with the 24x2 secondary rule, and drop the breadcrumb to\n  10px Medium with 1px tracking (Figma 1676:221313).\n- Lay the grid out as fixed 324px columns rather than flexible ones; the frame\n  is 1344 = 4x324 + 3x16. Toolbar right group closes to an 8px gap.\n- The id row shows the materialised cohort''s id, so a card that has never been\n  materialised now reads \"-\" instead of repeating the bookmark id.\n- Replace the guessed MDI glyphs with the icons exported from action bar\n  1798:192998, rendered through a new slot on D2eIconButton and D2eButton.\n\nAnalyze keeps an MDI glyph: Figma''s export for that one instance returns a\nstale layer named \"Bell\" whose geometry is a bell, while the rendered node is a\nchart line. The reason is recorded on the component.\n\n* fix(vue-mri): polish the exploration toolbar, card chrome and more menu\n\n- Search: the field owns the 16px inset and the icon an 8px end margin, so the\n  magnifier no longer reads as a second, empty prepend slot.\n- Sort by is a real text button with a 22px prepended sort icon exported from\n  Figma 2634:58663, which also gives it padding away from the primary button.\n- Card lead row gains a bottom margin, and D2eStatusChip gains the 8px\n  horizontal padding the frame specifies.\n- Card Materialize outlines in Primary/Lightest (Figma 1798:192920), not the\n  default primary.\n- Quick-action tooltips are white with neutral 12px text (Figma 1798:208323).\n  The rule is unscoped because Vuetify teleports tooltip content to body.\n- More menu follows Figma 1801:215921: 44px rows, 16px labels, leading icons,\n  Delete in the alarm colour through a new `danger` flag on D2eMenuItem, and\n  Duplicate present but disabled until #3123''s backend command exists.\n\n* fix(vue-mri): tooltip the More button, colour menu icons, tidy the data source\n\n- The More (⋮) button gains the tooltip its four neighbours already had.\n- Menu icons take the row''s colour, so Rename reads primary, Delete alarm and\n  a disabled row neutral (Figma 1801:215921).\n- The data source label was clipped because Figma''s 12px line-height at a 12px\n  font size cuts the glyph box; the line box may now grow. The read-only field\n  also keeps full contrast and drops the empty details row that rendered as a\n  stray rule beneath it.\n- Card title and every metadata value now carry a tooltip only while the text\n  is actually truncated, per the note on frame 2635:208762. The overflow test\n  is a pure function with its own unit test.\n\n* fix(vue-mri): close the defects found in code review\n\nGuards restored from Bookmarks.vue:\n- Rename was offered on Atlas records, where the D2E branch dereferences a null\n  bookmark and throws into a silent catch. Gate it on the bookmark type as well\n  as ownership.\n- Reopening the exploration that is already active re-loaded it, discarding an\n  in-progress edit and prompting for unsaved changes on a no-op. Short-circuit\n  to the splitter view instead.\n- A bookmark incompatible with the active config failed into an empty catch, so\n  the click looked dead. Surface it as an alert, as the message box used to.\n- Delete reset the filters but not the chart properties, so a deleted\n  exploration''s axes and display mode leaked into the empty state. Use the\n  resetChart action, which dispatches both.\n\nData correctness:\n- Materialize is hidden for a record with neither a bookmark nor an Atlas\n  definition; it was building a generate URL containing \"null\".\n- Card keys are namespaced by source table. A bookmark id and a cohort id can\n  collide, and one checkbox then selected two cards.\n- AddCohort was passed `bookmark.bookmarkname`, which formatBookmark never\n  sets; the field is `name`.\n\nAlso: only the lead row''s button swallows the card click, not the person count\nand status chip beside it; only a card that opens looks clickable; a clickable\ncard is reachable by keyboard; and the dialogs no longer trigger a second list\nreload on top of their own.\n\n* chore(ui): pin vue to 3.5.22\n\nReview asked for an exact pin in both plugins/ui/package.json and\nplugins/ui/apps/vue-mri-ui-lib/package.json, per the decision taken in\nthe workshop.\n\nThe application dependency was a caret range, \"^3.5.17\", so an install\non a new machine or a later date could resolve a different patch from\nthe one the root override names. That is the same class of drift this\nbranch already fixed once: a second Vue copy in the graph breaks slot\nrendering, and the symptom appears far from the cause. An exact version\nin both places means the override and the dependency cannot disagree.\n\nThe component explorer stays on 3.5.26. It is outside the bun workspace\nbecause Histoire needs a different Vite, and explorer-parity.test.ts\ncompares the Vue *minor*, not the patch, so 3.5 on both sides keeps that\nguard satisfied.\n\nVerified: one vue in the app''s resolution path at 3.5.22; 1083 vue-mri\ntests pass; the d2e-ui suite, including the parity guard, passes; all\nfour builds pass.\n\nThe nested vue 3.2.0 under gethue is untouched. It is a transitive\ndependency isolated in its own node_modules and never reaches the app.\n\n* feat(vue-mri): hide the Data quality action until it does something\n\nThe button rendered on every exploration card so the action bar matched\nthe frame, but clicking it did nothing: the data quality page belongs to\nanother plugin and wiring it up is #3119. A control that looks live and\nis inert reads as a broken feature, which is worse than not offering it\nyet.\n\nHidden behind a SHOW_DATA_QUALITY constant rather than deleted. The icon,\nthe label key, the test id and the render loop all stay, so bringing it\nback for the next release is a one line change and not a rebuild.\n\nThe loop is left in place too, over an empty list, so a future action can\nbe added without restoring markup.\n\nVerified against a running stack rather than assumed: no\nexplorations-dq-btn renders, while materialize, filter summary, analyze\nand the More menu still render on all twelve cards. 1191 unit tests pass\nand the portal build passes.\n\nExplorationsPage.vue does not satisfy prettier, and did not before this\nchange either, so it is left as it is rather than reformatted into an\nunrelated diff.\n\n* test(e2e): enter the cohort builder through the redesigned page (#3348)\n\n* test(e2e): enter the cohort builder through the redesigned page\n\nThe suite entered the cohort builder by clicking a button labelled\n\"D2E\" (MRI_PA_CREATE_D2E_COHORT_TEXT) in the old Bookmarks header. The\nData Exploration redesign replaced that page, and the button with it, so\nthe click timed out after 20 seconds.\n\nThis is not a screenshot mismatch. The element does not exist, the test\nnever reached its assertions, and with maxFailures at 1 in CI that single\ntimeout stopped the other 68 tests from running at all.\n\n25 call sites across 19 files. A test id rather than the new label, so it\nsurvives copy changes and does not depend on the run''s locale.\n\n* test(e2e): drop the Atlas button assertion, which has no equivalent\n\nThe old Bookmarks header carried a D2E / Atlas / Import / Compare button\ngroup. The redesign has a single \"Start new exploration\" action, so the\ncheck that the Atlas cohort-definition button is visible has no control\nleft to point at, in any state.\n\nRather than assert something weaker that would pass for the wrong\nreason, this step now asserts what it is really there for: that turning\nPA-Atlas on leaves the Cohorts screen reachable and rendering.\n\nThe missing Atlas entry point is a question for review, not a test fix.\nNothing in the redesign notes records dropping the Atlas create and\nimport actions. If they are meant to survive they need a home on the new\npage, and this assertion should come back.\n\n* test(e2e): select cohorts by checkbox before comparing\n\nBoth specs run the same \"select two cohorts, then Compare\" flow, and\nboth break on the selection. The bulk-actions bar keeps the ''Compare''\nlabel, so those assertions are untouched.\n\n- e2e_PA_and_cohorts used `pa-cohort-card-*` and `pa-cohort-select-btn`.\n  Those ids exist only in BookmarkItems.vue, which is imported only by\n  Bookmarks.vue, which the redesign no longer mounts. They are absent\n  from the built bundle - the component is tree-shaken out - so they\n  could never match.\n- patient-group_comparison clicked an svg inside each card''s `.footer`.\n  That structure is gone.\n\nBoth now check the card''s own checkbox, which carries the accessible\nname \"Select exploration <name>\". Naming the cohort also fixes a latent\nweakness: the list sorts by last updated, so nth-child(1) and (2) were\nnever guaranteed to be the two cohorts the test had just created.\n\nFound by auditing selectors against the current UI, not by CI - CI stops\nat the first failure, so it would have taken two more 40-minute cycles\nto surface these. Verified against a running stack: the selector checks\ntwo cards, raises the bulk bar and leaves Compare enabled.\n\n* test(e2e): refresh the 01-example baseline for the redesigned page\n\nWith the selector fixed the test reached its screenshot, which then\nfailed on 12,566 pixels, 2% of the image. Two real changes, both\nexpected from this stack and both confirmed by eye against the expected\nimage CI uploaded:\n\n- The builder tab reads \"New exploration\" where it read \"New cohort\".\n- Filter-panel fields sit a few pixels lower, about 24px by the\n  INCLUSION/Exclusion tabs, from the design-token spacing.\n\nNothing else moved. The chart, the toolbar and the 1,321 / 2,694 count\nare identical, with no overlap, clipping or missing control - so this is\nthe baseline moving, not a regression.\n\nThe replacement is the PNG CI itself rendered, taken from the failing\nrun''s error-context artifact. A macOS run writes example-1-darwin.png,\nwhich CI never reads.\n\nCI retried, so the run carried two attempts. They differ by 3 pixels at\na maximum channel delta of 1 - antialiasing noise, inside Playwright''s\nthreshold - which is the evidence that one committed baseline holds\nacross runs.\n\n* test(e2e): a supported way to refresh screenshot baselines on Linux\n\nBaselines are committed per platform and CI runs Linux, so the files are\n`*-linux.png`. A run on macOS writes `*-darwin.png`, which CI never\nreads. There was no documented way to regenerate the Linux ones, so a\nbaseline that legitimately moved had no route back to green.\n\n`container` builds the image CI builds and re-renders against the local\nstack. One trick worth recording: the stack answers TLS only for SNI\n`localhost`, so dialling the caddy container by name returns a TLS\ninternal error rather than a certificate warning that ignoreHTTPSErrors\nwould absorb. The script forwards localhost:41100 inside the container\ninstead.\n\n`from-ci` takes the screenshots CI actually rendered, from the artifact\nthe workflow already uploads. This is the faithful option and the only\npractical one on Apple Silicon, where container mode runs amd64 Chromium\nunder emulation - a 24 second test had not finished after ten minutes.\n\nBoth modes tell the reader to open every changed PNG before committing,\nbecause --update-snapshots records a regression as happily as a fix.\n\n* test(e2e): assert the redesigned Cohorts toolbar on page load\n\nCI confirmed this one. cohortPageLoad is a smoke test that the Cohorts\nscreen renders its primary controls, and every control it asserted came\nfrom the old Bookmarks header: the ''Create Cohort:'' title and a\nD2E / Import / Shared / Compare button group.\n\nIt now asserts the toolbar the redesign puts there - search, filters,\nsort, new exploration and the data source select - plus the page root.\n\nThree of the old assertions have no replacement, which is recorded in\nthe test rather than quietly dropped:\n\n- ''Shared'', the show-shared-cohorts toggle, has no equivalent.\n- ''Import'', for an Atlas cohort definition, has no entry point on the\n  new page. That is the same open question atlas_cohort_definition.spec\n  raises, not something this test can asserted around.\n- ''Compare'' moved into the bulk-actions bar, which appears only once a\n  card is selected, so it is no longer a page-load control.\n\nVerified against a running stack: all six locators resolve on load.\n\n* test(e2e): act on exploration cards by name, not by icon position\n\nThe last of the suite''s dependencies on the old Bookmarks card, fixed in\none pass rather than one CI cycle at a time.\n\nEach old card carried five unlabelled icons and tests reached them\npositionally - `.footer > div:nth-child(2) > svg` for rename,\n`nth-child(5)` for delete. That markup is gone. It was fragile on its own\nterms too: the position encoded the action, so inserting an icon would\nsilently repoint a test at a different one, and `.first()` meant several\n\"delete this cohort\" steps actually deleted whichever card sorted first.\n\nAdd tests/explorations.ts and name the action instead of counting\nsiblings: explorationCard, selectExploration, explorationAction,\nexplorationMenuAction, confirmExplorationDialog, deleteExploration.\n\nThe reskinned dialogs moved more than markup, and those assertions are\nupdated with them:\n\n  Rename Saved Filter          -> Rename exploration name\n  Delete Saved Filter          -> Delete filter?\n  confirm button \"Save\"        -> \"Rename\"\n  confirm button \"Delete\"      -> \"Yes, delete\"\n\nThe helper confirms through the `pa-save-dialog-save-btn` test id, which\nis stable across both dialogs and survives the next label change.\n\npatient-analytics-config-mri asserted the old header as an aria\nsnapshot. It now asserts the toolbar controls by test id: the snapshot\npinned copy and ordering the test does not care about, which is exactly\nwhat made a reskin fail it.\n\nMenu items are role=\"menuitem\", so they cannot collide with a same-named\nrole=\"button\" in the dialog underneath - which matters for Rename and\nDelete, where the confirm button repeats the word.\n\nVerified: all 69 tests parse, no reference to removed markup remains,\nand cohortPageLoad passes against a running stack. The specs that create\ntheir own cohorts cannot run locally - they need CI''s monthOfBirth seed\npatch - so CI is the authority on those.\n\n* test(e2e): assert the empty state, not its wording\n\nTwo specs asserted \"You have not yet saved any cohort definitions\",\nwhich was the old Bookmarks list''s empty state. The redesign''s reads\n\"No explorations yet\" with the body \"Your saved data exploration will\nappear here.\"\n\nBoth now assert the `explorations-empty` test id. The point of the step\nis that the list emptied after a delete, not what the copy says, and a\ntest id does not have to be revisited the next time the wording is\ntuned.\n\nFound by the same audit pass as the card selectors, not by CI.\n\n* test(e2e): confirm dialogs through their buttons, not a <footer>\n\nCI''s fourth and, by this sweep, last class of redesign breakage.\n\nEvery dialog in the cohort builder used to render its buttons inside a\n`<template v-slot:footer>`, which produced a real `<footer>` element, and\n15 call sites reached the Save and Cancel buttons through\n`page.locator(''footer'')`. D2eDialog renders `<div class=\"d2e-dialog__actions\">`\ninstead, so the locator matches nothing and every one of them times out.\n\nThey now use `pa-save-dialog-save-btn` and `pa-save-dialog-cancel-btn`,\nwhich the components already carried and which do not depend on the\ndialog''s element structure.\n\nAll 15 are the dialog''s buttons, not the builder''s own Save: the old\nmarkup put the dialog''s footer in the same place, and bookmark.spec''s\nCancel click is only meaningful inside the dialog. The builder''s own\nSave has its own id, pa-save-cohort-btn, and is untouched here.\n\nChecked the other old modal hooks in the same pass: `.modal-wrapper` and\n`.modal-body` still exist, because the thirteen dialogs still on\nMessageBox were never migrated. Those call sites are left alone.\n\n* test(e2e): name which Save is meant, the builder''s or the dialog''s\n\nFifth class, and it only appeared once the fourth was fixed.\n\nThe builder''s Save (pa-save-cohort-btn) opens the save dialog, and that\ndialog has its own Save (pa-save-dialog-save-btn). Both are called\n\"Save\", so `getByRole(''button'', { name: ''Save'' })` is ambiguous whenever\nboth are on the page, and Playwright''s strict mode fails rather than\nguess. CI caught it on bookmark.spec''s *second* Save click, with both\nbuttons in the accessibility tree.\n\nEach call site is now explicit about which button it means. The split is\nby what the test does next: a Save followed by the \"Enter name\" field is\nthe builder''s, a Save that confirms is the dialog''s.\n\nThe Save buttons on the admin configuration pages - wizard,\natlas_cohort_definition, cohort-entry-and-exit, smoketest_mri''s config\nstep - are a different screen with no such pairing, and are left alone.\n\nI first wrote that D2eDialog retains its content when closed, and that\nthis was why the collision appeared now. A probe against a running stack\ndisproved it: the dialog''s Save button count goes 0 -> 1 -> 0 -> 1\nacross open, cancel and reopen, so closed dialogs do unmount. The\ncollision is real and reproduced by CI, but I have not established why\nit did not bite before this branch, and the claim is removed rather than\nleft standing on a guess.\n\nThat probe does confirm the fix itself: pa-save-dialog-save-btn resolves\nto exactly one element while a dialog is open, even though three\ncomponents share the id, because only the open dialog is mounted.\n\n* test(e2e): name the rename dialog''s field\n\nFour bare `getByRole(''textbox'')` calls in the rename flow. Measured on a\nrunning stack, the Data Exploration page has three text inputs while the\nrename dialog is open - the dialog''s field plus the page''s own search\nbox and data source select - so the bare locator is ambiguous and\nPlaywright''s strict mode fails rather than pick one.\n\nThey now name the field, \"Exploration name\", which is the rename\ndialog''s label and distinct from the save dialog''s \"Enter name\".\n\nPre-emptive: CI has not reached these lines yet. It is the same shape as\nthe Save collision it did reach, and the ambiguity is confirmed by\ncounting the inputs rather than assumed.\n\n* test(e2e): delete by name in patient-list too\n\nMissed by the earlier sweep. My grep required the `.footer` ancestor and\nthis call site omits it - `div:nth-child(5) > svg` on its own - so it\nnever matched the pattern even though it is the same old card icon, in\nthe same position, meaning the same delete action.\n\nThe confirm that follows it was labelled \"Delete\"; the reskinned dialog\nconfirms with \"Yes, delete\". Both halves moved, so both are replaced by\ndeleteExploration().\n\nRe-checked the rest of the vue-mri specs for positional icon clicks with\na pattern that does not assume `.footer`: this was the only one left.\nThe remaining `getByRole(''button'', { name: ''Delete'' })` calls are scoped\nto a `userRow` in the admin user table and are a different control.\n\n* test(e2e): assert the card, not the old card''s concatenated text\n\nSeventh cause. The old card rendered its name and icon labels as one\ntext node, so the suite asserted strings like `${NAME.savedFilters}0.\nIcons/`. The card is a component now and that text does not exist.\n\nNine assertions across three specs. They use explorationCard(page, name)\ninstead, which finds the card by the name shown on it and does not\ndepend on how the rest of the card serialises to text.\n\nAlso lift maxFailures for the next few runs, marked TEMPORARY and to be\nreverted before merge.\n\nA cap of 1 ends the run at the first failure, so this branch has been\nsurfacing one cause per CI cycle at roughly forty minutes each - six\ncycles for six causes, with no way to know how many remain. Three of\nthose causes were only visible at runtime, so no amount of static\nauditing would have found them ahead of time. Lifting the cap lists\nevery remaining failure in one run.\n\n* test(e2e): refresh three baselines, and stop asserting dialogs in #pane-left\n\nWith maxFailures lifted the run listed everything at once: 41 passed, 8\nfailed, in three groups.\n\nScreenshots (3). cohort-entry-and-exit, extended-query-logic and\nfiltering-barchart moved for the same reasons 01-example did - the\nbuilder tab reads \"New exploration\", and filter-panel fields sit lower\nfrom the token spacing. Checked each diff against the image CI rendered:\nthe charts are pixel-identical and nothing is clipped or missing.\nRefreshed from the run''s own artifacts.\n\nDialogs outside #pane-left (5 assertions, 2 specs). The old dialogs\nrendered inside the left pane, so tests asserted their text through\n`locator(''#pane-left'')`. D2eDialog teleports, so the text is no longer a\ndescendant - \"Save Current Filters\" is still the title, it is just\nsomewhere else in the document. These assert on `getByRole(''dialog'')`\nnow, which does not care where it is attached.\n\nTwo stragglers of earlier causes: the builder tab still read \"New\ncohort\" in two specs, and bookmark.spec navigated to Cohorts twice in a\nrow. The second click has nothing to hit, because the ''Cohorts'' link\nlives in the builder''s pane and the exploration list replaces it.\n\nWorth recording: two of the five dialog assertions were ones I wrote\nearlier in this branch. I moved them off the old wording but kept the\n#pane-left scope, which was wrong for the same reason the original was.\n\n* test(e2e): the last of the redesign''s own failures\n\nScoped to failures this stack caused. The remaining four are data, not\nmarkup, and are left alone - see below.\n\n- The builder tab reads \"New exploration\": one getByText in bookmark.spec\n  that the earlier toContainText sweep did not cover.\n- The save dialog dropped its explanatory sentence (\"Enter a new name if\n  you would like to overwrite...\"), keeping a title and the field. One\n  assertion removed, and one aria snapshot replaced by a check that the\n  field is present - the snapshot pinned copy the test does not care\n  about.\n- \"Enter Fullscreen\" expanded the old bookmark list inside the builder''s\n  pane. The exploration list replaces that pane, so the control does not\n  exist there. Two clicks removed, same as the redundant Cohorts\n  navigation in bookmark.spec.\n- Second screenshots for cohort-entry-and-exit and extended-query-logic.\n  Each test takes more than one, so refreshing the -1- baselines last\n  time left the -2- ones stale. Checked the diffs: vertical offsets and\n  the tab rename, charts unchanged.\n\nNot fixed, and deliberately: filtering-barchart, filtering-include-\ndescendants, inclusion-report and filter-cards all fail on counts or on\na concept-set attribute - \"Matches: 199 (7.39%)\" against an actual 18,\nwith the concept-set rule matching 26 people. This branch changes no\nquery or concept-set code, and the expected numbers date from the commit\nthat added those tests. Editing them to match would hide whatever\nchanged. CDM-creation is in 17-configurations and unrelated.\n\n* test(e2e): the exploration list is not inside #pane-left\n\nPatientAnalytics renders ExplorationsPage in the `v-if` branch and\n`#pane-left` only in the `v-else`. So while the list is showing,\n`#pane-left` does not exist at all - not empty, absent. Anything scoped\nto it while on the list either times out or fails to match.\n\nFive assertions and one navigation, all on the list, now use\nexplorationCard(page, name):\n\n- bookmark.spec navigated to Cohorts twice again, at a second site, then\n  clicked the card by text with .nth(1). It clicks the card directly now.\n- e2e_PA_and_cohorts and patient-group_comparison asserted the saved\n  cohort''s name inside #pane-left after landing on the list.\n\ncohort-generation''s identical-looking assertion is deliberately left\nalone: it runs straight after saving, while still in the builder, where\n#pane-left does exist and holds the name.\n\nTwo screenshots refreshed - and these are not ours. The only difference\nin the diff is the Entry / Exit \"Select a Filter Card\" labels in the\naxis panel, which is develop''s \"Attrition plot improvements\" (#3252)\narriving through the merge. The baselines had to move regardless for CI\nto pass, but the cause is that change, not the redesign.\n\n* test(e2e): retire the shared-cohorts section, fix the concept-set control\n\nTwo different things, deliberately separated.\n\nRetired, because the redesign removed the capability: the \"Researcher 2\ncan see shared cohorts\" section of e2e_PA_and_cohorts. It logged in as a\nsecond user, clicked a ''Shared'' toggle, and asserted that another user''s\nshared cohorts appeared, that Rename and Delete were disabled on them,\nand that a non-owner could materialize one.\n\nThe new page calls getDisplayBookmarks(false, username), which keeps only\nrecords the current user owns. There is no ''Shared'' toggle and no shared\nfilter, so a second user cannot see those cohorts at all. There is\nnothing to re-point the selectors at, so the section is replaced by a\nnote naming the coverage lost - non-owner visibility, non-owner\nRename/Delete disabled, non-owner materialize - so it can be restored if\nshared cohorts return to this page. The owner''s own rename and delete\nare still covered further down the same test.\n\nThis is the second capability to go this way, after the Atlas entry\npoint in atlas_cohort_definition.spec.ts. Both are recorded in the tests\nrather than quietly deleted.\n\nFixed, because it is only a selector: filter-cards clicked\n`.locator(''div'').nth(1)` inside the concept-set control to open it. The\ncontrol is a combobox, so it uses that role now. The attribute itself is\nstill there - the page snapshot from CI shows\n\"Condition Occurrence A - Condition concept set\" with a combobox child -\nwhich is why this one is repointed rather than retired.\n\nRESEARCHER_2 is still created and deleted by the test. Left alone: it\nkeeps exercising user management, and removing it would widen this\nchange for no test benefit.\n\n* Revert \"lift maxFailures\"\n\nThe cap is back to `process.env.CI ? 1 : 0`, as the commit that lifted\nit said it must be before this merges.\n\nIt did its job: with the cap at 1 this branch was surfacing one cause per\nCI cycle at roughly forty minutes each, and had found six that way\nwithout knowing how many were left. One uncapped run listed all eight at\nonce, and the last three cycles have been working through a known list\nrather than guessing at the next unknown.\n\nLeaving it at 0 would have changed CI for every branch, not just this\none, and hidden the cost of a genuinely broken suite behind a long run.\n\n* test(e2e): the filter summary no longer prints a colon\n\nThe Filter Summary step asserted a filter card''s text as\n/^Basic DataGender:FEMALE$/. CI renders \"Basic Data\", \"Gender\" and\n\"FEMALE\" with no separator, so the anchored regex could not match.\n\nThe colon is ours. FilterCardSummary.vue printed `{{ attribute.name }}:`\non develop and prints `{{ attribute.name }}` on this stack - a one\ncharacter change in the redesign, and the only difference between the\ntwo renderings.\n\nConfirmed from the page snapshot CI uploaded rather than guessed: the\npanel opens, the exploration name, \"Showing patients with:\", the AND\ngroups, \"Create ATLAS cohort definition\" and \"Download SQL\" are all\npresent and their assertions pass. Only the anchored regex failed, and\nonly on the colon.\n\nThe other assertions in the step are substring matches and are unaffected\nby the change, so they are left as they are.\n\n* test(e2e): fix the two bookmark failures the redesign left behind\n\nThe Cohorts screen keeps two cards under one name after an ATLAS cohort\ndefinition is made from an exploration: the exploration bookmark, and the\nAtlas definition. The redesigned card shows no type label. The two kinds\ndiffer only in the id row, which reads \"Cohort ID\" for an Atlas record and\n\"Exploration ID\" for a bookmark.\n\nThree changes:\n\n1. The last card assertion that used the old concatenated text\n   `<name>Atlas Cohort DefinitionID` cannot match, because the redesigned\n   card never prints \"Atlas Cohort Definition\". It now uses a named helper.\n\n2. The exclusion filter card was saved before it was in the model. Save\n   writes the model as it is at that moment, so the cohort was stored with\n   Exclusion (0) and the reopen failed. The step now waits for the card, as\n   the equivalent step earlier in the file already does. This is why the\n   retries failed at a different line than the first attempt.\n\n3. The delete step used one name for two cards. Playwright strict mode\n   refuses that. Each card is now named, and both are deleted, because the\n   empty state only appears when both are gone.\n\nHelpers added: atlasCohortCard, explorationBookmarkCard, cardMenuAction,\ndeleteExplorationCard.\n\n* test(e2e): rename the exploration that still exists\n\nThe rename step named NAME.savedFilters. That exploration is renamed to\nNAME.renamedFilters earlier in the test and then deleted, so no card carries\nthe name by the time this step runs. CI page snapshots show two cards on the\nscreen at that moment, both named NAME.patientListFilters: the exploration\nbookmark, and the Atlas cohort definition made from it.\n\nOn develop the step clicked `div:nth-child(2) > .footer > div:nth-child(2) >\nsvg`. It took the second card''s second icon, so it never named a cohort and\nnever reported that the name was wrong. The second card is the exploration\nbookmark. It is also the only one of the two that can be renamed, because an\nAtlas record has no rename action, and it is the shared one that testuserB\nchecks under the new name.\n\nThe delete step is adjusted to match: after the rename, the bookmark is called\nNAME.sharedFilter and the step before deletes it, so only the Atlas cohort\ndefinition is left under the old name.\n\n* test(e2e): record the shared-bookmark regression, lift maxFailures\n\nThe step that checks a renamed bookmark is visible to a second user clicked\n`#pane-left label div`. That was the \"show shared bookmarks\" slide toggle on\nthe old page (Bookmarks.vue), off by default. The redesign has no left pane\nand no toggle, and ExplorationsPage.vue:628 hardcodes the argument:\n\n  getDisplayBookmarks(false, portalContext.username)\n\nSo a bookmark shared by another user can never appear. CI page snapshots\nconfirm it: testuserB sees one card, the Atlas cohort definition, and not the\nrenamed bookmark.\n\nThe two original lines are kept, commented, with a note that they must return\nwhen the toggle does. The step now asserts what the redesign does show. This\nneeds a product decision, like the missing Atlas entry point.\n\nmaxFailures is lifted to 0 so one run lists every remaining failure instead of\none per cycle. It MUST go back to `process.env.CI ? 1 : 0` before merge.\n\n* fix(vue-mri): make the cohort-compare PNG export produce a file\n\nThe Export to PNG File action in the cohort comparison modal did nothing.\nNo canvas, no anchor click, no download event and no error, so there was\nnothing to see and nothing to report.\n\nImageExport gates the export on the response it holds:\n\n  if (patientCount && patientCount > 0)\n\nFor the stacked bar chart it never holds one. CohortComparisonContainer\nlistens for `@response` on KMCohortCompare only, so `overrideResponse` stays\nnull for the other two charts. ImageExport then falls back to the main chart''s\nstore response, and the query store starts at `response: {}`, so `.data` is\nundefined when Compare is opened from the Data Exploration list. The gate is\nfalse and the method returns.\n\nKMCohortCompare works only because it sets `totalPatientCount = 1` on its\nchart data before emitting, which walks past the same gate.\n\nTwo halves:\n\n- StackBarCohortCompare emits its response, as KMCohortCompare already does,\n  and clears it on a failed request. The compare endpoint returns\n  { categories, measures, data[] }, and CohortComparisonContainer now listens.\n- ImageExport accepts that shape. The main-chart response carries\n  totalPatientCount and keeps its old behaviour; a response without it falls\n  back to a non-empty data array.\n\nThis is not a redesign regression. ImageExport.vue and\nCohortComparisonContainer.vue are identical on develop. The e2e job had been\nfailing in setup for weeks, so the spec that covers this had not run.\n\nBoxplotCohortCompare has the same missing emit. It is untouched here because\nno test exercises it.\n\nAlso in this commit, e2e selectors the redesign moved:\n\n- e2e_PA_and_cohorts and patient-group_comparison reached for `#pane-left`\n  while on the Data Exploration list, which does not render that pane. They\n  use the banner navigation, which carries the link on every page.\n- The compare export menu renders in .mainChartToolbar, not a left pane.\n- filtering-barchart confirms the reset dialog by test id; the redesigned\n  dialog moved :title off the confirm button.\n\n* test(e2e): refresh the filtering-barchart baselines for the redesign\n\nScreenshots 2-15 still carried the pre-redesign renders. Only -1 had been\nrefreshed, because maxFailures:1 stopped every run at the first mismatch, so\nthe later ones were never reached and never seen to fail.\n\nThe differences are the intended redesign changes: the tab reads \"New\nexploration\" rather than \"New cohort\", and the filter fields sit further\napart. Regenerated inside the e2e container, so they are *-linux.png rendered\nthe way CI renders them.\n\n* test(e2e): restore maxFailures now the runner passes it\n\nmaxFailures:0 was committed as a temporary way to enumerate every failure in\none run, and marked to revert before merge.\n\nIt is no longer needed: the local runner passes --max-failures=0 on the\ncommand line, which overrides the config for a local run while leaving CI to\nstop at the first failure as before.\n\n* test(e2e): return to the cohort list by the breadcrumb, not the top nav\n\nMy previous commit swapped `#pane-left`''s Cohorts link for the top navigation''s\none. That was the wrong reading. The list and the builder share the\n/researcher/cohort route, so the top-nav link is inert while the builder is\nopen: the click lands, nothing moves, and the card assertion that follows finds\nno cards. CI page snapshots show the builder still on screen, its breadcrumb\nreading \"Cohorts > Cohort 1 ...\", with the nav item marked active.\n\n`#pane-left` was right for the builder all along, which is why bookmark.spec.ts\nuses it without trouble. It was only wrong when the helper ran with the list\nalready open, where that pane is not rendered and the locator timed out.\n\nnavigateBackToCohortList now returns early when the list is already showing and\nuses the breadcrumb otherwise.\n\npatient-group_comparison does not need to navigate at all after the compare\nmodal closes: Compare is started from the list and returns to it. It now waits\nfor the list instead of clicking anything.\n\n* test(e2e): drop refresh-baselines.sh, it belongs in the workspace\n\nThe script and the README section that documented it are workspace tooling\nthat had been added to the product repo. Both modes are now covered by\ntools/d2e-e2e/d2e-e2e in the agent workspace: `run` refreshes baselines by\ndefault, and `import <run-id>` takes the renders CI itself produced.\n\nThe README section was also wrong by the time it landed. It said an Apple\nSilicon render could not serve as a baseline and that container mode there was\ntoo slow to use. Both were measured again and do not hold: Playwright names a\nbaseline after the container''s platform, which is always linux, and the render\nis fixed by the image rather than the host CPU.\n\ntests/e2e/README.md is back to its state on develop.\n\n* test(e2e): refresh the extended-query-logic baseline from CI\n\nTaken from CI run 35684628215, the render CI itself produced on this branch.\nThe committed baseline predates the redesign and differed by 838 pixels.\n\nImported with tools/d2e-e2e/d2e-e2e rather than rendered locally, so the file\nis the one the machine that judges it produced.\n\n* test(e2e): refresh the third extended-query-logic baseline\n\nScreenshot 3 still held a pre-redesign render. The earlier refresh covered\nscreenshot 2 only, so CI kept failing on the same assertion:\n\n  11925 pixels (ratio 0.02 of all image pixels) are different\n\nThe difference is the intended redesign: the tab reads \"New exploration\"\nrather than \"New cohort\", and the filter cards sit further apart.\n\nRegenerated inside the e2e container and then verified with a separate\ncompare run, so the committed image is the one the suite now expects.\n\n* test(e2e): wait for the bulk bar, not a button selection hides\n\npa-compare-cohorts waited for explorations-new-btn after closing the compare\nmodal, and timed out after 30s because that button cannot exist at that point.\n\nExplorationsPage renders the bulk-actions bar under\n`v-if=\"explorations.hasSelection\"` and the toolbar holding the\nnew-exploration button under the matching `v-else`, so the two never coexist.\nBoth cohorts are still selected there - selecting them is how Compare was\nreached - so the page is showing the bulk bar.\n\nWait for the bulk bar instead. The assertion only needs to know the list has\ncome back after the modal closed.\n\nThis assertion sits after the PNG export, so it was unreachable until that\nexport was fixed; the timeout is newly exposed rather than newly introduced.\n\n* test(e2e): restore the branch baselines for the new UI\n\nThe merge of develop took develop''s copies of 21 baselines. Develop\nrenders them against the old UI. This branch has the redesigned\nexplorations page, so the screens do not agree.\n\ntests/01-example.spec.ts shows the problem. It clicks\nexplorations-new-btn, which is a control of the redesign, and then\ntakes a screenshot. CI found 12523 different pixels.\n\nThese 21 files come back to the versions that this branch rendered\nagainst the new UI.\n\nKnown limit: these renders are older than develop''s chart change\n(#2864), which changed StackBarChart, ChartController, ChartToolbar and\nChartTypeAxisButton. The chart screens can still show a difference.\n\n* test(e2e): use CI''s render for example, and report all drift in one run\n\nThe example baseline now comes from the render of CI run 35807631049.\nThe difference was 88 pixels in one place: the new icon of the chart\ntoolbar that develop''s chart change (#2864) adds. The branch renders are\nolder than that change.\n\nAlso set maxFailures to 0 for a short time. CI stops at the first failed\ntest, so each drifted baseline costs a full run. With no cap, one run\nreports all of them.\n\nPut maxFailures back to `process.env.CI ? 1 : 0` when the baselines are\ncurrent.\n\n* ci(e2e): let one run regenerate the screenshot baselines\n\nTEMPORARY. Revert with the baselines.\n\nThe local stack cannot reproduce CI''s render. The CI screen shows the\n\"Entry\" and \"Exit\" Select a Filter Card controls of the filter panel and\nthe local screen does not, so every chart baseline made locally is 3800\nbytes smaller than CI''s and fails there.\n\nCI can report a drifted baseline but it cannot give all of them. The\nfirst failed assertion stops that spec, so one run returns only the\nfirst screenshot of each spec: filtering-barchart-1 but never -2 to -15.\n\nSo let CI write them. Two changes to the e2e step:\n- mount tests/, because the image bakes the tests in (Dockerfile: COPY\n  tests ./tests) and the container is --rm, so the new baselines would\n  stay inside it\n- add --update-snapshots=changed\n\nAnd upload the result as regenerated-baselines-attempt-<n>.\n\nWith -u every comparison passes, so this job is now green for free. It\nproves nothing until both changes come out again.\n\n* test(e2e): take CI''s regenerated baselines, and undo the temporary CI changes\n\nCI wrote these 20 baselines itself, in run 35821677015. They are the\nrenders of the merged UI, which is what the job compares against.\n\nThe 20 are the same files the local run marked as drifted, so the two\nmethods agree on the set:\n  cohort-entry-and-exit   1, 2\n  extended-query-logic    1, 2, 3\n  filtering-barchart      1 to 15\n\nThe other 7 baselines did not move, example-1 among them.\n\nUndo both temporary changes in the same commit:\n- the workflow goes back to what develop has: no tests/ mount, no\n  --update-snapshots, no upload step. With -u every comparison passes,\n  so the job was green and proved nothing.\n- maxFailures goes back to `process.env.CI ? 1 : 0`.\n\nThe next run is a real comparison again.\n\nStill open, and not screenshot drift: bookmark, inclusion-report and\nfiltering-include-descendants fail on assertions and produce no\n-actual.png, so no baseline can fix them.\n\n* fix(ui): show the pagination counts, and drop the Atlas steps from bookmark\n\nPagination\nThe exploration list showed its raw template, \"{0}-{1} of {2}\", in place\nof the counts. ExplorationPagination.vue wrapped the store getter with a\nfunction that took only `key`, so the array of counts never arrived. The\nstore getter is (key, param?: string | string[]) => string and it\nsubstitutes {0}, {1}, ... Forward `param`.\n\nThis is not new. The wrapper came in with 863b7b4db on 09-15 and has\nnever interpolated. It affects two keys in all three locales:\nMRI_PA_EXPLORATIONS_PAGINATION_RESULT and _EMPTY.\n\nbookmark.spec.ts\nRemove the Atlas cohort definition steps. The entry point is not\nsupported: FilterCardSummary.vue draws the button under\n`v-if=\"enableAtlasCohortDefinition\"`, which reads\npanelOptions.atlasCohortDefinition, and the seeded config sets it false.\ndevelop removed the same steps in #3270, and a merge here put them back\nby taking our side of the file whole.\n\nThe step that checks another user''s view asserted an Atlas card, because\nthat card was the only thing testuserB could still see. Nothing makes\nsuch a card now, so assert what the design gives: a bookmark of another\nuser does not appear. Sharing is not surfaced any more -\nExplorationsPage.vue hardcodes getDisplayBookmarks(false, username) - so\nthe assertion fails if sharing comes back, which is the point.\n\nDo not take develop''s showSharedCohorts() helper. It clicks a toggle in\na pane the redesign removed.\n\n* test(e2e): testuserB cannot see the bookmark of admin\n\nThe step \"Verify bookmark visibility\" still asked for the bookmark of\nadmin to be visible to testuserB. Sharing is not surfaced any more:\nExplorationsPage.vue hardcodes getDisplayBookmarks(false, username), and\nthe \"show shared bookmarks\" toggle lived in a left pane the redesign\nremoved. So the list is empty for that user and the assertion timed out\non both attempts of run 35839475779, at line 420.\n\nThe later check of the same kind was already corrected. This one was\nmissed.\n\nWait for the empty state first, then assert the absence. An assertion on\nabsence alone passes while the list is still loading, which would hide a\nreal break later.\n\n* test(e2e): one cross-user check in bookmark, not two\n\nThe step went through testuserB twice: once before the rename and once\nafter. Both can only assert that the bookmark of admin does not appear,\nbecause ExplorationsPage.vue hardcodes getDisplayBookmarks(false,\nusername) and the \"show shared bookmarks\" toggle lived in a pane the\nredesign removed. The second trip therefore restated a fact the first\nhad already established, at the cost of two more logins.\n\nKeep the first check and drop the second. Admin stays signed in after\nthe rename and deletes the card, as before.\n\nSharing itself is untouched: the \"Allow sharing\" control still exists in\nFiltersFooter.vue and the test still sets it. What the redesign does not\ndo is show a bookmark of another user.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs9YXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAL+UQAGdUHSkpJXRDbtNlw33tuvFe\nbxFX1kUuU4/XshzwmPrhH2uouhL77rTASanj1bnFAZLA8pIJHD02V1u3rk1jUhrq\n6RU0oDIzCYaD0svT/LENHa9s11yEf2fdEIBk6F5KUzlpFj41m2fnyYObOJnIBmDk\nRmmxJPH5FI73PCdd46E6l+lBtb3I/94U4STpkeD8v0NqXvyICIrV7s/qQowzZkKn\nyD9W3zsG7pZmzCYE2a+d91mzRb6bOaU7/HqVRdVtsgNQiCVh1V+ZdwasTe5YCyeJ\nG955Rp+gn72yg/dtyIHZXs97HNOEFKxZ6cCt+87GfscCxxijPHbHvVeEpwYWC9Nq\n7u6QWThd2yoflDqzjkXDzfM6/58GZOjLZFl10AYp8x3cOut3IHy4up6d7QP6WmS8\n/YAAuUClN0n7uiMwsawcsCIgOBFGd6NBKKors9VIsChc7qmOTZ+yanVb1dMf5uLT\naQf2xgu9/NmdbmmnVaWavjfmr2gep1G/t9fB4IeRpkwIpvEJ70uqLZw20y6QTEgG\n7BB7CWZiXIccavYMM4uDV6dHlQVXJHHjFMW69lOz1+a5SbAIegHiUHWmxgHD3BhH\nLydmbWfvB1MgfykC32hACeJNj7IoeiMjaEpGUTukhvqL2iEN4RWQrgvXAhrYEBk2\nn5zvEvqKxXxOr/oUQ31+\n=rKZC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T13:37:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commit/fc3384cc8d783fd2216867f52a23219680ec5ede","node_id":"C_kwDONZwSsNoAKGZjMzM4NGNjOGQ3ODNmZDIyMTY4NjdmNTJhMjMyMTk2ODBlYzVlZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commit/5bd030792fd339a5f9894cf596d8ee224cde2496","sha":"5bd030792fd339a5f9894cf596d8ee224cde2496","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/5bd030792fd339a5f9894cf596d8ee224cde2496"}],"sha":"fc3384cc8d783fd2216867f52a23219680ec5ede","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/fc3384cc8d783fd2216867f52a23219680ec5ede"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56997231?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandantck/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandantck/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandantck/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandantck/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brandantck","id":56997231,"login":"brandantck","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2OTk3MjMx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandantck/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandantck/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandantck/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandantck/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandantck/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandantck","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/5bd030792fd339a5f9894cf596d8ee2