ts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/khairul-syazwan","id":80243918,"login":"khairul-syazwan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwMjQzOTE4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/khairul-syazwan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/20d6f0b650f18a2671a4103e149f0c0e6d85599a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T07:47:46Z","email":"80243918+khairul-syazwan@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Khairul Syazwan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T07:47:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ui): clear cohort dirty state as soon as the save completes (#3382)\n\n* fix(vue-mri): clear cohort dirty state when the save returns\n\nSaving a cohort re-captured the unsaved-changes baseline only after the\ncohort list refresh (GET /d2e-webapi/cohortdefinition?source=pa) resolved.\nThat refresh is needed only to resolve the saved bookmark id. Until it\nreturned, the cohort still compared dirty, so a user who navigated away in\nthat window was asked about unsaved changes on a cohort that was saved.\nA slow network makes the window wide enough to hit reliably.\n\nRe-baseline with the payload that was written, immediately after the write\nreturns. The list refresh and the active-bookmark swap are unchanged.\n\nFixes #3341\n\n* no-mistakes(review): test: pin written payload in saveBookmark baseline test\n\n* no-mistakes(review): fix: re-baseline post-refresh from written payload\n\n* no-mistakes(document): comment post-refresh baseline capture; format save test\n\n* fix(vue-mri): take the saved cohort id from the save response\n\nThe save flow waited for the cohort list refresh\n(GET /d2e-webapi/cohortdefinition?source=pa) to learn the id of the bookmark\nit had just written. That wait is what left a saved cohort reporting unsaved\nchanges, and narrowing the window only made the race rarer.\n\nbookmark-svc already returns the id: insert answers { status, bmkId } and\nupdate answers ''success'', and every other field of the stored record is\neither fixed by createBookmarkDto (view_name null, version 1) or known to the\ncaller. So the refresh is not needed to adopt the saved cohort at all. Build\nthe record from the response, adopt it immediately, and refresh the cohort\nlist in the background.\n\nThis also makes a successful save checkable. fireBookmarkQuery reports a\nfailed insert or update itself and then resolves, so a resolved promise was\nnever proof the cohort was saved; the code now requires a success payload\nbefore it marks anything clean. A failed save leaves the cohort dirty\ninstead of silently reporting it as saved.\n\nBoth save paths are covered. SaveCohortModal took the same wait before\nmaterializing, so it had the same race; it now uses the response too, and\nraises instead of materializing a cohort that was never written. Its second\nrefresh, after materialization, stays as it is, because only the server\nknows the resulting cohortDefinitionId.\n\nCloses the three follow-ups recorded on the pull request.\n\n* no-mistakes(review): upsert saved bookmark into cohort list on save\n\n* no-mistakes(review): keep awaited cohort list refresh; baseline written payload\n\n* no-mistakes(review): move save-success tests into BookmarkUtils test file\n\n* no-mistakes(review): match modal save error text to failed command\n\n* no-mistakes(document): fix isBookmarkSaveSuccess doc comment placement and wording","tree":{"sha":"2a3d8e267cbea533129591aae1c0a02c8325fa15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/git/trees/2a3d8e267cbea533129591aae1c0a02c8325fa15"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/git/commits/20d6f0b650f18a2671a4103e149f0c0e6d85599a","verification":{"payload":"tree 2a3d8e267cbea533129591aae1c0a02c8325fa15\nparent 57cdc8dc03ce536e19b481e733eec27fe8f4c0d8\nauthor Khairul Syazwan <80243918+khairul-syazwan@users.noreply.github.com> 1790063266 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790063266 +0000\n\nfix(ui): clear cohort dirty state as soon as the save completes (#3382)\n\n* fix(vue-mri): clear cohort dirty state when the save returns\n\nSaving a cohort re-captured the unsaved-changes baseline only after the\ncohort list refresh (GET /d2e-webapi/cohortdefinition?source=pa) resolved.\nThat refresh is needed only to resolve the saved bookmark id. Until it\nreturned, the cohort still compared dirty, so a user who navigated away in\nthat window was asked about unsaved changes on a cohort that was saved.\nA slow network makes the window wide enough to hit reliably.\n\nRe-baseline with the payload that was written, immediately after the write\nreturns. The list refresh and the active-bookmark swap are unchanged.\n\nFixes #3341\n\n* no-mistakes(review): test: pin written payload in saveBookmark baseline test\n\n* no-mistakes(review): fix: re-baseline post-refresh from written payload\n\n* no-mistakes(document): comment post-refresh baseline capture; format save test\n\n* fix(vue-mri): take the saved cohort id from the save response\n\nThe save flow waited for the cohort list refresh\n(GET /d2e-webapi/cohortdefinition?source=pa) to learn the id of the bookmark\nit had just written. That wait is what left a saved cohort reporting unsaved\nchanges, and narrowing the window only made the race rarer.\n\nbookmark-svc already returns the id: insert answers { status, bmkId } and\nupdate answers ''success'', and every other field of the stored record is\neither fixed by createBookmarkDto (view_name null, version 1) or known to the\ncaller. So the refresh is not needed to adopt the saved cohort at all. Build\nthe record from the response, adopt it immediately, and refresh the cohort\nlist in the background.\n\nThis also makes a successful save checkable. fireBookmarkQuery reports a\nfailed insert or update itself and then resolves, so a resolved promise was\nnever proof the cohort was saved; the code now requires a success payload\nbefore it marks anything clean. A failed save leaves the cohort dirty\ninstead of silently reporting it as saved.\n\nBoth save paths are covered. SaveCohortModal took the same wait before\nmaterializing, so it had the same race; it now uses the response too, and\nraises instead of materializing a cohort that was never written. Its second\nrefresh, after materialization, stays as it is, because only the server\nknows the resulting cohortDefinitionId.\n\nCloses the three follow-ups recorded on the pull request.\n\n* no-mistakes(review): upsert saved bookmark into cohort list on save\n\n* no-mistakes(review): keep awaited cohort list refresh; baseline written payload\n\n* no-mistakes(review): move save-success tests into BookmarkUtils test file\n\n* no-mistakes(review): match modal save error text to failed command\n\n* no-mistakes(document): fix isBookmarkSaveSuccess doc comment placement and wording","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqskZUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGr8QAEK1Mn01vy2r+qKsiImWNoaU\nAxCTybpzhSYK2m6+HxrKXWqIBmFfS3tjc5QmvT6dxvbE2A2EV0nOr+RQbyMnQctU\nxefg/1Nnf4fTrQSDlomZqc7l6CaS6/if1seJMcXi1EWSH01uE8XZYDWkxXF64oHE\nLA1LM6KD9AJ4KLf7Q6Ygm5YxD3sHOH+2F+Fo8mbja/b3lB2xOjuJkxAkVDeQ3r7L\noyXoZv4DtOG1fYcDQcB4fkXEBRR68XPHwXpb+aXlqvGWrNvgsQ3yms0OKU96gMLp\n7