/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/d690698aabc5d3659ecf9eb19baa16e77e707f35"}],"sha":"15647adfc347d1451cd68d442ce731b2f2597680","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/15647adfc347d1451cd68d442ce731b2f2597680"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48011859?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suwarnoong/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suwarnoong/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suwarnoong/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suwarnoong/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/suwarnoong","id":48011859,"login":"suwarnoong","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MDExODU5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suwarnoong/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suwarnoong/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suwarnoong/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suwarnoong/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suwarnoong/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/suwarnoong","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/d690698aabc5d3659ecf9eb19baa16e77e707f35/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T05:51:44Z","email":"48011859+suwarnoong@users.noreply.github.com","name":"suwarno ong"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T05:51:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(portal): recover PhysioNet first-login access without a second sign-in (#3366)\n\n* fix(portal): recover PhysioNet first-login access without a second sign-in\n\nOn a first federated login the access token is minted before the entitlements\ngrant. With USER_MGMT__ROLE_SOURCE=logto the /user-group/list response is derived\nfrom that pre-grant token''s `roles` claim, so the just-granted dataset-researcher\nrole is invisible and the portal shows \"Access denied\" until a second login.\n\nAfter the grant, silently refresh the token and re-fetch the user groups (bounded\nby MAX_REFRESH_ATTEMPTS) until the fresh mint reflects the role. This replaces the\nprior interactive re-login (and its sessionStorage guard / 8s block) with a silent\nrefresh_token grant — no redirect, no reload.\n\nAlso drop the \"must sign in again\" admin copy on grant/revoke: the change now takes\neffect automatically via the authz-freshness stale-token refresh.\n\n* revert(e2e): restore original granted-permission assertion in wizard spec\n\nDrops the stray one-line assertion tweak accidentally bundled into the\nPhysioNet first-login fix; keeps develop''s wizard.spec.ts changes intact.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(e2e): match new granted-permission label in wizard spec\n\nUpdate the assertion to the full ACCESS_PANEL__SUCCESS copy:\n\"User admin has been granted permission to access the dataset.\"\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fc52455cd4f78a85de2379d98173e03925b123b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/git/trees/fc52455cd4f78a85de2379d98173e03925b123b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/git/commits/d690698aabc5d3659ecf9eb19baa16e77e707f35","verification":{"payload":"tree fc52455cd4f78a85de2379d98173e03925b123b4\nparent 80bab912068b94abd4cc0c3aedc8788d9ccf3f9a\nauthor suwarno ong <48011859+suwarnoong@users.noreply.github.com> 1790056304 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790056304 +0000\n\nfix(portal): recover PhysioNet first-login access without a second sign-in (#3366)\n\n* fix(portal): recover PhysioNet first-login access without a second sign-in\n\nOn a first federated login the access token is minted before the entitlements\ngrant. With USER_MGMT__ROLE_SOURCE=logto the /user-group/list response is derived\nfrom that pre-grant token''s `roles` claim, so the just-granted dataset-researcher\nrole is invisible and the portal shows \"Access denied\" until a second login.\n\nAfter the grant, silently refresh the token and re-fetch the user groups (bounded\nby MAX_REFRESH_ATTEMPTS) until the fresh mint reflects the role. This replaces the\nprior interactive re-login (and its sessionStorage guard / 8s block) with a silent\nrefresh_token grant — no redirect, no reload.\n\nAlso drop the \"must sign in again\" admin copy on grant/revoke: the change now takes\neffect automatically via the authz-freshness stale-token refresh.\n\n* revert(e2e): restore original granted-permission assertion in wizard spec\n\nDrops the stray one-line assertion tweak accidentally bundled into the\nPhysioNet first-login fix; keeps develop''s wizard.spec.ts changes intact.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(e2e): match new granted-permission label in wizard spec\n\nUpdate the assertion to the full ACCESS_PANEL__SUCCESS copy:\n\"User admin has been granted permission to access the dataset.\"\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsipCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjEgQAI5dfcgO/Tz5iJJzGy7ykE6v\nn5m4qP1jMxC8lxDrtiNavQpPXUo0rwQmgXcfjMbYhyw5A2QWGDujgpAA7WHsqe7t\nygCy+R3n3Dw6iEwH4LMa97s9m+dqrK4sXVXekCl8lquEdrmkBvYZKDC1fpV1HLPd\niQ57lXSNVBlkNtNbPDP5ifHK1J3rc1vBdVY9ZHfSd2c26ZrRGqfoRQd2sZFqwP99\nWuDPSUUhEUbQkKPDvPLKVkQKYY4whyqabAcifCvEKBHICMIgIHhqTstfFwLpUZbV\nVaGCdwjfldn4CAPrl5HUw395dc8fxzuURSQgPKf41CPrGFYmT1MfcSFM/0G6SvuC\neOlp7GW4Oa0+MVRtk0sUgWV4EjPaisa2jA2f5F3ZAe8TusHJZswuVBm/DCd8e98j\n4I6JnKV3oZoWHoGvYwbESrqWba4SSqVFoXYRxRBuwMk9oi2OwkLuCdMjIgE65k1d\nH9j4IVUvb0/YRlENGmuKZCi+lHZEBa3AQ5uqno9S2+TJZt4pkJhurl3BrDSPPXDB\nLzavAcWAI1FuViF8+tGPSTi/9vWylsasKXedmkajTIlW1f2Y2No0wNuk/78+t+wj\n2jwTiOhOlFD5tMNVmiV7V2DzBzugMAPwwcr9F0I8vB29u8alHR/iKJd/qOI0g0wC\n6ssy9hOEhqdjBKQRnMBI\n=QnfB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T07:12:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commit/d690698aabc5d3659ecf9eb19baa16e77e707f35","node_id":"C_kwDONZwSsNoAKGQ2OTA2OThhYWJjNWQzNjU5ZWNmOWViMTliYWExNmU3N2U3MDdmMzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commit/80bab912068b94abd4cc0c3aedc8788d9ccf3f9a","sha":"80bab912068b94abd4cc0c3aedc8788d9ccf3f9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/80bab912068b94abd4cc0c3aedc8788d9ccf3f9a"}],"sha":"d690698aabc5d3659ecf9eb19baa16e77e707f35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/d690698aabc5d3659ecf9eb19baa16e77e707f35"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16306573?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/csafreen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/csafreen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/csafreen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/csafreen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/csafreen","id":16306573,"login":"csafreen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzA2NTcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/csafreen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/csafreen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/csafreen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/csafreen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/csafreen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/csafreen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/commits/80bab912068b94abd4cc0c3aedc8788d9ccf3f9a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T04:03:24Z","email":"csafreen@gmail.com","name":"Afreen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T04:03:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Bug Fix: Concurrency limit deadlock in prefect jobs (#3370)\n\n* commit\n\n* commit\n\n* fix(cache): make concurrency slot reconciliation race-safe and long-run safe\n\nReconciling from a diff of two non-atomic reads (running task runs vs\nactive_slots) could release a slot a new task had just acquired. Now:\norphaned task runs are released through Prefect''s own state transition, and a\nslot is only decremented directly when no task run or lease claims it across\ntwo observations 5s apart. Reconcilers are serialized with a global lock.\n\nA task run is orphaned when its flow run has ended or has been idle (no new\ntask-run activity) past the threshold, instead of running longer than it, so\n13+ hour copies are no longer at risk of being force-crashed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ce25bbb70492a0a86afffc692a08a0518b1cd277","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/git/trees/ce25bbb70492a0a86afffc692a08a0518b1cd277"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OHDSI/Data2Evidence/git/commits/80bab912068b94abd4cc0c3aedc8788d9ccf3f9a","verification":{"payload":"tree ce25bbb70492a0a86afffc692a08a0518b1cd277\nparent 6d39291994346165b7c21cbca7c7e668525d780a\nauthor Afreen <csafreen@gmail.com> 1790049804 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790049804 +0000\n\nBug Fix: Concurrency limit deadlock in prefect jobs (#3370)\n\n* commit\n\n* commit\n\n* fix(cache): make concurrency slot reconciliation race-safe and long-run safe\n\nReconciling from a diff of two non-atomic reads (running task runs vs\nactive_slots) could release a slot a new task had just acquired. Now:\norphaned task runs are released through Prefect''s own state transition, and a\nslot is only decremented directly when no task run or lease claims it across\ntwo observations 5s apart. Reconcilers are serialized with a global lock.\n\nA task run is orphaned when its flow run has ended or has been idle (no new\ntask-run activity) past the threshold, instead of running longer than it, so\n13+ hour copies are no longer at risk of being force-crashed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqshVrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAN+cQABlkUrniq4jH2FEs5UgtiKZt\nVf27awb6Lia8Tid+4Vtd1g4nkd62YUqpujUc2lraT/CRitIQ8+aMGeU3LfP7Uwww\ndeFFeL5JKyazkF2jodM2F+DqXQyL6ykglBL9Vrb4hxzici+rQOWnxLK5rmlYMr8G\nWFePYpiF8XMxWn5sjAcBsL80W39+cWGx80dTTpjri9jIh6MAxEE9vO++xpWlRlpC\nq6TNOneL8ouObFglVl3HyjRGwDeXdqkvEU98Z/sWJSKBzE8qlPwBUoMfUPLp9i0a\nqeBJ2wXTYhXQ47Z6gPoZmmUfZWe9sOfTA48kwmFyE+Y66h9sM2ilWHQFKv/zeqWV\nO67M5lzdRGMClj4Vt4UtgRH9L8Zsfr+x5Axci3lFB5j4Ywc1AU1QDRJJnZ5kpss9\ngWczTT8SdR7LD2ue7Rd9BcSoBPea7GiHSFGkSxnwSkxFzV+XPPAWmvJD4/YcOUEF\nutmlBBi46lIWd5tUBrOXFR/V87EsBlnriLh5/hezf5kutGhziO5jvoNho