 fixer (based on pr-fix.md) — loop-guard cap (3),\n  minimal fix, push-to-pull-request-branch with allowed-files + [skip-ci], re-label\n  needs-qa; cap exhausted -> needs-human.\n- .github/workflows/qa-watchdog.md: hourly scheduled sweeper — resets PRs stuck in\n  qa-running (>90m, past QA''s 55m timeout) and enrolled PRs that lost their state label\n  (>120m) back to needs-qa; never touches terminal states; never merges.\n- Generated .lock.yml for each agentic workflow + an actions-lock.json pin.\n\nEvery cascading state write uses the agent PAT (GH_AW_AGENT_TOKEN, with GITHUB_TOKEN\nfallback) so the label actually triggers the next workflow — a label written with the\ndefault GITHUB_TOKEN is suppressed by GitHub''s recursion guard — and is attributed to a\nwrite+ member so gh-aw''s label_command activation membership gate passes. All PR content\nis treated as untrusted; existing security preambles are kept. Reuses the shared\njira-report.md and loop-guard.md imports. No existing workflows are modified.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add pinned-model Jira → draft-PR authoring workflow\n\nAdd jira-pr-author, a gh-aw workflow that authors the *initial* draft PR for a\nJira-originated task on a PINNED model (claude-opus-4.8) instead of the hosted\nCopilot agent''s \"Auto\" model, so first-cut authoring quality is deterministic.\nIt is the front door that feeds the existing state:* QA label state machine.\n\nTrigger: repository_dispatch (type: jira-task), fired by a Jira Automation rule,\nplus workflow_dispatch for manual testing. Because repository_dispatch only fires\non the default branch, this workflow becomes live only once merged to develop.\n\nFlow:\n- A pre-agent `ctx` step sanitizes the UNTRUSTED Jira payload — validates the\n  issue key against ^[A-Z][A-Z0-9]+-[0-9]+$, strips control chars, caps length —\n  and writes the validated task to /tmp/gh-aw/agent/jira-task.md. The agent reads\n  that file at runtime (the dir is exposed via --add-dir /tmp/gh-aw/, the same\n  convention pr-qa-playwright uses for auth.json). The prompt is rendered in the\n  activation job, which runs before the agent job, so step OUTPUTS can never reach\n  it — the file handoff is what makes the sanitized key/summary/description\n  actually available to the agent.\n- The agent implements a minimal first cut, SELF-REVIEWS it statically (imports\n  resolve, JSON well-formed, i18n via t()), then ALWAYS opens a DRAFT PR via the\n  create-pull-request safe output: labelled jira-agent (so qa-bootstrap-enroll.yml\n  stamps state:needs-qa and the QA machine takes over), branch jira/<KEY>\n  (preserve-branch-name), title [<KEY>] <summary> (so jira-report resolves the\n  ticket), base develop, using the GH_AW_AGENT_TOKEN PAT so the resulting\n  opened/labeled events cascade past GitHub''s recursion guard.\n\nReal lint, build, type-check and Playwright are delegated downstream to CI + the\nQA state machine — the gh-aw agent sandbox physically cannot execute\nnode/npm/python even when allowlisted (a missing_tool was observed in trial run 1),\nso the bash allowlist is inspection-only (git/ls/cat/grep/head/tail/wc) and the\nbody performs STATIC review and always opens the PR rather than gating on a build\nit cannot run.\n\nAll Jira content is treated as untrusted; the agent is instructed never to follow\ninstructions embedded in it and never to touch .github/ or CI config. The agent\njob is read-all; every GitHub write flows through the safe-output job.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQpm5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxJMQAGKk8yhwa1r/HNyEEuIy8dSQ\n1Eren5n1uk9JmUEZd2xhvOoUBBMUS/j6VK3AjeSJ73fXbTjlVx39q+jpZi4/N+2E\nN++5xQLV9GBnglm7GK9qgplfYg4/e6EdKkaI66kAH85CLfbIckTP5CV0D0c1vz/e\nkLOOh2/cT8BjdWuBVq8s0O8r+lm7iZpNQPuN/6tuBCi/xTdcYnG