/amjithtitus09/care_fe/commits/d619378ddfa282a73e5cc09007b40073f411adf0"}],"sha":"64e757af82bfd26557505b8359beaeebb727076a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amjithtitus09/care_fe/commits/64e757af82bfd26557505b8359beaeebb727076a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37619282?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/amjithtitus09","id":37619282,"login":"amjithtitus09","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NjE5Mjgy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amjithtitus09/care_fe/commits/d619378ddfa282a73e5cc09007b40073f411adf0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-28T09:52:00Z","email":"amjithtitus09@gmail.com","name":"Amjith Titus"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-28T09:52:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Harden autonomous loop: CI self-heal, event-driven merge, honest QA (#62)\n\n* fix(gh-aw): scope reviewer concurrency by event so PR comments don''t cancel reviews\n\nBot comments on a PR (Visual QA results, CI diagnosis, the rework hand-back)\narrive as issue_comment events and each spawns a reviewer run, because gh-aw\nonly matches the /review slash command after the run starts. Those skip-bound\nruns shared the per-PR concurrency group with the real pull_request review run,\nso under cancel-in-progress they cancelled it mid-flight (observed on #54: the\nCHANGES_REQUESTED review posted, then a rework-handoff comment''s run cancelled\nthe finishing run 1s later — a different timing would have lost the review).\n\nAdd github.event_name to the concurrency group key. cancel-in-progress still\napplies within an event type (a new commit supersedes an older review; a fresh\n/review supersedes a prior one), but comments can no longer cancel the\ncommit-triggered review.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(gh-aw): hand back rework via @copilot comment instead of assign-to-agent\n\nThe autonomous rework arm used gh-aw''s built-in `assign-to-agent` safe output,\nwhich assigns the Copilot coding agent over the REST `assignees` endpoint. That\nendpoint returns 404 for the Copilot agent (it is only assignable via the GraphQL\n`replaceActorsForAssignable` mutation), and assignment does not start a rework\nsession on an existing PR anyway. Per GitHub''s docs, the documented way to iterate\non a PR with the coding agent is to mention `@copilot` in a comment from a user\nwith write access.\n\nReplace `assign-to-agent` in the reviewer and QA workflows with a new shared\ncustom safe-job, `request_rework` (shared/request-rework.md), that posts an\n`@copilot` comment under the GH_AW_AGENT_TOKEN PAT. Posting from a dedicated job\n(a) uses the write-access identity the coding agent requires and (b) avoids\ngh-aw''s built-in @mention neutralization, so the mention survives verbatim. The\ncomment carries the durable \"handed back to the coding agent\" marker the shared\nrework cap counts, so the cap (3) still holds across reviewer + QA.\n\nVerified live on PR #54 (ENG-614): an equivalent @copilot hand-back comment made\nthe coding agent start a session and push the exact fix, turning the failing Lint\ncheck green with no manual approval.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(gh-aw): auto-complete approved+tested agent PRs (un-draft + squash-merge)\n\nThe Copilot coding agent opens DRAFT pull requests; the reviewer and QA\nworkflows drive them to the terminal `reviewed` (APPROVED) and `Tested`\nlabels, but nothing in GitHub then un-drafts or merges them — so a fully\nreconciled PR sits as a draft forever (the \"still draft PRs\" gap), requiring\na human to finish it.\n\nAdd a deterministic, non-agent workflow that closes the loop with zero human\nintervention. On a 5-minute schedule (and via workflow_dispatch) it scans open\nagent PRs and, for any that are fully reconciled — author is the Copilot agent\n(or `jira-agent` opt-in), labels include `reviewed`+`Tested` and exclude\n`needs-human`/`changes required`, reviewDecision is APPROVED with an APPROVE\nreview on the current head SHA, base is develop, no merge conflict, and the\nrepo''s lint check is green — it marks the PR ready for review and squash-merges\nit, comments, deletes the branch, and reports the merge to the linked JIRA\nissue (best effort).\n\nA plain workflow (not gh-aw) is used on purpose: the terminal merge must be\ndeterministic and is not subject to the Copilot \"Require approval for workflow\nruns\" gate or the gh-aw activation guard. schedule/workflow_dispatch are never\ngated, so it runs unimpeded.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Make ci-doctor self-heal CI failures via @copilot hand-back\n\nPreviously ci-doctor only diagnosed a failing check and told a human to\ncomment /fix, so a Copilot PR that failed CI (e.g. a Prettier formatting\nerror) hung indefinitely with no autonomous recovery.\n\nci-doctor now hands fixable Code/Test failures back to the Copilot coding\nagent via the proven request_rework arm (shared with reviewer/QA), bounded\nby the shared rework cap (3) with needs-human escalation. Flaky/Infra,\nDependencies and Config failures are still only diagnosed, not handed back.\n\nSince ci-doctor runs in workflow_run context (no pull_request payload),\nshared/request-rework.md gains an optional pr_number input that the agent\nsets to the PR it locates by head SHA; reviewer/QA keep falling back to the\nevent PR. Recompiled all three locks (request_rework embeds the change).\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Make pr-auto-complete event-driven, not cron-only\n\nGitHub heavily throttles high-frequency schedule crons on this repo, so the\n*/5 schedule actually ran ~75-90 min apart — a fully-reconciled PR could sit\nun-merged for over an hour. Add workflow_run triggers on the reviewer, QA,\nlint and Playwright workflows so the terminal merge scan fires within seconds\nof a PR gaining its last terminal signal (reviewed / Tested / lint-green after\na rework). The cron stays as a backstop.\n\nThe scan is unchanged and idempotent; the global serial concurrency group\n(cancel-in-progress: false) still guarantees no two scans merge at once.\nworkflow_run always runs this file from the default branch and is never\nsubject to the Copilot approval gate.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Make Visual QA honest about scope instead of hollow Tested\n\nThe QA built the PR, screenshotted whatever route it could reach, and stamped\na green Tested — but for an auth-gated feature (no backend in CI) it only ever\nsaw the login screen, so Tested implied a feature was verified when nothing was.\n\nReframe it as an explicit build + boot + public-surface visual smoke test:\n- Step 2 classifies each changed route as public (UI verifiable here) or\n  auth-gated (only boot smoke is observable) and records which the PR touches.\n- Step 3 captures browser console messages — a real runtime signal that can\n  catch a crash the PR introduced at boot even when the route falls back to login.\n- Step 4 makes a green Pass state plainly whether it is a build/boot smoke pass\n  (auth-gated) or real feature-UI verification (public); never dresses a login\n  fallback up as feature testing.\n- Step 6 comment leads with scope, shows a Reachable? column and an explicit\n  ''this PR''s changed area'' line, and separates what was verified from what was not.\n- Tested now explicitly means ''passed the build + boot + public smoke gate''.\n\nDeep auth-gated feature E2E stays delegated to the repo''s coded Playwright suite\n(playwright.yaml), the correct home for it; reproducing a backend in this agent\nworkflow would be slow, fragile and would undermine loop reliability.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: carefe-bot <bot@care.local>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"267e0aa856ea916c49f1c3085c7e4610083d3688","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amjithtitus09/care_fe/git/trees/267e0aa856ea916c49f1c3085c7e4610083d3688"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amjithtitus09/care_fe/git/commits/d619378ddfa282a73e5cc09007b40073f411adf0","verification":{"payload":"tree 267e0aa856ea916c49f1c3085c7e4610083d3688\nparent 84834dff0080519e117f875108f02902f786624e\nauthor Amjith Titus <amjithtitus09@gmail.com> 1782640320 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782640320 +0530\n\nHarden autonomous loop: CI self-heal, event-driven merge, honest QA (#62)\n\n* fix(gh-aw): scope reviewer concurrency by event so PR comments don''t cancel reviews\n\nBot comments on a PR (Visual QA results, CI diagnosis, the rework hand-back)\narrive as issue_comment events and each spawns a reviewer run, because gh-aw\nonly matches the /review slash command after the run starts. Those skip-bound\nruns shared the per-PR concurrency group with the real pull_request review run,\nso under cancel-in-progress they cancelled it mid-flight (observed on #54: the\nCHANGES_REQUESTED review posted, then a rework-handoff comment''s run cancelled\nthe finishing run 1s later — a different timing would have lost the review).\n\nAdd github.event_name to the concurrency group key. cancel-in-progress still\napplies within an event type (a new commit supersedes an older review; a fresh\n/review supersedes a prior one), but comments can no longer cancel the\ncommit-triggered review.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(gh-aw): hand back rework via @copilot comment instead of assign-to-agent\n\nThe autonomous rework arm used gh-aw''s built-in `assign-to-agent` safe output,\nwhich assigns the Copilot coding agent over the REST `assignees` endpoint. That\nendpoint returns 404 for the Copilot agent (it is only assignable via the GraphQL\n`replaceActorsForAssignable` mutation), and assignment does not start a rework\nsession on an existing PR anyway. Per GitHub''s docs, the documented way to iterate\non a PR with the coding agent is to mention `@copilot` in a comment from a user\nwith write access.\n\nReplace `assign-to-agent` in the reviewer and QA workflows with a new shared\ncustom safe-job, `request_rework` (shared/request-rework.md), that posts an\n`@copilot` comment under the GH_AW_AGENT_TOKEN PAT. Posting from a dedicated job\n(a) uses the write-access identity the coding agent requires and (b) avoids\ngh-aw''s built-in @mention neutralization, so the mention survives verbatim. The\ncomment carries the durable \"handed back to the coding agent\" marker the shared\nrework cap counts, so the cap (3) still holds across reviewer + QA.\n\nVerified live on PR #54 (ENG-614): an equivalent @copilot hand-back comment made\nthe coding agent start a session and push the exact fix, turning the failing Lint\ncheck green with no manual approval.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(gh-aw): auto-complete approved+tested agent PRs (un-draft + squash-merge)\n\nThe Copilot coding agent opens DRAFT pull requests; the reviewer and QA\nworkflows drive them to the terminal `reviewed` (APPROVED) and `Tested`\nlabels, but nothing in GitHub then un-drafts or merges them — so a fully\nreconciled PR sits as a draft forever (the \"still draft PRs\" gap), requiring\na human to finish it.\n\nAdd a deterministic, non-agent workflow that closes the loop with zero human\nintervention. On a 5-minute schedule (and via workflow_dispatch) it scans open\nagent PRs and, for any that are fully reconciled — author is the Copilot agent\n(or `jira-agent` opt-in), labels include `reviewed`+`Tested` and exclude\n`needs-human`/`changes required`, reviewDecision is APPROVED with an APPROVE\nreview on the current head SHA, base is develop, no merge conflict, and the\nrepo''s lint check is green — it marks the PR ready for review and squash-merges\nit, comments, deletes the branch, and reports the merge to the linked JIRA\nissue (best effort).\n\nA plain workflow (not gh-aw) is used on purpose: the terminal merge must be\ndeterministic and is not subject to the Copilot \"Require approval for workflow\nruns\" gate or the gh-aw activation guard. schedule/workflow_dispatch are never\ngated, so it runs unimpeded.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Make ci-doctor self-heal CI failures via @copilot hand-back\n\nPreviously ci-doctor only diagnosed a failing check and told a human to\ncomment /fix, so a Copilot PR that failed CI (e.g. a Prettier formatting\nerror) hung indefinitely with no autonomous recovery.\n\nci-doctor now hands fixable Code/Test failures back to the Copilot coding\nagent via the proven request_rework arm (shared with reviewer/QA), bounded\nby the shared rework cap (3) with needs-human escalation. Flaky/Infra,\nDependencies and Config failures are still only diagnosed, not handed back.\n\nSince ci-doctor runs in workflow_run context (no pull_request payload),\nshared/request-rework.md gains an optional pr_number input that the agent\nsets to the PR it locates by head SHA; reviewer/QA keep falling back to the\nevent PR. Recompiled all three locks (request_rework embeds the change).\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Make pr-auto-complete event-driven, not cron-only\n\nGitHub heavily throttles high-frequency schedule crons on this repo, so the\n*/5 schedule actually ran ~75-90 min apart — a fully-reconciled PR could sit\nun-merged for over an hour. Add workflow_run triggers on the reviewer, QA,\nlint and Playwright workflows so the terminal merge scan fires within seconds\nof a PR gaining its last terminal signal (reviewed / Tested / lint-green after\na rework). The cron stays as a backstop.\n\nThe scan is unchanged and idempotent; the global serial concurrency group\n(cancel-in-progress: false) still guarantees no two scans merge at once.\nworkflow_run always runs this file from the default branch and is never\nsubject to the Copilot approval gate.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Make Visual QA honest about scope instead of hollow Tested\n\nThe QA built the PR, screenshotted whatever route it could reach, and stamped\na green Tested — but for an auth-gated feature (no backend in CI) it only ever\nsaw the login screen, so Tested implied a feature was verified when nothing was.\n\nReframe it as an explicit build + boot + public-surface visual smoke test:\n- Step 2 classifies each changed route as public (UI verifiable here) or\n  auth-gated (only boot smoke is observable) and records which the PR touches.\n- Step 3 captures browser console messages — a real runtime signal that can\n  catch a crash the PR introduced at boot even when the route falls back to login.\n- Step 4 makes a green Pass state plainly whether it is a build/boot smoke pass\n  (auth-gated) or real feature-UI verification (public); never dresses a login\n  fallback up as feature testing.\n- Step 6 comment leads with scope, shows a Reachable? column and an explicit\n  ''this PR''s changed area'' line, and separates what was verified from what was not.\n- Tested now explicitly means ''passed the build + boot + public smoke gate''.\n\nDeep auth-gated feature E2E stays delegated to the repo''s coded Playwright suite\n(playwright.yaml), the correct home for it; reproducing a backend in this agent\nworkflow would be slow, fragile and would undermine loop reliability.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: carefe-bot <bot@care.local>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQO7ACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuGoQADYYgQSW9yho/G8fN8AJApgk\nK0pCC59lAjFa1w9wA1+0vkS43JyF+lys8ZAMnNDBeWlc3hYL5zjfow9caUTM3dLD\nd4RKMbH6xlK5nGpyH565dhwSEie4O5EMq54Pp6LocpHuAjT+NtkW9SytQ+cFMdNl\nFyOvjNvpKmBauOeNhlELjYTb3inMM3OqbhHpCCa0IHBUchti2xREYbto7lrX4tCa\niH7BPdlIHDzDpbQBZnZTafnMflmZz7gbhmXCLwQ+dvjMUdjJ1LHzBkPfr5sCPi62\naK4ZPKo4VIt4fTx9y6y8dgUTb7k5cW6mO+7nTKmDPDpqj6dTZrMivkE4d2mAPnmA\n/uRtofzXeD077j1PkNZVS3EaX542A8lK+h7nFhQSOOLzxVzJXPKmRXGlqpEHg2NU\nPcB+mNYKrfHmdcjvmfEEvi0nxxNv2Hx0kC3P/4/0tuyK/SCG0YQcFwX5Yp0XX7Va\nhf/OA8lCLZZcotpivOS1bHaq/AiRmYa6Sz1ATlM8ubQe7MT+xB0JNwNFJRRrb1K1\n1BzdlBJq1JTWKc+OLxXybpI1cbXeXLuyHwyI8WxT8bye2KYe0TbA2/dMhuvMcWJi\nnXvtZBGqWC/VlrPqy/MrW6STWRZFJcy+JZD4xzCK8azVPyBuq1qIsv0Kb/wGYzIy\nrMAGChLhESVX3FQ+Zo6b\n=Qhys\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-28T09:52:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/use