","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/amjithtitus09/care_fe/commit/67e3b0a7a3a2cbdb9319cc5ed9f614842260436d","node_id":"C_kwDONbM8otoAKDY3ZTNiMGE3YTNhMmNiZGI5MzE5Y2M1ZWQ5ZjYxNDg0MjI2MDQzNmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/amjithtitus09/care_fe/commit/b62c4b4d6a302b5218e7d777f0a25e36e0b85fc9","sha":"b62c4b4d6a302b5218e7d777f0a25e36e0b85fc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amjithtitus09/care_fe/commits/b62c4b4d6a302b5218e7d777f0a25e36e0b85fc9"}],"sha":"67e3b0a7a3a2cbdb9319cc5ed9f614842260436d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amjithtitus09/care_fe/commits/67e3b0a7a3a2cbdb9319cc5ed9f614842260436d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37619282?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/amjithtitus09","id":37619282,"login":"amjithtitus09","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NjE5Mjgy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amjithtitus09/care_fe/commits/b62c4b4d6a302b5218e7d777f0a25e36e0b85fc9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T22:08:58Z","email":"amjithtitus09@gmail.com","name":"Amjith Titus"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-27T22:08:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Bulletproof the autonomous PR loop: terminal auto-merge + rework arm + reviewer race fix (#57)\n\n* fix(gh-aw): scope reviewer concurrency by event so PR comments don''t cancel reviews\n\nBot comments on a PR (Visual QA results, CI diagnosis, the rework hand-back)\narrive as issue_comment events and each spawns a reviewer run, because gh-aw\nonly matches the /review slash command after the run starts. Those skip-bound\nruns shared the per-PR concurrency group with the real pull_request review run,\nso under cancel-in-progress they cancelled it mid-flight (observed on #54: the\nCHANGES_REQUESTED review posted, then a rework-handoff comment''s run cancelled\nthe finishing run 1s later — a different timing would have lost the review).\n\nAdd github.event_name to the concurrency group key. cancel-in-progress still\napplies within an event type (a new commit supersedes an older review; a fresh\n/review supersedes a prior one), but comments can no longer cancel the\ncommit-triggered review.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(gh-aw): hand back rework via @copilot comment instead of assign-to-agent\n\nThe autonomous rework arm used gh-aw''s built-in `assign-to-agent` safe output,\nwhich assigns the Copilot coding agent over the REST `assignees` endpoint. That\nendpoint returns 404 for the Copilot agent (it is only assignable via the GraphQL\n`replaceActorsForAssignable` mutation), and assignment does not start a rework\nsession on an existing PR anyway. Per GitHub''s docs, the documented way to iterate\non a PR with the coding agent is to mention `@copilot` in a comment from a user\nwith write access.\n\nReplace `assign-to-agent` in the reviewer and QA workflows with a new shared\ncustom safe-job, `request_rework` (shared/request-rework.md), that posts an\n`@copilot` comment under the GH_AW_AGENT_TOKEN PAT. Posting from a dedicated job\n(a) uses the write-access identity the coding agent requires and (b) avoids\ngh-aw''s built-in @mention neutralization, so the mention survives verbatim. The\ncomment carries the durable \"handed back to the coding agent\" marker the shared\nrework cap counts, so the cap (3) still holds across reviewer + QA.\n\nVerified live on PR #54 (ENG-614): an equivalent @copilot hand-back comment made\nthe coding agent start a session and push the exact fix, turning the failing Lint\ncheck green with no manual approval.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(gh-aw): auto-complete approved+tested agent PRs (un-draft + squash-merge)\n\nThe Copilot coding agent opens DRAFT pull requests; the reviewer and QA\nworkflows drive them to the terminal `reviewed` (APPROVED) and `Tested`\nlabels, but nothing in GitHub then un-drafts or merges them — so a fully\nreconciled PR sits as a draft forever (the \"still draft PRs\" gap), requiring\na human to finish it.\n\nAdd a deterministic, non-agent workflow that closes the loop with zero human\nintervention. On a 5-minute schedule (and via workflow_dispatch) it scans open\nagent PRs and, for any that are fully reconciled — author is the Copilot agent\n(or `jira-agent` opt-in), labels include `reviewed`+`Tested` and exclude\n`needs-human`/`changes required`, reviewDecision is APPROVED with an APPROVE\nreview on the current head SHA, base is develop, no merge conflict, and the\nrepo''s lint check is green — it marks the PR ready for review and squash-merges\nit, comments, deletes the branch, and reports the merge to the linked JIRA\nissue (best effort).\n\nA plain workflow (not gh-aw) is used on purpose: the terminal merge must be\ndeterministic and is not subject to the Copilot \"Require approval for workflow\nruns\" gate or the gh-aw activation guard. schedule/workflow_dispatch are never\ngated, so it runs unimpeded.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: carefe-bot <bot@care.local>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ab3eadca417664324bb3fa2f5d8a3eb740578f0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amjithtitus09/care_fe/git/trees/ab3eadca417664324bb3fa2f5d8a3eb740578f0c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amjithtitus09/care_fe/git/commits/b62c4b4d6a302b5218e7d777f0a25e36e0b85fc9","verification":{"payload":"tree ab3eadca417664324bb3fa2f5d8a3eb740578f0c\nparent 7397f0c9ccfdf9e8d0220d882417df12a7b13363\nauthor Amjith Titus <amjithtitus09@gmail.com> 1782598138 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782598138 +0530\n\nBulletproof the autonomous PR loop: terminal auto-merge + rework arm + reviewer race fix (#57)\n\n* fix(gh-aw): scope reviewer concurrency by event so PR comments don''t cancel reviews\n\nBot comments on a PR (Visual QA results, CI diagnosis, the rework hand-back)\narrive as issue_comment events and each spawns a reviewer run, because gh-aw\nonly matches the /review slash command after the run starts. Those skip-bound\nruns shared the per-PR concurrency group with the real pull_request review run,\nso under cancel-in-progress they cancelled it mid-flight (observed on #54: the\nCHANGES_REQUESTED review posted, then a rework-handoff comment''s run cancelled\nthe finishing run 1s later — a different timing would have lost the review).\n\nAdd github.event_name to the concurrency group key. cancel-in-progress still\napplies within an event type (a new commit supersedes an older review; a fresh\n/review supersedes a prior one), but comments can no longer cancel the\ncommit-triggered review.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(gh-aw): hand back rework via @copilot comment instead of assign-to-agent\n\nThe autonomous rework arm used gh-aw''s built-in `assign-to-agent` safe output,\nwhich assigns the Copilot coding agent over the REST `assignees` endpoint. That\nendpoint returns 404 for the Copilot agent (it is only assignable via the GraphQL\n`replaceActorsForAssignable` mutation), and assignment does not start a rework\nsession on an existing PR anyway. Per GitHub''s docs, the documented way to iterate\non a PR with the coding agent is to mention `@copilot` in a comment from a user\nwith write access.\n\nReplace `assign-to-agent` in the reviewer and QA workflows with a new shared\ncustom safe-job, `request_rework` (shared/request-rework.md), that posts an\n`@copilot` comment under the GH_AW_AGENT_TOKEN PAT. Posting from a dedicated job\n(a) uses the write-access identity the coding agent requires and (b) avoids\ngh-aw''s built-in @mention neutralization, so the mention survives verbatim. The\ncomment carries the durable \"handed back to the coding agent\" marker the shared\nrework cap counts, so the cap (3) still holds across reviewer + QA.\n\nVerified live on PR #54 (ENG-614): an equivalent @copilot hand-back comment made\nthe coding agent start a session and push the exact fix, turning the failing Lint\ncheck green with no manual approval.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* feat(gh-aw): auto-complete approved+tested agent PRs (un-draft + squash-merge)\n\nThe Copilot coding agent opens DRAFT pull requests; the reviewer and QA\nworkflows drive them to the terminal `reviewed` (APPROVED) and `Tested`\nlabels, but nothing in GitHub then un-drafts or merges them — so a fully\nreconciled PR sits as a draft forever (the \"still draft PRs\" gap), requiring\na human to finish it.\n\nAdd a deterministic, non-agent workflow that closes the loop with zero human\nintervention. On a 5-minute schedule (and via workflow_dispatch) it scans open\nagent PRs and, for any that are fully reconciled — author is the Copilot agent\n(or `jira-agent` opt-in), labels include `reviewed`+`Tested` and exclude\n`needs-human`/`changes required`, reviewDecision is APPROVED with an APPROVE\nreview on the current head SHA, base is develop, no merge conflict, and the\nrepo''s lint check is green — it marks the PR ready for review and squash-merges\nit, comments, deletes the branch, and reports the merge to the linked JIRA\nissue (best effort).\n\nA plain workflow (not gh-aw) is used on purpose: the terminal merge must be\ndeterministic and is not subject to the Copilot \"Require approval for workflow\nruns\" gate or the gh-aw activation guard. schedule/workflow_dispatch are never\ngated, so it runs unimpeded.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: carefe-bot <bot@care.local>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQEn6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9xoQAAnvL88BWA8bxrkwi7e4+dMC\np6JJP/yIVorG/qBYyWwh4UZFmLCcguEogRnkv8An9a5Rmtb18pegIAXLQJKC9l9y\nRLZaXzv+hWu/ah7YngzjU9JW+nuLDe34mQb+DNKO2rhb51DI6tOZ0YiyeZbOh4Py\nZLYTTi1Bcg/LQ9nFwFe2U5hEKBeT80GiEw40MTUVfDqRknkfBBhlVD9v8LtXuXyG\nUPGIwhqYsqKtsfnsNj1npgqveU2wFOK5WnNcJBZlUfQJYnc57eaVWeLi6OKCkH19\ng+E4Rkf02PaRMTHGIULJJzzOeBy1ecd93PkE0kHOzHvMgG7ORpWmoRzVhits793X\nrFrUgB9OOx8u+Egnj+PuWy9j6srv4BFOGrcOM765HDgq3uUheEYJY6hGf4qPKvD2\ncekBPKxOLWIugcxStwTAK8TT2eEEEp/smuX92J8mUd2afLgn87dFVWUgIKK6TorQ\nZENGFuvAbPQwuRjvja3yVgmywxqJVkh/fmciHKdjloHZ/R4WEt2f8AIMzvsQc+un\nbtXw7k/lqEJFC8XGh51r2IMmyPR6kw05h76IKM6xsLRNW5QUrh4lVVEK5miJEzfw\