hub.com/users/amjithtitus09/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/amjithtitus09","id":37619282,"login":"amjithtitus09","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NjE5Mjgy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amjithtitus09/care_fe/commits/7397f0c9ccfdf9e8d0220d882417df12a7b13363/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T17:43:58Z","email":"amjithtitus09@gmail.com","name":"Amjith Titus"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-27T17:43:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gh-aw): drop ''labeled'' trigger so bot label events don''t cancel reviews (#52)\n\nOn the Copilot agent''s PRs, the repo''s label-automation bot adds labels moments\nafter the PR opens. Each ''labeled'' event spawned an extra reviewer/QA run whose\nactor is the automation bot, not the PR author; the activation guard correctly\nrefuses those, but with concurrency.cancel-in-progress they first CANCEL the\nvalid author-triggered (opened/synchronize) run — so the PR ends up un-reviewed\nand un-tested (observed on PR #51: 0 reviews despite a successful-looking run).\n\nRemove ''labeled'' from the pull_request trigger types for both the reviewer and\nQA workflows. The Copilot open/rework pushes still activate via the\nauthor==Copilot branch, and the needs review / needs testing labels are still\nhonored in ''if:'' on those runs. cancel-in-progress stays true (preserves cost\ncontrol on the expensive QA builds). Recompiled both lock files (no other churn).\n\nCo-authored-by: carefe-bot <bot@care.local>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"cd04f7e8cdac94bef7fde8d6dc482a3cc23d8c96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amjithtitus09/care_fe/git/trees/cd04f7e8cdac94bef7fde8d6dc482a3cc23d8c96"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amjithtitus09/care_fe/git/commits/7397f0c9ccfdf9e8d0220d882417df12a7b13363","verification":{"payload":"tree cd04f7e8cdac94bef7fde8d6dc482a3cc23d8c96\nparent cb6227402b4e7677dc7443e70cc13a50f0ebc383\nauthor Amjith Titus <amjithtitus09@gmail.com> 1782582238 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782582238 +0530\n\nfix(gh-aw): drop ''labeled'' trigger so bot label events don''t cancel reviews (#52)\n\nOn the Copilot agent''s PRs, the repo''s label-automation bot adds labels moments\nafter the PR opens. Each ''labeled'' event spawned an extra reviewer/QA run whose\nactor is the automation bot, not the PR author; the activation guard correctly\nrefuses those, but with concurrency.cancel-in-progress they first CANCEL the\nvalid author-triggered (opened/synchronize) run — so the PR ends up un-reviewed\nand un-tested (observed on PR #51: 0 reviews despite a successful-looking run).\n\nRemove ''labeled'' from the pull_request trigger types for both the reviewer and\nQA workflows. The Copilot open/rework pushes still activate via the\nauthor==Copilot branch, and the needs review / needs testing labels are still\nhonored in ''if:'' on those runs. cancel-in-progress stays true (preserves cost\ncontrol on the expensive QA builds). Recompiled both lock files (no other churn).\n\nCo-authored-by: carefe-bot <bot@care.local>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqQAveCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADjkQAJR1hFNRJgGguOWcsOnp29px\nqAOStMhtWuCEqg1M++2anuAfaKalxul7nUeIoq+3IOp3L1ue30p+LWU6rwTaWgD5\n40r3rxwh