ttps://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/amjithtitus09","id":37619282,"login":"amjithtitus09","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NjE5Mjgy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/amjithtitus09","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amjithtitus09/care_fe/commits/e40153cd9cc1ab07c7b7996791d43f6c8f7e7988/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-24T19:08:26Z","email":"amjithtitus09@gmail.com","name":"Amjith Titus"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-24T19:08:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: scaffold gh-aw PR review/QA/rework loop (pilot) (#31)\n\n* ci: scaffold gh-aw PR review/QA/rework loop (pilot)\n\nAdd a set of GitHub Agentic Workflows (gh-aw) that implement a PR\nreview -> Playwright QA -> CI diagnosis -> rework -> JIRA report loop:\n\n- pr-reviewer.md      professional code review + verdict (pull_request + /review)\n- pr-qa-playwright.md before/after Playwright screenshots, gated on src/**\n- ci-doctor.md        diagnose failed CI runs and comment on the PR\n- pr-fix.md           /fix command with a hard rework cap + human escalation\n- shared/jira-report.md  non-agent JIRA REST reporting (token never seen by agent)\n- shared/loop-guard.md   reusable rework-cap + escalation fragment\n\nHardening: per-PR concurrency with cancel-in-progress, max-turns and\ntimeout-minutes, github lockdown, minimal network allowlists, label/path\ntrigger scoping, and untrusted-input handling. Generated .lock.yml files\nvia `gh aw compile` and added the v0.80.9 setup action to actions-lock.json.\n\nCODEOWNERS: add fork-valid /.github/ owner so the human merge gate resolves\non the personal fork.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* ci: switch gh-aw workflows from claude to copilot engine\n\nUse the GitHub Copilot engine (COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN) instead of the\nAnthropic Claude Code engine, matching the existing daily-playwright-improver\nworkflow and avoiding a separate ANTHROPIC_API_KEY secret. The Copilot engine\ndefaults to the claude-sonnet-4.6 model and can be overridden per-repo via the\nGH_AW_MODEL_AGENT_COPILOT variable. max-turns budgets are preserved.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* ci: pin gh-aw workflows to claude-opus-4.8 with higher budgets\n\nMove max-turns to top-level (non-deprecated) and raise turn/timeout\nbudgets now that the agents run on Opus 4.8:\n- pr-reviewer:   40 turns / 20 min\n- pr-qa-playwright: 60 turns / 45 min\n- ci-doctor:     40 turns / 25 min\n- pr-fix:        80 turns / 45 min\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* ci: harden gh-aw jira reporting and rework cap after review\n\n- jira-report: match JIRA keys case-insensitively and normalize to\n  uppercase, so reporting works off lowercase branch names (the only\n  key source for ci-doctor''s workflow_run trigger).\n- jira-report: fall back to github.event.issue.title for PR_TITLE so the\n  key is derivable on the /review issue_comment path.\n- loop-guard: cross-check the cache-memory attempt counter against prior\n  ''automated fix attempt'' PR comments so the rework cap survives cache loss.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: carefe-bot <bot@care.local>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ec2cc934d1905eaa519b470d17f57cb88d3b15fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amjithtitus09/care_fe/git/trees/ec2cc934d1905eaa519b470d17f57cb88d3b15fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/amjithtitus09/care_fe/git/commits/e40153cd9cc1ab07c7b7996791d43f6c8f7e7988","verification":{"payload":"tree ec2cc934d1905eaa519b470d17f57cb88d3b15fa\nparent f8a2f09de14aeccd2839b475a77b184be2a9988c\nauthor Amjith Titus <amjithtitus09@gmail.com> 1782328106 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782328106 +0530\n\nci: scaffold gh-aw PR review/QA/rework loop (pilot) (#31)\n\n* ci: scaffold gh-aw PR review/QA/rework loop (pilot)\n\nAdd a set of GitHub Agentic Workflows (gh-aw) that implement a PR\nreview -> Playwright QA -> CI diagnosis -> rework -> JIRA report loop:\n\n- pr-reviewer.md      professional code review + verdict (pull_request + /review)\n- pr-qa-playwright.md before/after Playwright screenshots, gated on src/**\n- ci-doctor.md        diagnose failed CI runs and comment on the PR\n- pr-fix.md           /fix command with a hard rework cap + human escalation\n- shared/jira-report.md  non-agent JIRA REST reporting (token never seen by agent)\n- shared/loop-guard.md   reusable rework-cap + escalation fragment\n\nHardening: per-PR concurrency with cancel-in-progress, max-turns and\ntimeout-minutes, github lockdown, minimal network allowlists, label/path\ntrigger scoping, and untrusted-input handling. Generated .lock.yml files\nvia `gh aw compile` and added the v0.80.9 setup action to actions-lock.json.\n\nCODEOWNERS: add fork-valid /.github/ owner so the human merge gate resolves\non the personal fork.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* ci: switch gh-aw workflows from claude to copilot engine\n\nUse the GitHub Copilot engine (COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN) instead of the\nAnthropic Claude Code engine, matching the existing daily-playwright-improver\nworkflow and avoiding a separate ANTHROPIC_API_KEY secret. The Copilot engine\ndefaults to the claude-sonnet-4.6 model and can be overridden per-repo via the\nGH_AW_MODEL_AGENT_COPILOT variable. max-turns budgets are preserved.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* ci: pin gh-aw workflows to claude-opus-4.8 with higher budgets\n\nMove max-turns to top-level (non-deprecated) and raise turn/timeout\nbudgets now that the agents run on Opus 4.8:\n- pr-reviewer:   40 turns / 20 min\n- pr-qa-playwright: 60 turns / 45 min\n- ci-doctor:     40 turns / 25 min\n- pr-fix:        80 turns / 45 min\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* ci: harden gh-aw jira reporting and rework cap after review\n\n- jira-report: match JIRA keys case-insensitively and normalize to\n  uppercase, so reporting works off lowercase branch names (the only\n  key source for ci-doctor''s workflow_run trigger).\n- jira-report: fall back to github.event.issue.title for PR_TITLE so the\n  key is derivable on the /review issue_comment path.\n- loop-guard: cross-check the cache-memory attempt counter against prior\n  ''automated fix attempt'' PR comments so the rework cap survives cache loss.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: carefe-bot <bot@care.local>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPCsqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAw+kQAK8Dvd73d4mxXCMG5iV1woIT\nxHkIsmD1vRz2K84DdGnC+FmWPvK251+dYibZGUomi8r424pdKvouKkOmoMl75nN+\nRarw0Z7tnaxSVvwcBxz2RjPqkw6Rj1B2ECDtGymkEjOqrpzodrRxCVJFcrL4pHm9\neAbd/75+Pola7q+/R/DRDpo3Rz88AnUiOKRVlO1wY7o4zX+np7r668IjJwklH+FE\nAzGLJuyeFuKvfR/7j7ZbSg3/NwvghyhZ0GieXh8bYnBplluljXOsmJn5/DYn3vya\narHYKEGtsRNJbb4cepnEZxLQU1rEeXbJEiZTyu+arJgsgr2WjhZxqCbai2UnVfvw\nYQFQW7HABo+pOQOfh9QrIvJAeNJKd4krLHhRotZfGODplzjyVYfPLNX